"6d6214cd-ebee-4b8a-a6c1-a017e2295d43","f8b2f00d-5f02-42f4-a7c6-6caaa31c6e0c","ai_stage:assistant","GENERATION","lV.chat","2026-09-29 16:35:30.810000","2026-09-29 16:36:54.759000","","default","","candidate-1","usku64aixf1e766qzwy4gx9r","DEFAULT","","","","","0a8ec527-44e0-4ee3-8005-a1865d712ec6","gpt-5.5-2026-04-23","{""response_format"":null}","{""input"":""2132"",""output"":""10841"",""total"":""12973"",""input_cached_tokens"":""0"",""input_audio_tokens"":""0"",""output_reasoning_tokens"":""2181"",""output_audio_tokens"":""0"",""output_accepted_prediction_tokens"":""0"",""output_rejected_prediction_tokens"":""0""}","{""input"":0.01066,""output"":0.32523,""input_cached_tokens"":0,""output_reasoning_tokens"":0.06543,""total"":0.40132}","0.40132","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for Macquarie.\n\n# Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent & Scoping Gateway\n\n## The Problem\nUnder Australian Consumer Data Right (CDR) legislation, Accredited Data Recipients (ADRs) and Data Holders must manage fine-grained, time-bound customer consent for financial accounts. You will build a CDR Consent Gateway that validates incoming consent authorizations, scopes account data access, and automatically revokes access when consent expires or is withdrawn.\n\n## Australian Statutory Constraints\n1. **CDR Arrangement Rules**: Consents must expire after a maximum duration of 12 months, with automated hourly reconciliation against revocation registries.\n2. **PII Masking (Privacy Act 1988)**: Australian BSB and Account numbers must be masked (e.g., '083-*** ... 1234') in telemetry and standard error traces.\n3. **AEST Timezone Invariant**: Consent expiry calculations must be anchored to Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST/AEDT) rather than browser-local timezones.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- Gateway grants access only to actively consented scopes (e.g. 'bank:accounts.basic:read').\n- Withdrawn consents instantly reject subsequent data requests.\n- Privacy-compliant error sanitization middleware strips sensitive identifiers.\n</challenge>""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway\n\n# Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent & Scoping Gateway\n\n## The Problem\nUnder Australian Consumer Data Right (CDR) legislation, Accredited Data Recipients (ADRs) and Data Holders must manage fine-grained, time-bound customer consent for financial accounts. You will build a CDR Consent Gateway that validates incoming consent authorizations, scopes account data access, and automatically revokes access when consent expires or is withdrawn.\n\n## Australian Statutory Constraints\n1. **CDR Arrangement Rules**: Consents must expire after a maximum duration of 12 months, with automated hourly reconciliation against revocation registries.\n2. **PII Masking (Privacy Act 1988)**: Australian BSB and Account numbers must be masked (e.g., '083-*** ... 1234') in telemetry and standard error traces.\n3. **AEST Timezone Invariant**: Consent expiry calculations must be anchored to Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST/AEDT) rather than browser-local timezones.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- Gateway grants access only to actively consented scopes (e.g. 'bank:accounts.basic:read').\n- Withdrawn consents instantly reject subsequent data requests.\n- Privacy-compliant error sanitization middleware strips sensitive identifiers.\n\n## Technical Invariants & Constraints\n- Consent duration must not exceed 365 days from creation.\n- Account numbers and BSBs must be masked in log events.\n- Revocation endpoints must be idempotent.\n- All expiry dates must use ISO 8601 with explicit Australian timezone offsets (+10:00 / +11:00).\n\n## Candidate Workspace Instructions\n1. Review the brief and technical constraints above.\n2. Write your implementation files in `src/`.\n3. Validate boundary conditions and domain rules.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway</h1>\n      <p>\n        Review the brief in <code>README.md</code>, or message the AI assistant to start implementing your solution.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/cdr-types.ts ===\nexport type CdrScope = 'bank:accounts.basic:read' | 'bank:accounts.detail:read' | 'bank:transactions:read';\n\nexport interface ConsentRecord {\n  consentId: string;\n  customerId: string;\n  scopes: CdrScope[];\n  status: 'AUTHORISED' | 'REVOKED' | 'EXPIRED';\n  authorisedAtIso: string;\n  expiresAtIso: string;\n}\n\nexport interface CdrAccessRequest {\n  consentId: string;\n  requestedScope: CdrScope;\n  timestampIso: string;\n}\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\nmake no mistake, finish everything""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\""message\"":\""Implemented the in-memory CDR Consent Gateway demo in React. Assumed this should run entirely in the browser with local data/no backend, while exposing the gateway rules as reusable functions under `src/`. It now demonstrates active scope validation, instant idempotent withdrawal, expiry handling, simulated hourly revocation reconciliation, Australian timezone ISO formatting, and sanitized telemetry/error logs. Check the preview by running allowed/denied requests, withdrawing a consent, adding one to the revocation registry, and confirming logs mask BSB/account data.\"",\""files\"":[{\""path\"":\""src/cdrGateway.js\"",\""contents\"":\""export const CDR_SCOPES = [\\n  \\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"",\\n  \\\""bank:accounts.detail:read\\\"",\\n  \\\""bank:transactions:read\\\"",\\n];\\n\\nconst MAX_CONSENT_DAYS = 365;\\nconst DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\\nconst AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN = /T\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}(?:\\\\+10:00|\\\\+11:00)$/;\\n\\nfunction pad(value) {\\n  return String(value).padStart(2, \\\""0\\\"");\\n}\\n\\nfunction firstSundayOfMonth(year, monthIndex) {\\n  const firstDay = new Date(Date.UTC(year, monthIndex, 1)).getUTCDay();\\n  return 1 + ((7 - firstDay) % 7);\\n}\\n\\nexport function getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant = new Date()) {\\n  const utcMs = instant.getTime();\\n  const year = instant.getUTCFullYear();\\n\\n  const dstStartThisYear = Date.UTC(\\n    year,\\n    9,\\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 9),\\n    16,\\n    0,\\n    0,\\n  );\\n  const dstEndThisYear = Date.UTC(\\n    year,\\n    3,\\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 3),\\n    16,\\n    0,\\n    0,\\n  );\\n\\n  const isDaylightSaving = utcMs >= dstStartThisYear || utcMs < dstEndThisYear;\\n  return isDaylightSaving ? 11 * 60 : 10 * 60;\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatAustralianIso(instant = new Date()) {\\n  const offsetMinutes = getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant);\\n  const localTime = new Date(instant.getTime() + offsetMinutes * 60 * 1000);\\n  const offset = offsetMinutes === 660 ? \\\""+11:00\\\"" : \\\""+10:00\\\"";\\n\\n  return `${localTime.getUTCFullYear()}-${pad(localTime.getUTCMonth() + 1)}-${pad(\\n    localTime.getUTCDate(),\\n  )}T${pad(localTime.getUTCHours())}:${pad(localTime.getUTCMinutes())}:${pad(\\n    localTime.getUTCSeconds(),\\n  )}${offset}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function parseAustralianIso(isoValue) {\\n  if (!AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN.test(isoValue)) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      \\\""Timestamp must be ISO 8601 with an explicit Australian offset (+10:00 or +11:00).\\\"",\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  const parsed = new Date(isoValue);\\n  if (Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime())) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\""Timestamp is not a valid ISO 8601 value.\\\"");\\n  }\\n  return parsed;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskBsb(value) {\\n  const digits = String(value ?? \\\""\\\"").replace(/\\\\D/g, \\\""\\\"");\\n  if (digits.length !== 6) return \\\""***-***\\\"";\\n  return `${digits.slice(0, 3)}-***`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskAccountNumber(value) {\\n  const digits = String(value ?? \\\""\\\"").replace(/\\\\D/g, \\\""\\\"");\\n  if (digits.length < 4) return \\\""... ****\\\"";\\n  return `... ${digits.slice(-4)}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskSensitiveIdentifiers(value) {\\n  if (typeof value !== \\\""string\\\"") return value;\\n\\n  return value\\n    .replace(/\\\\b(\\\\d{3})[-\\\\s]?(\\\\d{3})\\\\b/g, \\\""$1-***\\\"")\\n    .replace(\\n      /\\\\b(account(?:\\\\s+number)?|acct)\\\\s*[:#-]?\\\\s*(\\\\d{4,12})\\\\b/gi,\\n      (_match, label, accountNumber) => `${label}: ${maskAccountNumber(accountNumber)}`,\\n    );\\n}\\n\\nexport function sanitizeTelemetry(input) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(input)) {\\n    return input.map((entry) => sanitizeTelemetry(entry));\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input && typeof input === \\\""object\\\"") {\\n    return Object.fromEntries(\\n      Object.entries(input).map(([key, value]) => {\\n        const lowerKey = key.toLowerCase();\\n        if (lowerKey === \\\""bsb\\\"") return [key, maskBsb(value)];\\n        if (lowerKey === \\\""accountnumber\\\"" || lowerKey === \\\""account\\\"") {\\n          return [key, maskAccountNumber(value)];\\n        }\\n        return [key, sanitizeTelemetry(value)];\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return maskSensitiveIdentifiers(input);\\n}\\n\\nfunction createTelemetryEvent(level, code, message, details = {}) {\\n  return sanitizeTelemetry({\\n    level,\\n    code,\\n    message,\\n    details,\\n    observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction assertScope(scope) {\\n  if (!CDR_SCOPES.includes(scope)) {\\n    throw new Error(`Unsupported CDR scope: ${scope}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction normaliseScopes(scopes) {\\n  const unique = [...new Set(scopes)];\\n  unique.forEach(assertScope);\\n  return unique;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createConsent({\\n  consentId,\\n  customerId,\\n  scopes,\\n  durationDays,\\n  accounts = [],\\n  now = new Date(),\\n}) {\\n  if (!customerId) throw new Error(\\\""customerId is required.\\\"");\\n  if (!Number.isInteger(durationDays) || durationDays < 1) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\""Consent duration must be a positive whole number of days.\\\"");\\n  }\\n  if (durationDays > MAX_CONSENT_DAYS) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\""Consent duration must not exceed 365 days from creation.\\\"");\\n  }\\n\\n  const authorisedAt = new Date(now);\\n  const expiresAt = new Date(authorisedAt.getTime() + durationDays * DAY_MS);\\n\\n  return {\\n    consentId: consentId || `cdr-${crypto.randomUUID?.() || Date.now()}`,\\n    customerId,\\n    scopes: normaliseScopes(scopes),\\n    status: \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"",\\n    authorisedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(authorisedAt),\\n    expiresAtIso: formatAustralianIso(expiresAt),\\n    accounts,\\n    revokedAtIso: null,\\n    revocationReason: null,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function isConsentExpired(consent, atIso = formatAustralianIso(new Date())) {\\n  const at = parseAustralianIso(atIso);\\n  const expiry = parseAustralianIso(consent.expiresAtIso);\\n  return at.getTime() >= expiry.getTime();\\n}\\n\\nfunction markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso) {\\n  if (consent.status !== \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"") return consent;\\n  if (!isConsentExpired(consent, atIso)) return consent;\\n\\n  return {\\n    ...consent,\\n    status: \\\""EXPIRED\\\"",\\n    revocationReason: \\\""Consent expired by statutory time limit.\\\"",\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function authorizeAccess(consents, request) {\\n  const timestampIso = request.timestampIso || formatAustralianIso(new Date());\\n  parseAustralianIso(timestampIso);\\n  assertScope(request.requestedScope);\\n\\n  let inspectedConsent = null;\\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\\n    if (consent.consentId !== request.consentId) return consent;\\n    inspectedConsent = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, timestampIso);\\n    return inspectedConsent;\\n  });\\n\\n  if (!inspectedConsent) {\\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""error\\\"", \\\""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\\\"", \\\""Consent was not found.\\\"", {\\n      consentId: request.consentId,\\n      diagnosticContext: request.diagnosticContext,\\n    });\\n    return {\\n      consents: nextConsents,\\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 404, error: event },\\n      event,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (inspectedConsent.status !== \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"") {\\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\n      \\\""error\\\"",\\n      `CONSENT_${inspectedConsent.status}`,\\n      \\\""Consent is not active; access rejected.\\\"",\\n      {\\n        consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n        status: inspectedConsent.status,\\n        bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\\n        accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\\n      },\\n    );\\n    return {\\n      consents: nextConsents,\\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\\n      event,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!inspectedConsent.scopes.includes(request.requestedScope)) {\\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""error\\\"", \\\""SCOPE_NOT_CONSENTED\\\"", \\\""Requested scope is not consented.\\\"", {\\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n      requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\\n      consentedScopes: inspectedConsent.scopes,\\n      bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\\n      accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\\n    });\\n    return {\\n      consents: nextConsents,\\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\\n      event,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""info\\\"", \\\""ACCESS_GRANTED\\\"", \\\""CDR access granted for active consented scope.\\\"", {\\n    consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n    requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\\n    accountCount: inspectedConsent.accounts?.length || 0,\\n  });\\n\\n  return {\\n    consents: nextConsents,\\n    result: {\\n      granted: true,\\n      statusCode: 200,\\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n      scope: request.requestedScope,\\n    },\\n    event,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function revokeConsent(consents, consentId, reason = \\\""Customer withdrawal\\\"", at = new Date()) {\\n  const revokedAtIso = formatAustralianIso(at);\\n  let found = false;\\n  let wasAlreadyRevoked = false;\\n\\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\\n    if (consent.consentId !== consentId) return consent;\\n    found = true;\\n    if (consent.status === \\\""REVOKED\\\"") {\\n      wasAlreadyRevoked = true;\\n      return consent;\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      ...consent,\\n      status: \\\""REVOKED\\\"",\\n      revokedAtIso,\\n      revocationReason: reason,\\n    };\\n  });\\n\\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\n    found ? \\\""info\\\"" : \\\""warn\\\"",\\n    found ? (wasAlreadyRevoked ? \\\""CONSENT_REVOKE_IDEMPOTENT\\\"" : \\\""CONSENT_REVOKED\\\"") : \\\""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\\\"",\\n    found ? \\\""Revocation request processed idempotently.\\\"" : \\\""Revocation target was not found.\\\"",\\n    { consentId, reason },\\n  );\\n\\n  return { consents: nextConsents, found, wasAlreadyRevoked, event };\\n}\\n\\nexport function reconcileRevocations(consents, revocationRegistry, now = new Date()) {\\n  const atIso = formatAustralianIso(now);\\n  const revokedIds = new Set(revocationRegistry);\\n  const changedConsentIds = [];\\n\\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\\n    const expiredChecked = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso);\\n    if (expiredChecked !== consent) changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\\n\\n    if (revokedIds.has(consent.consentId) && expiredChecked.status !== \\\""REVOKED\\\"") {\\n      changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\\n      return {\\n        ...expiredChecked,\\n        status: \\\""REVOKED\\\"",\\n        revokedAtIso: atIso,\\n        revocationReason: \\\""Matched external revocation registry.\\\"",\\n      };\\n    }\\n    return expiredChecked;\\n  });\\n\\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""info\\\"", \\\""HOURLY_RECONCILIATION\\\"", \\\""Revocation reconciliation completed.\\\"", {\\n    checkedConsentCount: consents.length,\\n    registryCount: revokedIds.size,\\n    changedConsentIds: [...new Set(changedConsentIds)],\\n  });\\n\\n  return { consents: nextConsents, event };\\n}\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/App.jsx\"",\""contents\"":\""import { useEffect, useMemo, useState } from \\\""react\\\"";\\nimport {\\n  CDR_SCOPES,\\n  authorizeAccess,\\n  createConsent,\\n  formatAustralianIso,\\n  maskAccountNumber,\\n  maskBsb,\\n  reconcileRevocations,\\n  revokeConsent,\\n} from \\\""./cdrGateway.js\\\"";\\n\\nfunction daysAgo(days) {\\n  return new Date(Date.now() - days * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\\n}\\n\\nfunction buildInitialState() {\\n  const active = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-active-001\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-9271\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"", \\\""bank:transactions:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 180,\\n    now: daysAgo(2),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Everyday Offset\\\"", bsb: \\\""083-001\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""123456789\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const limited = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-basic-only-002\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-4418\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 90,\\n    now: daysAgo(1),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Savings\\\"", bsb: \\\""062-111\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""7788990011\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const expired = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-expired-003\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-7130\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"", \\\""bank:accounts.detail:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 1,\\n    now: daysAgo(4),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Closed Loan\\\"", bsb: \\\""182-222\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""4567891234\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const withdrawn = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-withdrawn-004\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-6580\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"", \\\""bank:transactions:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 365,\\n    now: daysAgo(3),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Transaction Account\\\"", bsb: \\\""032-999\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""987654321\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const revoked = revokeConsent(\\n    [withdrawn],\\n    withdrawn.consentId,\\n    \\\""Customer withdrew consent for account 987654321\\\"",\\n    daysAgo(1),\\n  ).consents[0];\\n\\n  return {\\n    consents: [active, limited, expired, revoked],\\n    registry: [revoked.consentId],\\n    logs: [\\n      {\\n        level: \\\""info\\\"",\\n        code: \\\""GATEWAY_READY\\\"",\\n        message: \\\""In-memory CDR Consent Gateway loaded with sample consents.\\\"",\\n        observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n        details: { statutoryMaxDurationDays: 365, timezone: \\\""Australia/Sydney\\\"" },\\n      },\\n    ],\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction statusLabel(status) {\\n  if (status === \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"") return \\\""Authorised\\\"";\\n  if (status === \\\""REVOKED\\\"") return \\\""Revoked\\\"";\\n  return \\\""Expired\\\"";\\n}\\n\\nfunction LogEntry({ entry }) {\\n  return (\\n    <article className={`log-entry log-${entry.level}`}>\\n      <div className=\\\""log-entry__header\\\"">\\n        <strong>{entry.code}</strong>\\n        <span>{entry.observedAtIso}</span>\\n      </div>\\n      <p>{entry.message}</p>\\n      {entry.details ? <pre>{JSON.stringify(entry.details, null, 2)}</pre> : null}\\n    </article>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nfunction ConsentCard({ consent, isSelected, onSelect }) {\\n  const primaryAccount = consent.accounts?.[0];\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button\\n      type=\\\""button\\\""\\n      className={`consent-card ${isSelected ? \\\""consent-card--selected\\\"" : \\\""\\\""}`}\\n      onClick={() => onSelect(consent.consentId)}\\n    >\\n      <span className={`status status--${consent.status.toLowerCase()}`}>{statusLabel(consent.status)}</span>\\n      <strong>{consent.consentId}</strong>\\n      <small>{consent.customerId}</small>\\n      <div className=\\\""account-line\\\"">\\n        {primaryAccount ? `${maskBsb(primaryAccount.bsb)} ${maskAccountNumber(primaryAccount.accountNumber)}` : \\\""No account\\\""}\\n      </div>\\n      <div className=\\\""date-grid\\\"">\\n        <span>Authorised</span>\\n        <time>{consent.authorisedAtIso}</time>\\n        <span>Expires</span>\\n        <time>{consent.expiresAtIso}</time>\\n      </div>\\n      <ul>\\n        {consent.scopes.map((scope) => (\\n          <li key={scope}>{scope}</li>\\n        ))}\\n      </ul>\\n    </button>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const initial = useMemo(buildInitialState, []);\\n  const [consents, setConsents] = useState(initial.consents);\\n  const [revocationRegistry, setRevocationRegistry] = useState(initial.registry);\\n  const [logs, setLogs] = useState(initial.logs);\\n  const [selectedConsentId, setSelectedConsentId] = useState(initial.consents[0].consentId);\\n  const [requestedScope, setRequestedScope] = useState(\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"");\\n  const [lastResult, setLastResult] = useState(null);\\n\\n  const selectedConsent = consents.find((consent) => consent.consentId === selectedConsentId);\\n\\n  function prependLog(event) {\\n    setLogs((current) => [event, ...current].slice(0, 12));\\n  }\\n\\n  function runAccessRequest() {\\n    const { consents: nextConsents, result, event } = authorizeAccess(consents, {\\n      consentId: selectedConsentId,\\n      requestedScope,\\n      timestampIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n      diagnosticContext: \\\""Standard trace for BSB 083-001 account 123456789\\\"",\\n    });\\n\\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\\n    setLastResult(result);\\n    prependLog(event);\\n  }\\n\\n  function withdrawSelectedConsent() {\\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = revokeConsent(\\n      consents,\\n      selectedConsentId,\\n      \\\""Customer withdrawal received for account 123456789\\\"",\\n    );\\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\\n    setLastResult(null);\\n    prependLog(event);\\n  }\\n\\n  function addSelectedToRegistry() {\\n    setRevocationRegistry((current) =>\\n      current.includes(selectedConsentId) ? current : [...current, selectedConsentId],\\n    );\\n    prependLog({\\n      level: \\\""info\\\"",\\n      code: \\\""REGISTRY_UPDATED\\\"",\\n      message: \\\""Consent added to simulated external revocation registry.\\\"",\\n      observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n      details: { consentId: selectedConsentId },\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  function runReconciliation() {\\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\\n      consents,\\n      revocationRegistry,\\n      new Date(),\\n    );\\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\\n    setLastResult(null);\\n    prependLog(event);\\n  }\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const hourlyReconciliation = window.setInterval(() => {\\n      setConsents((currentConsents) => {\\n        const { consents: reconciledConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\\n          currentConsents,\\n          revocationRegistry,\\n          new Date(),\\n        );\\n        setLogs((currentLogs) => [event, ...currentLogs].slice(0, 12));\\n        return reconciledConsents;\\n      });\\n    }, 60 * 60 * 1000);\\n\\n    return () => window.clearInterval(hourlyReconciliation);\\n  }, [revocationRegistry]);\\n\\n  const activeCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"").length;\\n  const revokedCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \\\""REVOKED\\\"").length;\\n  const expiredCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \\\""EXPIRED\\\"").length;\\n\\n  return (\\n    <main className=\\\""shell\\\"">\\n      <section className=\\\""hero\\\"">\\n        <div>\\n          <p className=\\\""eyebrow\\\"">Consumer Data Right</p>\\n          <h1>CDR Consent &amp; Scoping Gateway</h1>\\n          <p>\\n            Validates consented scopes, rejects withdrawn or expired arrangements, reconciles revocation\\n            registries, and masks Australian banking identifiers in telemetry.\\n          </p>\\n        </div>\\n        <div className=\\\""clock-card\\\"">\\n          <span>Gateway time anchor</span>\\n          <strong>{formatAustralianIso(new Date())}</strong>\\n          <small>Generated with Australia/Sydney +10:00/+11:00 offsets, not browser-local formatting.</small>\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n\\n      <section className=\\\""metrics\\\"" aria-label=\\\""Consent status summary\\\"">\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>{activeCount}</strong>\\n          <span>Authorised</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>{revokedCount}</strong>\\n          <span>Revoked</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>{expiredCount}</strong>\\n          <span>Expired</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>365</strong>\\n          <span>Max days</span>\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n\\n      <div className=\\\""workspace\\\"">\\n        <section className=\\\""panel\\\"">\\n          <div className=\\\""panel-heading\\\"">\\n            <h2>Consent arrangements</h2>\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" onClick={runReconciliation}>Run reconciliation</button>\\n          </div>\\n          <div className=\\\""consent-list\\\"">\\n            {consents.map((consent) => (\\n              <ConsentCard\\n                key={consent.consentId}\\n                consent={consent}\\n                isSelected={consent.consentId === selectedConsentId}\\n                onSelect={setSelectedConsentId}\\n              />\\n            ))}\\n          </div>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section className=\\\""panel control-panel\\\"">\\n          <h2>Access request simulator</h2>\\n          <label>\\n            Consent ID\\n            <select value={selectedConsentId} onChange={(event) => setSelectedConsentId(event.target.value)}>\\n              {consents.map((consent) => (\\n                <option key={consent.consentId} value={consent.consentId}>\\n                  {consent.consentId}\\n                </option>\\n              ))}\\n            </select>\\n          </label>\\n          <label>\\n            Requested CDR scope\\n            <select value={requestedScope} onChange={(event) => setRequestedScope(event.target.value)}>\\n              {CDR_SCOPES.map((scope) => (\\n                <option key={scope} value={scope}>{scope}</option>\\n              ))}\\n            </select>\\n          </label>\\n          <div className=\\\""button-row\\\"">\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" className=\\\""primary\\\"" onClick={runAccessRequest}>Authorize request</button>\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" onClick={withdrawSelectedConsent}>Withdraw consent</button>\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" onClick={addSelectedToRegistry}>Add to registry</button>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {selectedConsent ? (\\n            <div className=\\\""selected-summary\\\"">\\n              <h3>Selected arrangement</h3>\\n              <p><strong>Status:</strong> {statusLabel(selectedConsent.status)}</p>\\n              <p><strong>Scopes:</strong> {selectedConsent.scopes.join(\\\"", \\\"")}</p>\\n              {selectedConsent.revocationReason ? (\\n                <p><strong>Revocation reason:</strong> {selectedConsent.revocationReason}</p>\\n              ) : null}\\n            </div>\\n          ) : null}\\n\\n          {lastResult ? (\\n            <div className={`result result--${lastResult.granted ? \\\""granted\\\"" : \\\""denied\\\""}`}>\\n              <strong>{lastResult.granted ? \\\""Access granted\\\"" : \\\""Access denied\\\""}</strong>\\n              <pre>{JSON.stringify(lastResult, null, 2)}</pre>\\n            </div>\\n          ) : null}\\n        </section>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      <section className=\\\""panel\\\"">\\n        <div className=\\\""panel-heading\\\"">\\n          <h2>Sanitized telemetry &amp; error trace</h2>\\n          <span className=\\\""registry-count\\\"">Registry entries: {revocationRegistry.length}</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div className=\\\""logs\\\"">\\n          {logs.map((entry, index) => (\\n            <LogEntry key={`${entry.code}-${entry.observedAtIso}-${index}`} entry={entry} />\\n          ))}\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n    </main>\\n  );\\n}\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/styles.css\"",\""contents\"":\"":root {\\n  font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\""Segoe UI\\\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\\n  color: #172033;\\n  background: #f5f7fb;\\n  font-synthesis: none;\\n  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;\\n}\\n\\n* {\\n  box-sizing: border-box;\\n}\\n\\nbody {\\n  margin: 0;\\n}\\n\\nbutton,\\nselect {\\n  font: inherit;\\n}\\n\\nbutton {\\n  cursor: pointer;\\n}\\n\\n.shell {\\n  width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px));\\n  margin: 0 auto;\\n  padding: 32px 0 48px;\\n}\\n\\n.hero {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 360px;\\n  gap: 24px;\\n  align-items: stretch;\\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.hero > div:first-child,\\n.clock-card,\\n.panel,\\n.metrics > div {\\n  background: #ffffff;\\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\\n  border-radius: 22px;\\n  box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);\\n}\\n\\n.hero > div:first-child {\\n  padding: 32px;\\n}\\n\\n.eyebrow {\\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\\n  color: #0f766e;\\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\\n  text-transform: uppercase;\\n}\\n\\nh1,\\nh2,\\nh3,\\np {\\n  margin-top: 0;\\n}\\n\\nh1 {\\n  max-width: 760px;\\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem);\\n  line-height: 1;\\n  letter-spacing: -0.05em;\\n}\\n\\n.hero p {\\n  max-width: 780px;\\n  margin-bottom: 0;\\n  color: #475569;\\n  line-height: 1.7;\\n}\\n\\n.clock-card {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n  justify-content: center;\\n  gap: 10px;\\n  padding: 28px;\\n  background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0f172a, #164e63);\\n  color: white;\\n}\\n\\n.clock-card span,\\n.clock-card small {\\n  color: #bae6fd;\\n}\\n\\n.clock-card strong {\\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\\n  word-break: break-word;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\\n  gap: 16px;\\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics > div {\\n  padding: 20px;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics strong {\\n  display: block;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-size: 2rem;\\n  line-height: 1;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics span {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n  font-weight: 700;\\n}\\n\\n.workspace {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(340px, 0.85fr);\\n  gap: 24px;\\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.panel {\\n  padding: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.panel-heading {\\n  display: flex;\\n  gap: 16px;\\n  align-items: center;\\n  justify-content: space-between;\\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\\n}\\n\\n.panel h2 {\\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\\n}\\n\\n.panel-heading h2 {\\n  margin-bottom: 0;\\n}\\n\\n.panel-heading button,\\n.button-row button {\\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 10px 14px;\\n  background: white;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.button-row .primary {\\n  border-color: #0f766e;\\n  background: #0f766e;\\n  color: white;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-list {\\n  display: grid;\\n  gap: 14px;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card {\\n  width: 100%;\\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\\n  border-radius: 18px;\\n  padding: 16px;\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n  color: inherit;\\n  text-align: left;\\n  transition: border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card:hover,\\n.consent-card--selected {\\n  border-color: #0f766e;\\n  box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15, 118, 110, 0.12);\\n  transform: translateY(-1px);\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card strong,\\n.consent-card small,\\n.account-line {\\n  display: block;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card strong {\\n  margin-top: 10px;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card small,\\n.account-line,\\n.date-grid,\\n.consent-card li {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n}\\n\\n.account-line {\\n  margin-top: 6px;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.status {\\n  display: inline-flex;\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 5px 10px;\\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\\n  font-weight: 900;\\n  text-transform: uppercase;\\n}\\n\\n.status--authorised {\\n  background: #dcfce7;\\n  color: #166534;\\n}\\n\\n.status--revoked {\\n  background: #fee2e2;\\n  color: #991b1b;\\n}\\n\\n.status--expired {\\n  background: #fef3c7;\\n  color: #92400e;\\n}\\n\\n.date-grid {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: 86px minmax(0, 1fr);\\n  gap: 4px 10px;\\n  margin-top: 12px;\\n  font-size: 0.86rem;\\n}\\n\\n.date-grid span {\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.date-grid time {\\n  word-break: break-word;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card ul {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n  gap: 8px;\\n  padding: 0;\\n  margin: 12px 0 0;\\n  list-style: none;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card li {\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 5px 8px;\\n  background: #e0f2fe;\\n  color: #075985;\\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.control-panel label {\\n  display: grid;\\n  gap: 8px;\\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\\n  color: #334155;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\nselect {\\n  width: 100%;\\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\\n  border-radius: 12px;\\n  padding: 11px 12px;\\n  background: white;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n}\\n\\n.button-row {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n  gap: 10px;\\n  margin: 18px 0;\\n}\\n\\n.selected-summary,\\n.result {\\n  border-radius: 16px;\\n  padding: 16px;\\n  margin-top: 16px;\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n}\\n\\n.selected-summary h3 {\\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\\n}\\n\\n.selected-summary p {\\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\\n  color: #475569;\\n  line-height: 1.5;\\n}\\n\\n.result {\\n  border: 1px solid;\\n}\\n\\n.result--granted {\\n  border-color: #86efac;\\n  background: #f0fdf4;\\n}\\n\\n.result--denied {\\n  border-color: #fecaca;\\n  background: #fef2f2;\\n}\\n\\npre {\\n  overflow: auto;\\n  margin: 10px 0 0;\\n  border-radius: 12px;\\n  padding: 12px;\\n  background: #0f172a;\\n  color: #dbeafe;\\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\\n  line-height: 1.5;\\n}\\n\\n.registry-count {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.logs {\\n  display: grid;\\n  gap: 12px;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry {\\n  border-left: 5px solid #38bdf8;\\n  border-radius: 14px;\\n  padding: 14px;\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n}\\n\\n.log-error {\\n  border-left-color: #ef4444;\\n}\\n\\n.log-warn {\\n  border-left-color: #f59e0b;\\n}\\n\\n.log-info {\\n  border-left-color: #0f766e;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry__header {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n  gap: 8px 16px;\\n  justify-content: space-between;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry__header strong {\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry__header span,\\n.log-entry p {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry p {\\n  margin: 8px 0 0;\\n}\\n\\n@media (max-width: 920px) {\\n  .hero,\\n  .workspace,\\n  .metrics {\\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\\n  }\\n}\\n\""}],\""reasoning\"":\""The request was broad, so I implemented the full browser-based gateway demonstration expected by the brief rather than asking for narrower scope. Key choices: keep state in memory, make domain logic reusable in `cdrGateway.js`, generate Australian-offset ISO strings without browser-local formatting, enforce the 365-day duration cap in creation, sanitize all returned telemetry, and provide UI controls to demonstrate grant/deny/revoke/reconcile paths.\""}"",""refusal"":null,""annotations"":[],""parsed"":{""message"":""Implemented the in-memory CDR Consent Gateway demo in React. Assumed this should run entirely in the browser with local data/no backend, while exposing the gateway rules as reusable functions under `src/`. It now demonstrates active scope validation, instant idempotent withdrawal, expiry handling, simulated hourly revocation reconciliation, Australian timezone ISO formatting, and sanitized telemetry/error logs. Check the preview by running allowed/denied requests, withdrawing a consent, adding one to the revocation registry, and confirming logs mask BSB/account data."",""files"":[{""path"":""src/cdrGateway.js"",""contents"":""export const CDR_SCOPES = [\n  \""bank:accounts.basic:read\"",\n  \""bank:accounts.detail:read\"",\n  \""bank:transactions:read\"",\n];\n\nconst MAX_CONSENT_DAYS = 365;\nconst DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\nconst AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN = /T\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}(?:\\+10:00|\\+11:00)$/;\n\nfunction pad(value) {\n  return String(value).padStart(2, \""0\"");\n}\n\nfunction firstSundayOfMonth(year, monthIndex) {\n  const firstDay = new Date(Date.UTC(year, monthIndex, 1)).getUTCDay();\n  return 1 + ((7 - firstDay) % 7);\n}\n\nexport function getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant = new Date()) {\n  const utcMs = instant.getTime();\n  const year = instant.getUTCFullYear();\n\n  const dstStartThisYear = Date.UTC(\n    year,\n    9,\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 9),\n    16,\n    0,\n    0,\n  );\n  const dstEndThisYear = Date.UTC(\n    year,\n    3,\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 3),\n    16,\n    0,\n    0,\n  );\n\n  const isDaylightSaving = utcMs >= dstStartThisYear || utcMs < dstEndThisYear;\n  return isDaylightSaving ? 11 * 60 : 10 * 60;\n}\n\nexport function formatAustralianIso(instant = new Date()) {\n  const offsetMinutes = getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant);\n  const localTime = new Date(instant.getTime() + offsetMinutes * 60 * 1000);\n  const offset = offsetMinutes === 660 ? \""+11:00\"" : \""+10:00\"";\n\n  return `${localTime.getUTCFullYear()}-${pad(localTime.getUTCMonth() + 1)}-${pad(\n    localTime.getUTCDate(),\n  )}T${pad(localTime.getUTCHours())}:${pad(localTime.getUTCMinutes())}:${pad(\n    localTime.getUTCSeconds(),\n  )}${offset}`;\n}\n\nexport function parseAustralianIso(isoValue) {\n  if (!AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN.test(isoValue)) {\n    throw new Error(\n      \""Timestamp must be ISO 8601 with an explicit Australian offset (+10:00 or +11:00).\"",\n    );\n  }\n\n  const parsed = new Date(isoValue);\n  if (Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime())) {\n    throw new Error(\""Timestamp is not a valid ISO 8601 value.\"");\n  }\n  return parsed;\n}\n\nexport function maskBsb(value) {\n  const digits = String(value ?? \""\"").replace(/\\D/g, \""\"");\n  if (digits.length !== 6) return \""***-***\"";\n  return `${digits.slice(0, 3)}-***`;\n}\n\nexport function maskAccountNumber(value) {\n  const digits = String(value ?? \""\"").replace(/\\D/g, \""\"");\n  if (digits.length < 4) return \""... ****\"";\n  return `... ${digits.slice(-4)}`;\n}\n\nexport function maskSensitiveIdentifiers(value) {\n  if (typeof value !== \""string\"") return value;\n\n  return value\n    .replace(/\\b(\\d{3})[-\\s]?(\\d{3})\\b/g, \""$1-***\"")\n    .replace(\n      /\\b(account(?:\\s+number)?|acct)\\s*[:#-]?\\s*(\\d{4,12})\\b/gi,\n      (_match, label, accountNumber) => `${label}: ${maskAccountNumber(accountNumber)}`,\n    );\n}\n\nexport function sanitizeTelemetry(input) {\n  if (Array.isArray(input)) {\n    return input.map((entry) => sanitizeTelemetry(entry));\n  }\n\n  if (input && typeof input === \""object\"") {\n    return Object.fromEntries(\n      Object.entries(input).map(([key, value]) => {\n        const lowerKey = key.toLowerCase();\n        if (lowerKey === \""bsb\"") return [key, maskBsb(value)];\n        if (lowerKey === \""accountnumber\"" || lowerKey === \""account\"") {\n          return [key, maskAccountNumber(value)];\n        }\n        return [key, sanitizeTelemetry(value)];\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  return maskSensitiveIdentifiers(input);\n}\n\nfunction createTelemetryEvent(level, code, message, details = {}) {\n  return sanitizeTelemetry({\n    level,\n    code,\n    message,\n    details,\n    observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n  });\n}\n\nfunction assertScope(scope) {\n  if (!CDR_SCOPES.includes(scope)) {\n    throw new Error(`Unsupported CDR scope: ${scope}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction normaliseScopes(scopes) {\n  const unique = [...new Set(scopes)];\n  unique.forEach(assertScope);\n  return unique;\n}\n\nexport function createConsent({\n  consentId,\n  customerId,\n  scopes,\n  durationDays,\n  accounts = [],\n  now = new Date(),\n}) {\n  if (!customerId) throw new Error(\""customerId is required.\"");\n  if (!Number.isInteger(durationDays) || durationDays < 1) {\n    throw new Error(\""Consent duration must be a positive whole number of days.\"");\n  }\n  if (durationDays > MAX_CONSENT_DAYS) {\n    throw new Error(\""Consent duration must not exceed 365 days from creation.\"");\n  }\n\n  const authorisedAt = new Date(now);\n  const expiresAt = new Date(authorisedAt.getTime() + durationDays * DAY_MS);\n\n  return {\n    consentId: consentId || `cdr-${crypto.randomUUID?.() || Date.now()}`,\n    customerId,\n    scopes: normaliseScopes(scopes),\n    status: \""AUTHORISED\"",\n    authorisedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(authorisedAt),\n    expiresAtIso: formatAustralianIso(expiresAt),\n    accounts,\n    revokedAtIso: null,\n    revocationReason: null,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function isConsentExpired(consent, atIso = formatAustralianIso(new Date())) {\n  const at = parseAustralianIso(atIso);\n  const expiry = parseAustralianIso(consent.expiresAtIso);\n  return at.getTime() >= expiry.getTime();\n}\n\nfunction markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso) {\n  if (consent.status !== \""AUTHORISED\"") return consent;\n  if (!isConsentExpired(consent, atIso)) return consent;\n\n  return {\n    ...consent,\n    status: \""EXPIRED\"",\n    revocationReason: \""Consent expired by statutory time limit.\"",\n  };\n}\n\nexport function authorizeAccess(consents, request) {\n  const timestampIso = request.timestampIso || formatAustralianIso(new Date());\n  parseAustralianIso(timestampIso);\n  assertScope(request.requestedScope);\n\n  let inspectedConsent = null;\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\n    if (consent.consentId !== request.consentId) return consent;\n    inspectedConsent = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, timestampIso);\n    return inspectedConsent;\n  });\n\n  if (!inspectedConsent) {\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""error\"", \""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\"", \""Consent was not found.\"", {\n      consentId: request.consentId,\n      diagnosticContext: request.diagnosticContext,\n    });\n    return {\n      consents: nextConsents,\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 404, error: event },\n      event,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (inspectedConsent.status !== \""AUTHORISED\"") {\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\n      \""error\"",\n      `CONSENT_${inspectedConsent.status}`,\n      \""Consent is not active; access rejected.\"",\n      {\n        consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n        status: inspectedConsent.status,\n        bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\n        accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\n      },\n    );\n    return {\n      consents: nextConsents,\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\n      event,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!inspectedConsent.scopes.includes(request.requestedScope)) {\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""error\"", \""SCOPE_NOT_CONSENTED\"", \""Requested scope is not consented.\"", {\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n      requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\n      consentedScopes: inspectedConsent.scopes,\n      bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\n      accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\n    });\n    return {\n      consents: nextConsents,\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\n      event,\n    };\n  }\n\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""info\"", \""ACCESS_GRANTED\"", \""CDR access granted for active consented scope.\"", {\n    consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n    requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\n    accountCount: inspectedConsent.accounts?.length || 0,\n  });\n\n  return {\n    consents: nextConsents,\n    result: {\n      granted: true,\n      statusCode: 200,\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n      scope: request.requestedScope,\n    },\n    event,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function revokeConsent(consents, consentId, reason = \""Customer withdrawal\"", at = new Date()) {\n  const revokedAtIso = formatAustralianIso(at);\n  let found = false;\n  let wasAlreadyRevoked = false;\n\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\n    if (consent.consentId !== consentId) return consent;\n    found = true;\n    if (consent.status === \""REVOKED\"") {\n      wasAlreadyRevoked = true;\n      return consent;\n    }\n    return {\n      ...consent,\n      status: \""REVOKED\"",\n      revokedAtIso,\n      revocationReason: reason,\n    };\n  });\n\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\n    found ? \""info\"" : \""warn\"",\n    found ? (wasAlreadyRevoked ? \""CONSENT_REVOKE_IDEMPOTENT\"" : \""CONSENT_REVOKED\"") : \""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\"",\n    found ? \""Revocation request processed idempotently.\"" : \""Revocation target was not found.\"",\n    { consentId, reason },\n  );\n\n  return { consents: nextConsents, found, wasAlreadyRevoked, event };\n}\n\nexport function reconcileRevocations(consents, revocationRegistry, now = new Date()) {\n  const atIso = formatAustralianIso(now);\n  const revokedIds = new Set(revocationRegistry);\n  const changedConsentIds = [];\n\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\n    const expiredChecked = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso);\n    if (expiredChecked !== consent) changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\n\n    if (revokedIds.has(consent.consentId) && expiredChecked.status !== \""REVOKED\"") {\n      changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\n      return {\n        ...expiredChecked,\n        status: \""REVOKED\"",\n        revokedAtIso: atIso,\n        revocationReason: \""Matched external revocation registry.\"",\n      };\n    }\n    return expiredChecked;\n  });\n\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""info\"", \""HOURLY_RECONCILIATION\"", \""Revocation reconciliation completed.\"", {\n    checkedConsentCount: consents.length,\n    registryCount: revokedIds.size,\n    changedConsentIds: [...new Set(changedConsentIds)],\n  });\n\n  return { consents: nextConsents, event };\n}\n""},{""path"":""src/App.jsx"",""contents"":""import { useEffect, useMemo, useState } from \""react\"";\nimport {\n  CDR_SCOPES,\n  authorizeAccess,\n  createConsent,\n  formatAustralianIso,\n  maskAccountNumber,\n  maskBsb,\n  reconcileRevocations,\n  revokeConsent,\n} from \""./cdrGateway.js\"";\n\nfunction daysAgo(days) {\n  return new Date(Date.now() - days * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\n}\n\nfunction buildInitialState() {\n  const active = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-active-001\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-9271\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"", \""bank:transactions:read\""],\n    durationDays: 180,\n    now: daysAgo(2),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Everyday Offset\"", bsb: \""083-001\"", accountNumber: \""123456789\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const limited = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-basic-only-002\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-4418\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\""],\n    durationDays: 90,\n    now: daysAgo(1),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Savings\"", bsb: \""062-111\"", accountNumber: \""7788990011\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const expired = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-expired-003\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-7130\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"", \""bank:accounts.detail:read\""],\n    durationDays: 1,\n    now: daysAgo(4),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Closed Loan\"", bsb: \""182-222\"", accountNumber: \""4567891234\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const withdrawn = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-withdrawn-004\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-6580\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"", \""bank:transactions:read\""],\n    durationDays: 365,\n    now: daysAgo(3),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Transaction Account\"", bsb: \""032-999\"", accountNumber: \""987654321\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const revoked = revokeConsent(\n    [withdrawn],\n    withdrawn.consentId,\n    \""Customer withdrew consent for account 987654321\"",\n    daysAgo(1),\n  ).consents[0];\n\n  return {\n    consents: [active, limited, expired, revoked],\n    registry: [revoked.consentId],\n    logs: [\n      {\n        level: \""info\"",\n        code: \""GATEWAY_READY\"",\n        message: \""In-memory CDR Consent Gateway loaded with sample consents.\"",\n        observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n        details: { statutoryMaxDurationDays: 365, timezone: \""Australia/Sydney\"" },\n      },\n    ],\n  };\n}\n\nfunction statusLabel(status) {\n  if (status === \""AUTHORISED\"") return \""Authorised\"";\n  if (status === \""REVOKED\"") return \""Revoked\"";\n  return \""Expired\"";\n}\n\nfunction LogEntry({ entry }) {\n  return (\n    <article className={`log-entry log-${entry.level}`}>\n      <div className=\""log-entry__header\"">\n        <strong>{entry.code}</strong>\n        <span>{entry.observedAtIso}</span>\n      </div>\n      <p>{entry.message}</p>\n      {entry.details ? <pre>{JSON.stringify(entry.details, null, 2)}</pre> : null}\n    </article>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ConsentCard({ consent, isSelected, onSelect }) {\n  const primaryAccount = consent.accounts?.[0];\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\""button\""\n      className={`consent-card ${isSelected ? \""consent-card--selected\"" : \""\""}`}\n      onClick={() => onSelect(consent.consentId)}\n    >\n      <span className={`status status--${consent.status.toLowerCase()}`}>{statusLabel(consent.status)}</span>\n      <strong>{consent.consentId}</strong>\n      <small>{consent.customerId}</small>\n      <div className=\""account-line\"">\n        {primaryAccount ? `${maskBsb(primaryAccount.bsb)} ${maskAccountNumber(primaryAccount.accountNumber)}` : \""No account\""}\n      </div>\n      <div className=\""date-grid\"">\n        <span>Authorised</span>\n        <time>{consent.authorisedAtIso}</time>\n        <span>Expires</span>\n        <time>{consent.expiresAtIso}</time>\n      </div>\n      <ul>\n        {consent.scopes.map((scope) => (\n          <li key={scope}>{scope}</li>\n        ))}\n      </ul>\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const initial = useMemo(buildInitialState, []);\n  const [consents, setConsents] = useState(initial.consents);\n  const [revocationRegistry, setRevocationRegistry] = useState(initial.registry);\n  const [logs, setLogs] = useState(initial.logs);\n  const [selectedConsentId, setSelectedConsentId] = useState(initial.consents[0].consentId);\n  const [requestedScope, setRequestedScope] = useState(\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"");\n  const [lastResult, setLastResult] = useState(null);\n\n  const selectedConsent = consents.find((consent) => consent.consentId === selectedConsentId);\n\n  function prependLog(event) {\n    setLogs((current) => [event, ...current].slice(0, 12));\n  }\n\n  function runAccessRequest() {\n    const { consents: nextConsents, result, event } = authorizeAccess(consents, {\n      consentId: selectedConsentId,\n      requestedScope,\n      timestampIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n      diagnosticContext: \""Standard trace for BSB 083-001 account 123456789\"",\n    });\n\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\n    setLastResult(result);\n    prependLog(event);\n  }\n\n  function withdrawSelectedConsent() {\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = revokeConsent(\n      consents,\n      selectedConsentId,\n      \""Customer withdrawal received for account 123456789\"",\n    );\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\n    setLastResult(null);\n    prependLog(event);\n  }\n\n  function addSelectedToRegistry() {\n    setRevocationRegistry((current) =>\n      current.includes(selectedConsentId) ? current : [...current, selectedConsentId],\n    );\n    prependLog({\n      level: \""info\"",\n      code: \""REGISTRY_UPDATED\"",\n      message: \""Consent added to simulated external revocation registry.\"",\n      observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n      details: { consentId: selectedConsentId },\n    });\n  }\n\n  function runReconciliation() {\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\n      consents,\n      revocationRegistry,\n      new Date(),\n    );\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\n    setLastResult(null);\n    prependLog(event);\n  }\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const hourlyReconciliation = window.setInterval(() => {\n      setConsents((currentConsents) => {\n        const { consents: reconciledConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\n          currentConsents,\n          revocationRegistry,\n          new Date(),\n        );\n        setLogs((currentLogs) => [event, ...currentLogs].slice(0, 12));\n        return reconciledConsents;\n      });\n    }, 60 * 60 * 1000);\n\n    return () => window.clearInterval(hourlyReconciliation);\n  }, [revocationRegistry]);\n\n  const activeCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \""AUTHORISED\"").length;\n  const revokedCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \""REVOKED\"").length;\n  const expiredCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \""EXPIRED\"").length;\n\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <section className=\""hero\"">\n        <div>\n          <p className=\""eyebrow\"">Consumer Data Right</p>\n          <h1>CDR Consent &amp; Scoping Gateway</h1>\n          <p>\n            Validates consented scopes, rejects withdrawn or expired arrangements, reconciles revocation\n            registries, and masks Australian banking identifiers in telemetry.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\""clock-card\"">\n          <span>Gateway time anchor</span>\n          <strong>{formatAustralianIso(new Date())}</strong>\n          <small>Generated with Australia/Sydney +10:00/+11:00 offsets, not browser-local formatting.</small>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section className=\""metrics\"" aria-label=\""Consent status summary\"">\n        <div>\n          <strong>{activeCount}</strong>\n          <span>Authorised</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <strong>{revokedCount}</strong>\n          <span>Revoked</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <strong>{expiredCount}</strong>\n          <span>Expired</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <strong>365</strong>\n          <span>Max days</span>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <div className=\""workspace\"">\n        <section className=\""panel\"">\n          <div className=\""panel-heading\"">\n            <h2>Consent arrangements</h2>\n            <button type=\""button\"" onClick={runReconciliation}>Run reconciliation</button>\n          </div>\n          <div className=\""consent-list\"">\n            {consents.map((consent) => (\n              <ConsentCard\n                key={consent.consentId}\n                consent={consent}\n                isSelected={consent.consentId === selectedConsentId}\n                onSelect={setSelectedConsentId}\n              />\n            ))}\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section className=\""panel control-panel\"">\n          <h2>Access request simulator</h2>\n          <label>\n            Consent ID\n            <select value={selectedConsentId} onChange={(event) => setSelectedConsentId(event.target.value)}>\n              {consents.map((consent) => (\n                <option key={consent.consentId} value={consent.consentId}>\n                  {consent.consentId}\n                </option>\n              ))}\n            </select>\n          </label>\n          <label>\n            Requested CDR scope\n            <select value={requestedScope} onChange={(event) => setRequestedScope(event.target.value)}>\n              {CDR_SCOPES.map((scope) => (\n                <option key={scope} value={scope}>{scope}</option>\n              ))}\n            </select>\n          </label>\n          <div className=\""button-row\"">\n            <button type=\""button\"" className=\""primary\"" onClick={runAccessRequest}>Authorize request</button>\n            <button type=\""button\"" onClick={withdrawSelectedConsent}>Withdraw consent</button>\n            <button type=\""button\"" onClick={addSelectedToRegistry}>Add to registry</button>\n          </div>\n\n          {selectedConsent ? (\n            <div className=\""selected-summary\"">\n              <h3>Selected arrangement</h3>\n              <p><strong>Status:</strong> {statusLabel(selectedConsent.status)}</p>\n              <p><strong>Scopes:</strong> {selectedConsent.scopes.join(\"", \"")}</p>\n              {selectedConsent.revocationReason ? (\n                <p><strong>Revocation reason:</strong> {selectedConsent.revocationReason}</p>\n              ) : null}\n            </div>\n          ) : null}\n\n          {lastResult ? (\n            <div className={`result result--${lastResult.granted ? \""granted\"" : \""denied\""}`}>\n              <strong>{lastResult.granted ? \""Access granted\"" : \""Access denied\""}</strong>\n              <pre>{JSON.stringify(lastResult, null, 2)}</pre>\n            </div>\n          ) : null}\n        </section>\n      </div>\n\n      <section className=\""panel\"">\n        <div className=\""panel-heading\"">\n          <h2>Sanitized telemetry &amp; error trace</h2>\n          <span className=\""registry-count\"">Registry entries: {revocationRegistry.length}</span>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\""logs\"">\n          {logs.map((entry, index) => (\n            <LogEntry key={`${entry.code}-${entry.observedAtIso}-${index}`} entry={entry} />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n""},{""path"":""src/styles.css"",""contents"":"":root {\n  font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #172033;\n  background: #f5f7fb;\n  font-synthesis: none;\n  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\nbutton,\nselect {\n  font: inherit;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px));\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 32px 0 48px;\n}\n\n.hero {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 360px;\n  gap: 24px;\n  align-items: stretch;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.hero > div:first-child,\n.clock-card,\n.panel,\n.metrics > div {\n  background: #ffffff;\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\n  border-radius: 22px;\n  box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);\n}\n\n.hero > div:first-child {\n  padding: 32px;\n}\n\n.eyebrow {\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\n  color: #0f766e;\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\n  font-weight: 800;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\nh1,\nh2,\nh3,\np {\n  margin-top: 0;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  max-width: 760px;\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem);\n  line-height: 1;\n  letter-spacing: -0.05em;\n}\n\n.hero p {\n  max-width: 780px;\n  margin-bottom: 0;\n  color: #475569;\n  line-height: 1.7;\n}\n\n.clock-card {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 10px;\n  padding: 28px;\n  background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0f172a, #164e63);\n  color: white;\n}\n\n.clock-card span,\n.clock-card small {\n  color: #bae6fd;\n}\n\n.clock-card strong {\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n\n.metrics {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\n  gap: 16px;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.metrics > div {\n  padding: 20px;\n}\n\n.metrics strong {\n  display: block;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-size: 2rem;\n  line-height: 1;\n}\n\n.metrics span {\n  color: #64748b;\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.workspace {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(340px, 0.85fr);\n  gap: 24px;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.panel {\n  padding: 24px;\n}\n\n.panel-heading {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 16px;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n.panel h2 {\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\n}\n\n.panel-heading h2 {\n  margin-bottom: 0;\n}\n\n.panel-heading button,\n.button-row button {\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  background: white;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.button-row .primary {\n  border-color: #0f766e;\n  background: #0f766e;\n  color: white;\n}\n\n.consent-list {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 14px;\n}\n\n.consent-card {\n  width: 100%;\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\n  border-radius: 18px;\n  padding: 16px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n  color: inherit;\n  text-align: left;\n  transition: border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;\n}\n\n.consent-card:hover,\n.consent-card--selected {\n  border-color: #0f766e;\n  box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15, 118, 110, 0.12);\n  transform: translateY(-1px);\n}\n\n.consent-card strong,\n.consent-card small,\n.account-line {\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.consent-card strong {\n  margin-top: 10px;\n  color: #0f172a;\n}\n\n.consent-card small,\n.account-line,\n.date-grid,\n.consent-card li {\n  color: #64748b;\n}\n\n.account-line {\n  margin-top: 6px;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.status {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 5px 10px;\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\n  font-weight: 900;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\n.status--authorised {\n  background: #dcfce7;\n  color: #166534;\n}\n\n.status--revoked {\n  background: #fee2e2;\n  color: #991b1b;\n}\n\n.status--expired {\n  background: #fef3c7;\n  color: #92400e;\n}\n\n.date-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 86px minmax(0, 1fr);\n  gap: 4px 10px;\n  margin-top: 12px;\n  font-size: 0.86rem;\n}\n\n.date-grid span {\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.date-grid time {\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n\n.consent-card ul {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 8px;\n  padding: 0;\n  margin: 12px 0 0;\n  list-style: none;\n}\n\n.consent-card li {\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 5px 8px;\n  background: #e0f2fe;\n  color: #075985;\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.control-panel label {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 8px;\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n  color: #334155;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\nselect {\n  width: 100%;\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 11px 12px;\n  background: white;\n  color: #0f172a;\n}\n\n.button-row {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 10px;\n  margin: 18px 0;\n}\n\n.selected-summary,\n.result {\n  border-radius: 16px;\n  padding: 16px;\n  margin-top: 16px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n}\n\n.selected-summary h3 {\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.selected-summary p {\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  color: #475569;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.result {\n  border: 1px solid;\n}\n\n.result--granted {\n  border-color: #86efac;\n  background: #f0fdf4;\n}\n\n.result--denied {\n  border-color: #fecaca;\n  background: #fef2f2;\n}\n\npre {\n  overflow: auto;\n  margin: 10px 0 0;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  background: #0f172a;\n  color: #dbeafe;\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.registry-count {\n  color: #64748b;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.logs {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.log-entry {\n  border-left: 5px solid #38bdf8;\n  border-radius: 14px;\n  padding: 14px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n}\n\n.log-error {\n  border-left-color: #ef4444;\n}\n\n.log-warn {\n  border-left-color: #f59e0b;\n}\n\n.log-info {\n  border-left-color: #0f766e;\n}\n\n.log-entry__header {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 8px 16px;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n}\n\n.log-entry__header strong {\n  color: #0f172a;\n}\n\n.log-entry__header span,\n.log-entry p {\n  color: #64748b;\n}\n\n.log-entry p {\n  margin: 8px 0 0;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 920px) {\n  .hero,\n  .workspace,\n  .metrics {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n}\n""}],""reasoning"":""The request was broad, so I implemented the full browser-based gateway demonstration expected by the brief rather than asking for narrower scope. Key choices: keep state in memory, make domain logic reusable in `cdrGateway.js`, generate Australian-offset ISO strings without browser-local formatting, enforce the 365-day duration cap in creation, sanitize all returned telemetry, and provide UI controls to demonstrate grant/deny/revoke/reconcile paths.""}}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_schema\"",\""json_schema\"":{\""name\"":\""assistant_output\"",\""strict\"":true,\""schema\"":{\""$schema\"":\""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""message\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""},\""files\"":{\""type\"":\""array\"",\""items\"":{\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""path\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""},\""contents\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""}},\""required\"":[\""path\"",\""contents\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false},\""description\"":\""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""},\""reasoning\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""}},\""required\"":[\""message\"",\""files\"",\""reasoning\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false}}}"",""turnSeq"":""1"",""challengeTitle"":""Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","83949","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","7056675e1aaa63a8f50d00f789783e123c2eb2cb","t-f8b2f00d-5f02-42f4-a7c6-6caaa31c6e0c","[]"
"t-f8b2f00d-5f02-42f4-a7c6-6caaa31c6e0c","f8b2f00d-5f02-42f4-a7c6-6caaa31c6e0c","ai_stage:assistant","SPAN","ai_stage:assistant","2026-09-29 16:35:30.810000","","","default","","candidate-1","usku64aixf1e766qzwy4gx9r","DEFAULT","","","","","","","{}","{}","{}","0","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for Macquarie.\n\n# Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent & Scoping Gateway\n\n## The Problem\nUnder Australian Consumer Data Right (CDR) legislation, Accredited Data Recipients (ADRs) and Data Holders must manage fine-grained, time-bound customer consent for financial accounts. You will build a CDR Consent Gateway that validates incoming consent authorizations, scopes account data access, and automatically revokes access when consent expires or is withdrawn.\n\n## Australian Statutory Constraints\n1. **CDR Arrangement Rules**: Consents must expire after a maximum duration of 12 months, with automated hourly reconciliation against revocation registries.\n2. **PII Masking (Privacy Act 1988)**: Australian BSB and Account numbers must be masked (e.g., '083-*** ... 1234') in telemetry and standard error traces.\n3. **AEST Timezone Invariant**: Consent expiry calculations must be anchored to Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST/AEDT) rather than browser-local timezones.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- Gateway grants access only to actively consented scopes (e.g. 'bank:accounts.basic:read').\n- Withdrawn consents instantly reject subsequent data requests.\n- Privacy-compliant error sanitization middleware strips sensitive identifiers.\n</challenge>""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway\n\n# Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent & Scoping Gateway\n\n## The Problem\nUnder Australian Consumer Data Right (CDR) legislation, Accredited Data Recipients (ADRs) and Data Holders must manage fine-grained, time-bound customer consent for financial accounts. You will build a CDR Consent Gateway that validates incoming consent authorizations, scopes account data access, and automatically revokes access when consent expires or is withdrawn.\n\n## Australian Statutory Constraints\n1. **CDR Arrangement Rules**: Consents must expire after a maximum duration of 12 months, with automated hourly reconciliation against revocation registries.\n2. **PII Masking (Privacy Act 1988)**: Australian BSB and Account numbers must be masked (e.g., '083-*** ... 1234') in telemetry and standard error traces.\n3. **AEST Timezone Invariant**: Consent expiry calculations must be anchored to Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST/AEDT) rather than browser-local timezones.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- Gateway grants access only to actively consented scopes (e.g. 'bank:accounts.basic:read').\n- Withdrawn consents instantly reject subsequent data requests.\n- Privacy-compliant error sanitization middleware strips sensitive identifiers.\n\n## Technical Invariants & Constraints\n- Consent duration must not exceed 365 days from creation.\n- Account numbers and BSBs must be masked in log events.\n- Revocation endpoints must be idempotent.\n- All expiry dates must use ISO 8601 with explicit Australian timezone offsets (+10:00 / +11:00).\n\n## Candidate Workspace Instructions\n1. Review the brief and technical constraints above.\n2. Write your implementation files in `src/`.\n3. Validate boundary conditions and domain rules.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway</h1>\n      <p>\n        Review the brief in <code>README.md</code>, or message the AI assistant to start implementing your solution.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/cdr-types.ts ===\nexport type CdrScope = 'bank:accounts.basic:read' | 'bank:accounts.detail:read' | 'bank:transactions:read';\n\nexport interface ConsentRecord {\n  consentId: string;\n  customerId: string;\n  scopes: CdrScope[];\n  status: 'AUTHORISED' | 'REVOKED' | 'EXPIRED';\n  authorisedAtIso: string;\n  expiresAtIso: string;\n}\n\nexport interface CdrAccessRequest {\n  consentId: string;\n  requestedScope: CdrScope;\n  timestampIso: string;\n}\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\nmake no mistake, finish everything""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\""message\"":\""Implemented the in-memory CDR Consent Gateway demo in React. Assumed this should run entirely in the browser with local data/no backend, while exposing the gateway rules as reusable functions under `src/`. It now demonstrates active scope validation, instant idempotent withdrawal, expiry handling, simulated hourly revocation reconciliation, Australian timezone ISO formatting, and sanitized telemetry/error logs. Check the preview by running allowed/denied requests, withdrawing a consent, adding one to the revocation registry, and confirming logs mask BSB/account data.\"",\""files\"":[{\""path\"":\""src/cdrGateway.js\"",\""contents\"":\""export const CDR_SCOPES = [\\n  \\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"",\\n  \\\""bank:accounts.detail:read\\\"",\\n  \\\""bank:transactions:read\\\"",\\n];\\n\\nconst MAX_CONSENT_DAYS = 365;\\nconst DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\\nconst AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN = /T\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}(?:\\\\+10:00|\\\\+11:00)$/;\\n\\nfunction pad(value) {\\n  return String(value).padStart(2, \\\""0\\\"");\\n}\\n\\nfunction firstSundayOfMonth(year, monthIndex) {\\n  const firstDay = new Date(Date.UTC(year, monthIndex, 1)).getUTCDay();\\n  return 1 + ((7 - firstDay) % 7);\\n}\\n\\nexport function getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant = new Date()) {\\n  const utcMs = instant.getTime();\\n  const year = instant.getUTCFullYear();\\n\\n  const dstStartThisYear = Date.UTC(\\n    year,\\n    9,\\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 9),\\n    16,\\n    0,\\n    0,\\n  );\\n  const dstEndThisYear = Date.UTC(\\n    year,\\n    3,\\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 3),\\n    16,\\n    0,\\n    0,\\n  );\\n\\n  const isDaylightSaving = utcMs >= dstStartThisYear || utcMs < dstEndThisYear;\\n  return isDaylightSaving ? 11 * 60 : 10 * 60;\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatAustralianIso(instant = new Date()) {\\n  const offsetMinutes = getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant);\\n  const localTime = new Date(instant.getTime() + offsetMinutes * 60 * 1000);\\n  const offset = offsetMinutes === 660 ? \\\""+11:00\\\"" : \\\""+10:00\\\"";\\n\\n  return `${localTime.getUTCFullYear()}-${pad(localTime.getUTCMonth() + 1)}-${pad(\\n    localTime.getUTCDate(),\\n  )}T${pad(localTime.getUTCHours())}:${pad(localTime.getUTCMinutes())}:${pad(\\n    localTime.getUTCSeconds(),\\n  )}${offset}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function parseAustralianIso(isoValue) {\\n  if (!AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN.test(isoValue)) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      \\\""Timestamp must be ISO 8601 with an explicit Australian offset (+10:00 or +11:00).\\\"",\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  const parsed = new Date(isoValue);\\n  if (Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime())) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\""Timestamp is not a valid ISO 8601 value.\\\"");\\n  }\\n  return parsed;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskBsb(value) {\\n  const digits = String(value ?? \\\""\\\"").replace(/\\\\D/g, \\\""\\\"");\\n  if (digits.length !== 6) return \\\""***-***\\\"";\\n  return `${digits.slice(0, 3)}-***`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskAccountNumber(value) {\\n  const digits = String(value ?? \\\""\\\"").replace(/\\\\D/g, \\\""\\\"");\\n  if (digits.length < 4) return \\\""... ****\\\"";\\n  return `... ${digits.slice(-4)}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskSensitiveIdentifiers(value) {\\n  if (typeof value !== \\\""string\\\"") return value;\\n\\n  return value\\n    .replace(/\\\\b(\\\\d{3})[-\\\\s]?(\\\\d{3})\\\\b/g, \\\""$1-***\\\"")\\n    .replace(\\n      /\\\\b(account(?:\\\\s+number)?|acct)\\\\s*[:#-]?\\\\s*(\\\\d{4,12})\\\\b/gi,\\n      (_match, label, accountNumber) => `${label}: ${maskAccountNumber(accountNumber)}`,\\n    );\\n}\\n\\nexport function sanitizeTelemetry(input) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(input)) {\\n    return input.map((entry) => sanitizeTelemetry(entry));\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input && typeof input === \\\""object\\\"") {\\n    return Object.fromEntries(\\n      Object.entries(input).map(([key, value]) => {\\n        const lowerKey = key.toLowerCase();\\n        if (lowerKey === \\\""bsb\\\"") return [key, maskBsb(value)];\\n        if (lowerKey === \\\""accountnumber\\\"" || lowerKey === \\\""account\\\"") {\\n          return [key, maskAccountNumber(value)];\\n        }\\n        return [key, sanitizeTelemetry(value)];\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return maskSensitiveIdentifiers(input);\\n}\\n\\nfunction createTelemetryEvent(level, code, message, details = {}) {\\n  return sanitizeTelemetry({\\n    level,\\n    code,\\n    message,\\n    details,\\n    observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction assertScope(scope) {\\n  if (!CDR_SCOPES.includes(scope)) {\\n    throw new Error(`Unsupported CDR scope: ${scope}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction normaliseScopes(scopes) {\\n  const unique = [...new Set(scopes)];\\n  unique.forEach(assertScope);\\n  return unique;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createConsent({\\n  consentId,\\n  customerId,\\n  scopes,\\n  durationDays,\\n  accounts = [],\\n  now = new Date(),\\n}) {\\n  if (!customerId) throw new Error(\\\""customerId is required.\\\"");\\n  if (!Number.isInteger(durationDays) || durationDays < 1) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\""Consent duration must be a positive whole number of days.\\\"");\\n  }\\n  if (durationDays > MAX_CONSENT_DAYS) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\""Consent duration must not exceed 365 days from creation.\\\"");\\n  }\\n\\n  const authorisedAt = new Date(now);\\n  const expiresAt = new Date(authorisedAt.getTime() + durationDays * DAY_MS);\\n\\n  return {\\n    consentId: consentId || `cdr-${crypto.randomUUID?.() || Date.now()}`,\\n    customerId,\\n    scopes: normaliseScopes(scopes),\\n    status: \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"",\\n    authorisedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(authorisedAt),\\n    expiresAtIso: formatAustralianIso(expiresAt),\\n    accounts,\\n    revokedAtIso: null,\\n    revocationReason: null,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function isConsentExpired(consent, atIso = formatAustralianIso(new Date())) {\\n  const at = parseAustralianIso(atIso);\\n  const expiry = parseAustralianIso(consent.expiresAtIso);\\n  return at.getTime() >= expiry.getTime();\\n}\\n\\nfunction markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso) {\\n  if (consent.status !== \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"") return consent;\\n  if (!isConsentExpired(consent, atIso)) return consent;\\n\\n  return {\\n    ...consent,\\n    status: \\\""EXPIRED\\\"",\\n    revocationReason: \\\""Consent expired by statutory time limit.\\\"",\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function authorizeAccess(consents, request) {\\n  const timestampIso = request.timestampIso || formatAustralianIso(new Date());\\n  parseAustralianIso(timestampIso);\\n  assertScope(request.requestedScope);\\n\\n  let inspectedConsent = null;\\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\\n    if (consent.consentId !== request.consentId) return consent;\\n    inspectedConsent = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, timestampIso);\\n    return inspectedConsent;\\n  });\\n\\n  if (!inspectedConsent) {\\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""error\\\"", \\\""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\\\"", \\\""Consent was not found.\\\"", {\\n      consentId: request.consentId,\\n      diagnosticContext: request.diagnosticContext,\\n    });\\n    return {\\n      consents: nextConsents,\\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 404, error: event },\\n      event,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (inspectedConsent.status !== \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"") {\\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\n      \\\""error\\\"",\\n      `CONSENT_${inspectedConsent.status}`,\\n      \\\""Consent is not active; access rejected.\\\"",\\n      {\\n        consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n        status: inspectedConsent.status,\\n        bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\\n        accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\\n      },\\n    );\\n    return {\\n      consents: nextConsents,\\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\\n      event,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!inspectedConsent.scopes.includes(request.requestedScope)) {\\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""error\\\"", \\\""SCOPE_NOT_CONSENTED\\\"", \\\""Requested scope is not consented.\\\"", {\\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n      requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\\n      consentedScopes: inspectedConsent.scopes,\\n      bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\\n      accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\\n    });\\n    return {\\n      consents: nextConsents,\\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\\n      event,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""info\\\"", \\\""ACCESS_GRANTED\\\"", \\\""CDR access granted for active consented scope.\\\"", {\\n    consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n    requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\\n    accountCount: inspectedConsent.accounts?.length || 0,\\n  });\\n\\n  return {\\n    consents: nextConsents,\\n    result: {\\n      granted: true,\\n      statusCode: 200,\\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\\n      scope: request.requestedScope,\\n    },\\n    event,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function revokeConsent(consents, consentId, reason = \\\""Customer withdrawal\\\"", at = new Date()) {\\n  const revokedAtIso = formatAustralianIso(at);\\n  let found = false;\\n  let wasAlreadyRevoked = false;\\n\\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\\n    if (consent.consentId !== consentId) return consent;\\n    found = true;\\n    if (consent.status === \\\""REVOKED\\\"") {\\n      wasAlreadyRevoked = true;\\n      return consent;\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      ...consent,\\n      status: \\\""REVOKED\\\"",\\n      revokedAtIso,\\n      revocationReason: reason,\\n    };\\n  });\\n\\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\n    found ? \\\""info\\\"" : \\\""warn\\\"",\\n    found ? (wasAlreadyRevoked ? \\\""CONSENT_REVOKE_IDEMPOTENT\\\"" : \\\""CONSENT_REVOKED\\\"") : \\\""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\\\"",\\n    found ? \\\""Revocation request processed idempotently.\\\"" : \\\""Revocation target was not found.\\\"",\\n    { consentId, reason },\\n  );\\n\\n  return { consents: nextConsents, found, wasAlreadyRevoked, event };\\n}\\n\\nexport function reconcileRevocations(consents, revocationRegistry, now = new Date()) {\\n  const atIso = formatAustralianIso(now);\\n  const revokedIds = new Set(revocationRegistry);\\n  const changedConsentIds = [];\\n\\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\\n    const expiredChecked = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso);\\n    if (expiredChecked !== consent) changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\\n\\n    if (revokedIds.has(consent.consentId) && expiredChecked.status !== \\\""REVOKED\\\"") {\\n      changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\\n      return {\\n        ...expiredChecked,\\n        status: \\\""REVOKED\\\"",\\n        revokedAtIso: atIso,\\n        revocationReason: \\\""Matched external revocation registry.\\\"",\\n      };\\n    }\\n    return expiredChecked;\\n  });\\n\\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\\\""info\\\"", \\\""HOURLY_RECONCILIATION\\\"", \\\""Revocation reconciliation completed.\\\"", {\\n    checkedConsentCount: consents.length,\\n    registryCount: revokedIds.size,\\n    changedConsentIds: [...new Set(changedConsentIds)],\\n  });\\n\\n  return { consents: nextConsents, event };\\n}\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/App.jsx\"",\""contents\"":\""import { useEffect, useMemo, useState } from \\\""react\\\"";\\nimport {\\n  CDR_SCOPES,\\n  authorizeAccess,\\n  createConsent,\\n  formatAustralianIso,\\n  maskAccountNumber,\\n  maskBsb,\\n  reconcileRevocations,\\n  revokeConsent,\\n} from \\\""./cdrGateway.js\\\"";\\n\\nfunction daysAgo(days) {\\n  return new Date(Date.now() - days * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\\n}\\n\\nfunction buildInitialState() {\\n  const active = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-active-001\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-9271\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"", \\\""bank:transactions:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 180,\\n    now: daysAgo(2),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Everyday Offset\\\"", bsb: \\\""083-001\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""123456789\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const limited = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-basic-only-002\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-4418\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 90,\\n    now: daysAgo(1),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Savings\\\"", bsb: \\\""062-111\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""7788990011\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const expired = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-expired-003\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-7130\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"", \\\""bank:accounts.detail:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 1,\\n    now: daysAgo(4),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Closed Loan\\\"", bsb: \\\""182-222\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""4567891234\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const withdrawn = createConsent({\\n    consentId: \\\""consent-withdrawn-004\\\"",\\n    customerId: \\\""customer-6580\\\"",\\n    scopes: [\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"", \\\""bank:transactions:read\\\""],\\n    durationDays: 365,\\n    now: daysAgo(3),\\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \\\""Transaction Account\\\"", bsb: \\\""032-999\\\"", accountNumber: \\\""987654321\\\"" }],\\n  });\\n\\n  const revoked = revokeConsent(\\n    [withdrawn],\\n    withdrawn.consentId,\\n    \\\""Customer withdrew consent for account 987654321\\\"",\\n    daysAgo(1),\\n  ).consents[0];\\n\\n  return {\\n    consents: [active, limited, expired, revoked],\\n    registry: [revoked.consentId],\\n    logs: [\\n      {\\n        level: \\\""info\\\"",\\n        code: \\\""GATEWAY_READY\\\"",\\n        message: \\\""In-memory CDR Consent Gateway loaded with sample consents.\\\"",\\n        observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n        details: { statutoryMaxDurationDays: 365, timezone: \\\""Australia/Sydney\\\"" },\\n      },\\n    ],\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction statusLabel(status) {\\n  if (status === \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"") return \\\""Authorised\\\"";\\n  if (status === \\\""REVOKED\\\"") return \\\""Revoked\\\"";\\n  return \\\""Expired\\\"";\\n}\\n\\nfunction LogEntry({ entry }) {\\n  return (\\n    <article className={`log-entry log-${entry.level}`}>\\n      <div className=\\\""log-entry__header\\\"">\\n        <strong>{entry.code}</strong>\\n        <span>{entry.observedAtIso}</span>\\n      </div>\\n      <p>{entry.message}</p>\\n      {entry.details ? <pre>{JSON.stringify(entry.details, null, 2)}</pre> : null}\\n    </article>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nfunction ConsentCard({ consent, isSelected, onSelect }) {\\n  const primaryAccount = consent.accounts?.[0];\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button\\n      type=\\\""button\\\""\\n      className={`consent-card ${isSelected ? \\\""consent-card--selected\\\"" : \\\""\\\""}`}\\n      onClick={() => onSelect(consent.consentId)}\\n    >\\n      <span className={`status status--${consent.status.toLowerCase()}`}>{statusLabel(consent.status)}</span>\\n      <strong>{consent.consentId}</strong>\\n      <small>{consent.customerId}</small>\\n      <div className=\\\""account-line\\\"">\\n        {primaryAccount ? `${maskBsb(primaryAccount.bsb)} ${maskAccountNumber(primaryAccount.accountNumber)}` : \\\""No account\\\""}\\n      </div>\\n      <div className=\\\""date-grid\\\"">\\n        <span>Authorised</span>\\n        <time>{consent.authorisedAtIso}</time>\\n        <span>Expires</span>\\n        <time>{consent.expiresAtIso}</time>\\n      </div>\\n      <ul>\\n        {consent.scopes.map((scope) => (\\n          <li key={scope}>{scope}</li>\\n        ))}\\n      </ul>\\n    </button>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const initial = useMemo(buildInitialState, []);\\n  const [consents, setConsents] = useState(initial.consents);\\n  const [revocationRegistry, setRevocationRegistry] = useState(initial.registry);\\n  const [logs, setLogs] = useState(initial.logs);\\n  const [selectedConsentId, setSelectedConsentId] = useState(initial.consents[0].consentId);\\n  const [requestedScope, setRequestedScope] = useState(\\\""bank:accounts.basic:read\\\"");\\n  const [lastResult, setLastResult] = useState(null);\\n\\n  const selectedConsent = consents.find((consent) => consent.consentId === selectedConsentId);\\n\\n  function prependLog(event) {\\n    setLogs((current) => [event, ...current].slice(0, 12));\\n  }\\n\\n  function runAccessRequest() {\\n    const { consents: nextConsents, result, event } = authorizeAccess(consents, {\\n      consentId: selectedConsentId,\\n      requestedScope,\\n      timestampIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n      diagnosticContext: \\\""Standard trace for BSB 083-001 account 123456789\\\"",\\n    });\\n\\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\\n    setLastResult(result);\\n    prependLog(event);\\n  }\\n\\n  function withdrawSelectedConsent() {\\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = revokeConsent(\\n      consents,\\n      selectedConsentId,\\n      \\\""Customer withdrawal received for account 123456789\\\"",\\n    );\\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\\n    setLastResult(null);\\n    prependLog(event);\\n  }\\n\\n  function addSelectedToRegistry() {\\n    setRevocationRegistry((current) =>\\n      current.includes(selectedConsentId) ? current : [...current, selectedConsentId],\\n    );\\n    prependLog({\\n      level: \\\""info\\\"",\\n      code: \\\""REGISTRY_UPDATED\\\"",\\n      message: \\\""Consent added to simulated external revocation registry.\\\"",\\n      observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\\n      details: { consentId: selectedConsentId },\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  function runReconciliation() {\\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\\n      consents,\\n      revocationRegistry,\\n      new Date(),\\n    );\\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\\n    setLastResult(null);\\n    prependLog(event);\\n  }\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const hourlyReconciliation = window.setInterval(() => {\\n      setConsents((currentConsents) => {\\n        const { consents: reconciledConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\\n          currentConsents,\\n          revocationRegistry,\\n          new Date(),\\n        );\\n        setLogs((currentLogs) => [event, ...currentLogs].slice(0, 12));\\n        return reconciledConsents;\\n      });\\n    }, 60 * 60 * 1000);\\n\\n    return () => window.clearInterval(hourlyReconciliation);\\n  }, [revocationRegistry]);\\n\\n  const activeCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \\\""AUTHORISED\\\"").length;\\n  const revokedCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \\\""REVOKED\\\"").length;\\n  const expiredCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \\\""EXPIRED\\\"").length;\\n\\n  return (\\n    <main className=\\\""shell\\\"">\\n      <section className=\\\""hero\\\"">\\n        <div>\\n          <p className=\\\""eyebrow\\\"">Consumer Data Right</p>\\n          <h1>CDR Consent &amp; Scoping Gateway</h1>\\n          <p>\\n            Validates consented scopes, rejects withdrawn or expired arrangements, reconciles revocation\\n            registries, and masks Australian banking identifiers in telemetry.\\n          </p>\\n        </div>\\n        <div className=\\\""clock-card\\\"">\\n          <span>Gateway time anchor</span>\\n          <strong>{formatAustralianIso(new Date())}</strong>\\n          <small>Generated with Australia/Sydney +10:00/+11:00 offsets, not browser-local formatting.</small>\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n\\n      <section className=\\\""metrics\\\"" aria-label=\\\""Consent status summary\\\"">\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>{activeCount}</strong>\\n          <span>Authorised</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>{revokedCount}</strong>\\n          <span>Revoked</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>{expiredCount}</strong>\\n          <span>Expired</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>365</strong>\\n          <span>Max days</span>\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n\\n      <div className=\\\""workspace\\\"">\\n        <section className=\\\""panel\\\"">\\n          <div className=\\\""panel-heading\\\"">\\n            <h2>Consent arrangements</h2>\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" onClick={runReconciliation}>Run reconciliation</button>\\n          </div>\\n          <div className=\\\""consent-list\\\"">\\n            {consents.map((consent) => (\\n              <ConsentCard\\n                key={consent.consentId}\\n                consent={consent}\\n                isSelected={consent.consentId === selectedConsentId}\\n                onSelect={setSelectedConsentId}\\n              />\\n            ))}\\n          </div>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section className=\\\""panel control-panel\\\"">\\n          <h2>Access request simulator</h2>\\n          <label>\\n            Consent ID\\n            <select value={selectedConsentId} onChange={(event) => setSelectedConsentId(event.target.value)}>\\n              {consents.map((consent) => (\\n                <option key={consent.consentId} value={consent.consentId}>\\n                  {consent.consentId}\\n                </option>\\n              ))}\\n            </select>\\n          </label>\\n          <label>\\n            Requested CDR scope\\n            <select value={requestedScope} onChange={(event) => setRequestedScope(event.target.value)}>\\n              {CDR_SCOPES.map((scope) => (\\n                <option key={scope} value={scope}>{scope}</option>\\n              ))}\\n            </select>\\n          </label>\\n          <div className=\\\""button-row\\\"">\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" className=\\\""primary\\\"" onClick={runAccessRequest}>Authorize request</button>\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" onClick={withdrawSelectedConsent}>Withdraw consent</button>\\n            <button type=\\\""button\\\"" onClick={addSelectedToRegistry}>Add to registry</button>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {selectedConsent ? (\\n            <div className=\\\""selected-summary\\\"">\\n              <h3>Selected arrangement</h3>\\n              <p><strong>Status:</strong> {statusLabel(selectedConsent.status)}</p>\\n              <p><strong>Scopes:</strong> {selectedConsent.scopes.join(\\\"", \\\"")}</p>\\n              {selectedConsent.revocationReason ? (\\n                <p><strong>Revocation reason:</strong> {selectedConsent.revocationReason}</p>\\n              ) : null}\\n            </div>\\n          ) : null}\\n\\n          {lastResult ? (\\n            <div className={`result result--${lastResult.granted ? \\\""granted\\\"" : \\\""denied\\\""}`}>\\n              <strong>{lastResult.granted ? \\\""Access granted\\\"" : \\\""Access denied\\\""}</strong>\\n              <pre>{JSON.stringify(lastResult, null, 2)}</pre>\\n            </div>\\n          ) : null}\\n        </section>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      <section className=\\\""panel\\\"">\\n        <div className=\\\""panel-heading\\\"">\\n          <h2>Sanitized telemetry &amp; error trace</h2>\\n          <span className=\\\""registry-count\\\"">Registry entries: {revocationRegistry.length}</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div className=\\\""logs\\\"">\\n          {logs.map((entry, index) => (\\n            <LogEntry key={`${entry.code}-${entry.observedAtIso}-${index}`} entry={entry} />\\n          ))}\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n    </main>\\n  );\\n}\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/styles.css\"",\""contents\"":\"":root {\\n  font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\""Segoe UI\\\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\\n  color: #172033;\\n  background: #f5f7fb;\\n  font-synthesis: none;\\n  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;\\n}\\n\\n* {\\n  box-sizing: border-box;\\n}\\n\\nbody {\\n  margin: 0;\\n}\\n\\nbutton,\\nselect {\\n  font: inherit;\\n}\\n\\nbutton {\\n  cursor: pointer;\\n}\\n\\n.shell {\\n  width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px));\\n  margin: 0 auto;\\n  padding: 32px 0 48px;\\n}\\n\\n.hero {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 360px;\\n  gap: 24px;\\n  align-items: stretch;\\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.hero > div:first-child,\\n.clock-card,\\n.panel,\\n.metrics > div {\\n  background: #ffffff;\\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\\n  border-radius: 22px;\\n  box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);\\n}\\n\\n.hero > div:first-child {\\n  padding: 32px;\\n}\\n\\n.eyebrow {\\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\\n  color: #0f766e;\\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\\n  text-transform: uppercase;\\n}\\n\\nh1,\\nh2,\\nh3,\\np {\\n  margin-top: 0;\\n}\\n\\nh1 {\\n  max-width: 760px;\\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem);\\n  line-height: 1;\\n  letter-spacing: -0.05em;\\n}\\n\\n.hero p {\\n  max-width: 780px;\\n  margin-bottom: 0;\\n  color: #475569;\\n  line-height: 1.7;\\n}\\n\\n.clock-card {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n  justify-content: center;\\n  gap: 10px;\\n  padding: 28px;\\n  background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0f172a, #164e63);\\n  color: white;\\n}\\n\\n.clock-card span,\\n.clock-card small {\\n  color: #bae6fd;\\n}\\n\\n.clock-card strong {\\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\\n  word-break: break-word;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\\n  gap: 16px;\\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics > div {\\n  padding: 20px;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics strong {\\n  display: block;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-size: 2rem;\\n  line-height: 1;\\n}\\n\\n.metrics span {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n  font-weight: 700;\\n}\\n\\n.workspace {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(340px, 0.85fr);\\n  gap: 24px;\\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.panel {\\n  padding: 24px;\\n}\\n\\n.panel-heading {\\n  display: flex;\\n  gap: 16px;\\n  align-items: center;\\n  justify-content: space-between;\\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\\n}\\n\\n.panel h2 {\\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\\n}\\n\\n.panel-heading h2 {\\n  margin-bottom: 0;\\n}\\n\\n.panel-heading button,\\n.button-row button {\\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 10px 14px;\\n  background: white;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.button-row .primary {\\n  border-color: #0f766e;\\n  background: #0f766e;\\n  color: white;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-list {\\n  display: grid;\\n  gap: 14px;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card {\\n  width: 100%;\\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\\n  border-radius: 18px;\\n  padding: 16px;\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n  color: inherit;\\n  text-align: left;\\n  transition: border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card:hover,\\n.consent-card--selected {\\n  border-color: #0f766e;\\n  box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15, 118, 110, 0.12);\\n  transform: translateY(-1px);\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card strong,\\n.consent-card small,\\n.account-line {\\n  display: block;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card strong {\\n  margin-top: 10px;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card small,\\n.account-line,\\n.date-grid,\\n.consent-card li {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n}\\n\\n.account-line {\\n  margin-top: 6px;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.status {\\n  display: inline-flex;\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 5px 10px;\\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\\n  font-weight: 900;\\n  text-transform: uppercase;\\n}\\n\\n.status--authorised {\\n  background: #dcfce7;\\n  color: #166534;\\n}\\n\\n.status--revoked {\\n  background: #fee2e2;\\n  color: #991b1b;\\n}\\n\\n.status--expired {\\n  background: #fef3c7;\\n  color: #92400e;\\n}\\n\\n.date-grid {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: 86px minmax(0, 1fr);\\n  gap: 4px 10px;\\n  margin-top: 12px;\\n  font-size: 0.86rem;\\n}\\n\\n.date-grid span {\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.date-grid time {\\n  word-break: break-word;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card ul {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n  gap: 8px;\\n  padding: 0;\\n  margin: 12px 0 0;\\n  list-style: none;\\n}\\n\\n.consent-card li {\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 5px 8px;\\n  background: #e0f2fe;\\n  color: #075985;\\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.control-panel label {\\n  display: grid;\\n  gap: 8px;\\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\\n  color: #334155;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\nselect {\\n  width: 100%;\\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\\n  border-radius: 12px;\\n  padding: 11px 12px;\\n  background: white;\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n}\\n\\n.button-row {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n  gap: 10px;\\n  margin: 18px 0;\\n}\\n\\n.selected-summary,\\n.result {\\n  border-radius: 16px;\\n  padding: 16px;\\n  margin-top: 16px;\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n}\\n\\n.selected-summary h3 {\\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\\n}\\n\\n.selected-summary p {\\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\\n  color: #475569;\\n  line-height: 1.5;\\n}\\n\\n.result {\\n  border: 1px solid;\\n}\\n\\n.result--granted {\\n  border-color: #86efac;\\n  background: #f0fdf4;\\n}\\n\\n.result--denied {\\n  border-color: #fecaca;\\n  background: #fef2f2;\\n}\\n\\npre {\\n  overflow: auto;\\n  margin: 10px 0 0;\\n  border-radius: 12px;\\n  padding: 12px;\\n  background: #0f172a;\\n  color: #dbeafe;\\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\\n  line-height: 1.5;\\n}\\n\\n.registry-count {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n  font-weight: 800;\\n}\\n\\n.logs {\\n  display: grid;\\n  gap: 12px;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry {\\n  border-left: 5px solid #38bdf8;\\n  border-radius: 14px;\\n  padding: 14px;\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n}\\n\\n.log-error {\\n  border-left-color: #ef4444;\\n}\\n\\n.log-warn {\\n  border-left-color: #f59e0b;\\n}\\n\\n.log-info {\\n  border-left-color: #0f766e;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry__header {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n  gap: 8px 16px;\\n  justify-content: space-between;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry__header strong {\\n  color: #0f172a;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry__header span,\\n.log-entry p {\\n  color: #64748b;\\n}\\n\\n.log-entry p {\\n  margin: 8px 0 0;\\n}\\n\\n@media (max-width: 920px) {\\n  .hero,\\n  .workspace,\\n  .metrics {\\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\\n  }\\n}\\n\""}],\""reasoning\"":\""The request was broad, so I implemented the full browser-based gateway demonstration expected by the brief rather than asking for narrower scope. Key choices: keep state in memory, make domain logic reusable in `cdrGateway.js`, generate Australian-offset ISO strings without browser-local formatting, enforce the 365-day duration cap in creation, sanitize all returned telemetry, and provide UI controls to demonstrate grant/deny/revoke/reconcile paths.\""}"",""refusal"":null,""annotations"":[],""parsed"":{""message"":""Implemented the in-memory CDR Consent Gateway demo in React. Assumed this should run entirely in the browser with local data/no backend, while exposing the gateway rules as reusable functions under `src/`. It now demonstrates active scope validation, instant idempotent withdrawal, expiry handling, simulated hourly revocation reconciliation, Australian timezone ISO formatting, and sanitized telemetry/error logs. Check the preview by running allowed/denied requests, withdrawing a consent, adding one to the revocation registry, and confirming logs mask BSB/account data."",""files"":[{""path"":""src/cdrGateway.js"",""contents"":""export const CDR_SCOPES = [\n  \""bank:accounts.basic:read\"",\n  \""bank:accounts.detail:read\"",\n  \""bank:transactions:read\"",\n];\n\nconst MAX_CONSENT_DAYS = 365;\nconst DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\nconst AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN = /T\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}(?:\\+10:00|\\+11:00)$/;\n\nfunction pad(value) {\n  return String(value).padStart(2, \""0\"");\n}\n\nfunction firstSundayOfMonth(year, monthIndex) {\n  const firstDay = new Date(Date.UTC(year, monthIndex, 1)).getUTCDay();\n  return 1 + ((7 - firstDay) % 7);\n}\n\nexport function getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant = new Date()) {\n  const utcMs = instant.getTime();\n  const year = instant.getUTCFullYear();\n\n  const dstStartThisYear = Date.UTC(\n    year,\n    9,\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 9),\n    16,\n    0,\n    0,\n  );\n  const dstEndThisYear = Date.UTC(\n    year,\n    3,\n    firstSundayOfMonth(year, 3),\n    16,\n    0,\n    0,\n  );\n\n  const isDaylightSaving = utcMs >= dstStartThisYear || utcMs < dstEndThisYear;\n  return isDaylightSaving ? 11 * 60 : 10 * 60;\n}\n\nexport function formatAustralianIso(instant = new Date()) {\n  const offsetMinutes = getSydneyOffsetMinutes(instant);\n  const localTime = new Date(instant.getTime() + offsetMinutes * 60 * 1000);\n  const offset = offsetMinutes === 660 ? \""+11:00\"" : \""+10:00\"";\n\n  return `${localTime.getUTCFullYear()}-${pad(localTime.getUTCMonth() + 1)}-${pad(\n    localTime.getUTCDate(),\n  )}T${pad(localTime.getUTCHours())}:${pad(localTime.getUTCMinutes())}:${pad(\n    localTime.getUTCSeconds(),\n  )}${offset}`;\n}\n\nexport function parseAustralianIso(isoValue) {\n  if (!AUSTRALIAN_OFFSET_PATTERN.test(isoValue)) {\n    throw new Error(\n      \""Timestamp must be ISO 8601 with an explicit Australian offset (+10:00 or +11:00).\"",\n    );\n  }\n\n  const parsed = new Date(isoValue);\n  if (Number.isNaN(parsed.getTime())) {\n    throw new Error(\""Timestamp is not a valid ISO 8601 value.\"");\n  }\n  return parsed;\n}\n\nexport function maskBsb(value) {\n  const digits = String(value ?? \""\"").replace(/\\D/g, \""\"");\n  if (digits.length !== 6) return \""***-***\"";\n  return `${digits.slice(0, 3)}-***`;\n}\n\nexport function maskAccountNumber(value) {\n  const digits = String(value ?? \""\"").replace(/\\D/g, \""\"");\n  if (digits.length < 4) return \""... ****\"";\n  return `... ${digits.slice(-4)}`;\n}\n\nexport function maskSensitiveIdentifiers(value) {\n  if (typeof value !== \""string\"") return value;\n\n  return value\n    .replace(/\\b(\\d{3})[-\\s]?(\\d{3})\\b/g, \""$1-***\"")\n    .replace(\n      /\\b(account(?:\\s+number)?|acct)\\s*[:#-]?\\s*(\\d{4,12})\\b/gi,\n      (_match, label, accountNumber) => `${label}: ${maskAccountNumber(accountNumber)}`,\n    );\n}\n\nexport function sanitizeTelemetry(input) {\n  if (Array.isArray(input)) {\n    return input.map((entry) => sanitizeTelemetry(entry));\n  }\n\n  if (input && typeof input === \""object\"") {\n    return Object.fromEntries(\n      Object.entries(input).map(([key, value]) => {\n        const lowerKey = key.toLowerCase();\n        if (lowerKey === \""bsb\"") return [key, maskBsb(value)];\n        if (lowerKey === \""accountnumber\"" || lowerKey === \""account\"") {\n          return [key, maskAccountNumber(value)];\n        }\n        return [key, sanitizeTelemetry(value)];\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  return maskSensitiveIdentifiers(input);\n}\n\nfunction createTelemetryEvent(level, code, message, details = {}) {\n  return sanitizeTelemetry({\n    level,\n    code,\n    message,\n    details,\n    observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n  });\n}\n\nfunction assertScope(scope) {\n  if (!CDR_SCOPES.includes(scope)) {\n    throw new Error(`Unsupported CDR scope: ${scope}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction normaliseScopes(scopes) {\n  const unique = [...new Set(scopes)];\n  unique.forEach(assertScope);\n  return unique;\n}\n\nexport function createConsent({\n  consentId,\n  customerId,\n  scopes,\n  durationDays,\n  accounts = [],\n  now = new Date(),\n}) {\n  if (!customerId) throw new Error(\""customerId is required.\"");\n  if (!Number.isInteger(durationDays) || durationDays < 1) {\n    throw new Error(\""Consent duration must be a positive whole number of days.\"");\n  }\n  if (durationDays > MAX_CONSENT_DAYS) {\n    throw new Error(\""Consent duration must not exceed 365 days from creation.\"");\n  }\n\n  const authorisedAt = new Date(now);\n  const expiresAt = new Date(authorisedAt.getTime() + durationDays * DAY_MS);\n\n  return {\n    consentId: consentId || `cdr-${crypto.randomUUID?.() || Date.now()}`,\n    customerId,\n    scopes: normaliseScopes(scopes),\n    status: \""AUTHORISED\"",\n    authorisedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(authorisedAt),\n    expiresAtIso: formatAustralianIso(expiresAt),\n    accounts,\n    revokedAtIso: null,\n    revocationReason: null,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function isConsentExpired(consent, atIso = formatAustralianIso(new Date())) {\n  const at = parseAustralianIso(atIso);\n  const expiry = parseAustralianIso(consent.expiresAtIso);\n  return at.getTime() >= expiry.getTime();\n}\n\nfunction markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso) {\n  if (consent.status !== \""AUTHORISED\"") return consent;\n  if (!isConsentExpired(consent, atIso)) return consent;\n\n  return {\n    ...consent,\n    status: \""EXPIRED\"",\n    revocationReason: \""Consent expired by statutory time limit.\"",\n  };\n}\n\nexport function authorizeAccess(consents, request) {\n  const timestampIso = request.timestampIso || formatAustralianIso(new Date());\n  parseAustralianIso(timestampIso);\n  assertScope(request.requestedScope);\n\n  let inspectedConsent = null;\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\n    if (consent.consentId !== request.consentId) return consent;\n    inspectedConsent = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, timestampIso);\n    return inspectedConsent;\n  });\n\n  if (!inspectedConsent) {\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""error\"", \""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\"", \""Consent was not found.\"", {\n      consentId: request.consentId,\n      diagnosticContext: request.diagnosticContext,\n    });\n    return {\n      consents: nextConsents,\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 404, error: event },\n      event,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (inspectedConsent.status !== \""AUTHORISED\"") {\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\n      \""error\"",\n      `CONSENT_${inspectedConsent.status}`,\n      \""Consent is not active; access rejected.\"",\n      {\n        consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n        status: inspectedConsent.status,\n        bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\n        accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\n      },\n    );\n    return {\n      consents: nextConsents,\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\n      event,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!inspectedConsent.scopes.includes(request.requestedScope)) {\n    const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""error\"", \""SCOPE_NOT_CONSENTED\"", \""Requested scope is not consented.\"", {\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n      requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\n      consentedScopes: inspectedConsent.scopes,\n      bsb: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.bsb,\n      accountNumber: inspectedConsent.accounts?.[0]?.accountNumber,\n    });\n    return {\n      consents: nextConsents,\n      result: { granted: false, statusCode: 403, error: event },\n      event,\n    };\n  }\n\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""info\"", \""ACCESS_GRANTED\"", \""CDR access granted for active consented scope.\"", {\n    consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n    requestedScope: request.requestedScope,\n    accountCount: inspectedConsent.accounts?.length || 0,\n  });\n\n  return {\n    consents: nextConsents,\n    result: {\n      granted: true,\n      statusCode: 200,\n      consentId: inspectedConsent.consentId,\n      scope: request.requestedScope,\n    },\n    event,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function revokeConsent(consents, consentId, reason = \""Customer withdrawal\"", at = new Date()) {\n  const revokedAtIso = formatAustralianIso(at);\n  let found = false;\n  let wasAlreadyRevoked = false;\n\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\n    if (consent.consentId !== consentId) return consent;\n    found = true;\n    if (consent.status === \""REVOKED\"") {\n      wasAlreadyRevoked = true;\n      return consent;\n    }\n    return {\n      ...consent,\n      status: \""REVOKED\"",\n      revokedAtIso,\n      revocationReason: reason,\n    };\n  });\n\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\n    found ? \""info\"" : \""warn\"",\n    found ? (wasAlreadyRevoked ? \""CONSENT_REVOKE_IDEMPOTENT\"" : \""CONSENT_REVOKED\"") : \""CONSENT_NOT_FOUND\"",\n    found ? \""Revocation request processed idempotently.\"" : \""Revocation target was not found.\"",\n    { consentId, reason },\n  );\n\n  return { consents: nextConsents, found, wasAlreadyRevoked, event };\n}\n\nexport function reconcileRevocations(consents, revocationRegistry, now = new Date()) {\n  const atIso = formatAustralianIso(now);\n  const revokedIds = new Set(revocationRegistry);\n  const changedConsentIds = [];\n\n  const nextConsents = consents.map((consent) => {\n    const expiredChecked = markExpiredIfNeeded(consent, atIso);\n    if (expiredChecked !== consent) changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\n\n    if (revokedIds.has(consent.consentId) && expiredChecked.status !== \""REVOKED\"") {\n      changedConsentIds.push(consent.consentId);\n      return {\n        ...expiredChecked,\n        status: \""REVOKED\"",\n        revokedAtIso: atIso,\n        revocationReason: \""Matched external revocation registry.\"",\n      };\n    }\n    return expiredChecked;\n  });\n\n  const event = createTelemetryEvent(\""info\"", \""HOURLY_RECONCILIATION\"", \""Revocation reconciliation completed.\"", {\n    checkedConsentCount: consents.length,\n    registryCount: revokedIds.size,\n    changedConsentIds: [...new Set(changedConsentIds)],\n  });\n\n  return { consents: nextConsents, event };\n}\n""},{""path"":""src/App.jsx"",""contents"":""import { useEffect, useMemo, useState } from \""react\"";\nimport {\n  CDR_SCOPES,\n  authorizeAccess,\n  createConsent,\n  formatAustralianIso,\n  maskAccountNumber,\n  maskBsb,\n  reconcileRevocations,\n  revokeConsent,\n} from \""./cdrGateway.js\"";\n\nfunction daysAgo(days) {\n  return new Date(Date.now() - days * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\n}\n\nfunction buildInitialState() {\n  const active = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-active-001\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-9271\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"", \""bank:transactions:read\""],\n    durationDays: 180,\n    now: daysAgo(2),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Everyday Offset\"", bsb: \""083-001\"", accountNumber: \""123456789\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const limited = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-basic-only-002\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-4418\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\""],\n    durationDays: 90,\n    now: daysAgo(1),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Savings\"", bsb: \""062-111\"", accountNumber: \""7788990011\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const expired = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-expired-003\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-7130\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"", \""bank:accounts.detail:read\""],\n    durationDays: 1,\n    now: daysAgo(4),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Closed Loan\"", bsb: \""182-222\"", accountNumber: \""4567891234\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const withdrawn = createConsent({\n    consentId: \""consent-withdrawn-004\"",\n    customerId: \""customer-6580\"",\n    scopes: [\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"", \""bank:transactions:read\""],\n    durationDays: 365,\n    now: daysAgo(3),\n    accounts: [{ accountName: \""Transaction Account\"", bsb: \""032-999\"", accountNumber: \""987654321\"" }],\n  });\n\n  const revoked = revokeConsent(\n    [withdrawn],\n    withdrawn.consentId,\n    \""Customer withdrew consent for account 987654321\"",\n    daysAgo(1),\n  ).consents[0];\n\n  return {\n    consents: [active, limited, expired, revoked],\n    registry: [revoked.consentId],\n    logs: [\n      {\n        level: \""info\"",\n        code: \""GATEWAY_READY\"",\n        message: \""In-memory CDR Consent Gateway loaded with sample consents.\"",\n        observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n        details: { statutoryMaxDurationDays: 365, timezone: \""Australia/Sydney\"" },\n      },\n    ],\n  };\n}\n\nfunction statusLabel(status) {\n  if (status === \""AUTHORISED\"") return \""Authorised\"";\n  if (status === \""REVOKED\"") return \""Revoked\"";\n  return \""Expired\"";\n}\n\nfunction LogEntry({ entry }) {\n  return (\n    <article className={`log-entry log-${entry.level}`}>\n      <div className=\""log-entry__header\"">\n        <strong>{entry.code}</strong>\n        <span>{entry.observedAtIso}</span>\n      </div>\n      <p>{entry.message}</p>\n      {entry.details ? <pre>{JSON.stringify(entry.details, null, 2)}</pre> : null}\n    </article>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ConsentCard({ consent, isSelected, onSelect }) {\n  const primaryAccount = consent.accounts?.[0];\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\""button\""\n      className={`consent-card ${isSelected ? \""consent-card--selected\"" : \""\""}`}\n      onClick={() => onSelect(consent.consentId)}\n    >\n      <span className={`status status--${consent.status.toLowerCase()}`}>{statusLabel(consent.status)}</span>\n      <strong>{consent.consentId}</strong>\n      <small>{consent.customerId}</small>\n      <div className=\""account-line\"">\n        {primaryAccount ? `${maskBsb(primaryAccount.bsb)} ${maskAccountNumber(primaryAccount.accountNumber)}` : \""No account\""}\n      </div>\n      <div className=\""date-grid\"">\n        <span>Authorised</span>\n        <time>{consent.authorisedAtIso}</time>\n        <span>Expires</span>\n        <time>{consent.expiresAtIso}</time>\n      </div>\n      <ul>\n        {consent.scopes.map((scope) => (\n          <li key={scope}>{scope}</li>\n        ))}\n      </ul>\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const initial = useMemo(buildInitialState, []);\n  const [consents, setConsents] = useState(initial.consents);\n  const [revocationRegistry, setRevocationRegistry] = useState(initial.registry);\n  const [logs, setLogs] = useState(initial.logs);\n  const [selectedConsentId, setSelectedConsentId] = useState(initial.consents[0].consentId);\n  const [requestedScope, setRequestedScope] = useState(\""bank:accounts.basic:read\"");\n  const [lastResult, setLastResult] = useState(null);\n\n  const selectedConsent = consents.find((consent) => consent.consentId === selectedConsentId);\n\n  function prependLog(event) {\n    setLogs((current) => [event, ...current].slice(0, 12));\n  }\n\n  function runAccessRequest() {\n    const { consents: nextConsents, result, event } = authorizeAccess(consents, {\n      consentId: selectedConsentId,\n      requestedScope,\n      timestampIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n      diagnosticContext: \""Standard trace for BSB 083-001 account 123456789\"",\n    });\n\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\n    setLastResult(result);\n    prependLog(event);\n  }\n\n  function withdrawSelectedConsent() {\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = revokeConsent(\n      consents,\n      selectedConsentId,\n      \""Customer withdrawal received for account 123456789\"",\n    );\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\n    setLastResult(null);\n    prependLog(event);\n  }\n\n  function addSelectedToRegistry() {\n    setRevocationRegistry((current) =>\n      current.includes(selectedConsentId) ? current : [...current, selectedConsentId],\n    );\n    prependLog({\n      level: \""info\"",\n      code: \""REGISTRY_UPDATED\"",\n      message: \""Consent added to simulated external revocation registry.\"",\n      observedAtIso: formatAustralianIso(new Date()),\n      details: { consentId: selectedConsentId },\n    });\n  }\n\n  function runReconciliation() {\n    const { consents: nextConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\n      consents,\n      revocationRegistry,\n      new Date(),\n    );\n    setConsents(nextConsents);\n    setLastResult(null);\n    prependLog(event);\n  }\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const hourlyReconciliation = window.setInterval(() => {\n      setConsents((currentConsents) => {\n        const { consents: reconciledConsents, event } = reconcileRevocations(\n          currentConsents,\n          revocationRegistry,\n          new Date(),\n        );\n        setLogs((currentLogs) => [event, ...currentLogs].slice(0, 12));\n        return reconciledConsents;\n      });\n    }, 60 * 60 * 1000);\n\n    return () => window.clearInterval(hourlyReconciliation);\n  }, [revocationRegistry]);\n\n  const activeCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \""AUTHORISED\"").length;\n  const revokedCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \""REVOKED\"").length;\n  const expiredCount = consents.filter((consent) => consent.status === \""EXPIRED\"").length;\n\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <section className=\""hero\"">\n        <div>\n          <p className=\""eyebrow\"">Consumer Data Right</p>\n          <h1>CDR Consent &amp; Scoping Gateway</h1>\n          <p>\n            Validates consented scopes, rejects withdrawn or expired arrangements, reconciles revocation\n            registries, and masks Australian banking identifiers in telemetry.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\""clock-card\"">\n          <span>Gateway time anchor</span>\n          <strong>{formatAustralianIso(new Date())}</strong>\n          <small>Generated with Australia/Sydney +10:00/+11:00 offsets, not browser-local formatting.</small>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section className=\""metrics\"" aria-label=\""Consent status summary\"">\n        <div>\n          <strong>{activeCount}</strong>\n          <span>Authorised</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <strong>{revokedCount}</strong>\n          <span>Revoked</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <strong>{expiredCount}</strong>\n          <span>Expired</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <strong>365</strong>\n          <span>Max days</span>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <div className=\""workspace\"">\n        <section className=\""panel\"">\n          <div className=\""panel-heading\"">\n            <h2>Consent arrangements</h2>\n            <button type=\""button\"" onClick={runReconciliation}>Run reconciliation</button>\n          </div>\n          <div className=\""consent-list\"">\n            {consents.map((consent) => (\n              <ConsentCard\n                key={consent.consentId}\n                consent={consent}\n                isSelected={consent.consentId === selectedConsentId}\n                onSelect={setSelectedConsentId}\n              />\n            ))}\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section className=\""panel control-panel\"">\n          <h2>Access request simulator</h2>\n          <label>\n            Consent ID\n            <select value={selectedConsentId} onChange={(event) => setSelectedConsentId(event.target.value)}>\n              {consents.map((consent) => (\n                <option key={consent.consentId} value={consent.consentId}>\n                  {consent.consentId}\n                </option>\n              ))}\n            </select>\n          </label>\n          <label>\n            Requested CDR scope\n            <select value={requestedScope} onChange={(event) => setRequestedScope(event.target.value)}>\n              {CDR_SCOPES.map((scope) => (\n                <option key={scope} value={scope}>{scope}</option>\n              ))}\n            </select>\n          </label>\n          <div className=\""button-row\"">\n            <button type=\""button\"" className=\""primary\"" onClick={runAccessRequest}>Authorize request</button>\n            <button type=\""button\"" onClick={withdrawSelectedConsent}>Withdraw consent</button>\n            <button type=\""button\"" onClick={addSelectedToRegistry}>Add to registry</button>\n          </div>\n\n          {selectedConsent ? (\n            <div className=\""selected-summary\"">\n              <h3>Selected arrangement</h3>\n              <p><strong>Status:</strong> {statusLabel(selectedConsent.status)}</p>\n              <p><strong>Scopes:</strong> {selectedConsent.scopes.join(\"", \"")}</p>\n              {selectedConsent.revocationReason ? (\n                <p><strong>Revocation reason:</strong> {selectedConsent.revocationReason}</p>\n              ) : null}\n            </div>\n          ) : null}\n\n          {lastResult ? (\n            <div className={`result result--${lastResult.granted ? \""granted\"" : \""denied\""}`}>\n              <strong>{lastResult.granted ? \""Access granted\"" : \""Access denied\""}</strong>\n              <pre>{JSON.stringify(lastResult, null, 2)}</pre>\n            </div>\n          ) : null}\n        </section>\n      </div>\n\n      <section className=\""panel\"">\n        <div className=\""panel-heading\"">\n          <h2>Sanitized telemetry &amp; error trace</h2>\n          <span className=\""registry-count\"">Registry entries: {revocationRegistry.length}</span>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\""logs\"">\n          {logs.map((entry, index) => (\n            <LogEntry key={`${entry.code}-${entry.observedAtIso}-${index}`} entry={entry} />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n""},{""path"":""src/styles.css"",""contents"":"":root {\n  font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #172033;\n  background: #f5f7fb;\n  font-synthesis: none;\n  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\nbutton,\nselect {\n  font: inherit;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px));\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 32px 0 48px;\n}\n\n.hero {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 360px;\n  gap: 24px;\n  align-items: stretch;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.hero > div:first-child,\n.clock-card,\n.panel,\n.metrics > div {\n  background: #ffffff;\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\n  border-radius: 22px;\n  box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);\n}\n\n.hero > div:first-child {\n  padding: 32px;\n}\n\n.eyebrow {\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\n  color: #0f766e;\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\n  font-weight: 800;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\nh1,\nh2,\nh3,\np {\n  margin-top: 0;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  max-width: 760px;\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem);\n  line-height: 1;\n  letter-spacing: -0.05em;\n}\n\n.hero p {\n  max-width: 780px;\n  margin-bottom: 0;\n  color: #475569;\n  line-height: 1.7;\n}\n\n.clock-card {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 10px;\n  padding: 28px;\n  background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0f172a, #164e63);\n  color: white;\n}\n\n.clock-card span,\n.clock-card small {\n  color: #bae6fd;\n}\n\n.clock-card strong {\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n\n.metrics {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\n  gap: 16px;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.metrics > div {\n  padding: 20px;\n}\n\n.metrics strong {\n  display: block;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-size: 2rem;\n  line-height: 1;\n}\n\n.metrics span {\n  color: #64748b;\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.workspace {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(340px, 0.85fr);\n  gap: 24px;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.panel {\n  padding: 24px;\n}\n\n.panel-heading {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 16px;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n.panel h2 {\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\n}\n\n.panel-heading h2 {\n  margin-bottom: 0;\n}\n\n.panel-heading button,\n.button-row button {\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  background: white;\n  color: #0f172a;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.button-row .primary {\n  border-color: #0f766e;\n  background: #0f766e;\n  color: white;\n}\n\n.consent-list {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 14px;\n}\n\n.consent-card {\n  width: 100%;\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\n  border-radius: 18px;\n  padding: 16px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n  color: inherit;\n  text-align: left;\n  transition: border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;\n}\n\n.consent-card:hover,\n.consent-card--selected {\n  border-color: #0f766e;\n  box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15, 118, 110, 0.12);\n  transform: translateY(-1px);\n}\n\n.consent-card strong,\n.consent-card small,\n.account-line {\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.consent-card strong {\n  margin-top: 10px;\n  color: #0f172a;\n}\n\n.consent-card small,\n.account-line,\n.date-grid,\n.consent-card li {\n  color: #64748b;\n}\n\n.account-line {\n  margin-top: 6px;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.status {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 5px 10px;\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\n  font-weight: 900;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\n.status--authorised {\n  background: #dcfce7;\n  color: #166534;\n}\n\n.status--revoked {\n  background: #fee2e2;\n  color: #991b1b;\n}\n\n.status--expired {\n  background: #fef3c7;\n  color: #92400e;\n}\n\n.date-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 86px minmax(0, 1fr);\n  gap: 4px 10px;\n  margin-top: 12px;\n  font-size: 0.86rem;\n}\n\n.date-grid span {\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.date-grid time {\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n\n.consent-card ul {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 8px;\n  padding: 0;\n  margin: 12px 0 0;\n  list-style: none;\n}\n\n.consent-card li {\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 5px 8px;\n  background: #e0f2fe;\n  color: #075985;\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.control-panel label {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 8px;\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n  color: #334155;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\nselect {\n  width: 100%;\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 11px 12px;\n  background: white;\n  color: #0f172a;\n}\n\n.button-row {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 10px;\n  margin: 18px 0;\n}\n\n.selected-summary,\n.result {\n  border-radius: 16px;\n  padding: 16px;\n  margin-top: 16px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n}\n\n.selected-summary h3 {\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.selected-summary p {\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  color: #475569;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.result {\n  border: 1px solid;\n}\n\n.result--granted {\n  border-color: #86efac;\n  background: #f0fdf4;\n}\n\n.result--denied {\n  border-color: #fecaca;\n  background: #fef2f2;\n}\n\npre {\n  overflow: auto;\n  margin: 10px 0 0;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  background: #0f172a;\n  color: #dbeafe;\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.registry-count {\n  color: #64748b;\n  font-weight: 800;\n}\n\n.logs {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.log-entry {\n  border-left: 5px solid #38bdf8;\n  border-radius: 14px;\n  padding: 14px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n}\n\n.log-error {\n  border-left-color: #ef4444;\n}\n\n.log-warn {\n  border-left-color: #f59e0b;\n}\n\n.log-info {\n  border-left-color: #0f766e;\n}\n\n.log-entry__header {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 8px 16px;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n}\n\n.log-entry__header strong {\n  color: #0f172a;\n}\n\n.log-entry__header span,\n.log-entry p {\n  color: #64748b;\n}\n\n.log-entry p {\n  margin: 8px 0 0;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 920px) {\n  .hero,\n  .workspace,\n  .metrics {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n}\n""}],""reasoning"":""The request was broad, so I implemented the full browser-based gateway demonstration expected by the brief rather than asking for narrower scope. Key choices: keep state in memory, make domain logic reusable in `cdrGateway.js`, generate Australian-offset ISO strings without browser-local formatting, enforce the 365-day duration cap in creation, sanitize all returned telemetry, and provide UI controls to demonstrate grant/deny/revoke/reconcile paths.""}}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_schema\"",\""json_schema\"":{\""name\"":\""assistant_output\"",\""strict\"":true,\""schema\"":{\""$schema\"":\""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""message\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""},\""files\"":{\""type\"":\""array\"",\""items\"":{\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""path\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""},\""contents\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""}},\""required\"":[\""path\"",\""contents\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false},\""description\"":\""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""},\""reasoning\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""}},\""required\"":[\""message\"",\""files\"",\""reasoning\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false}}}"",""turnSeq"":""1"",""challengeTitle"":""Mid-Level Backend Engineer — Consumer Data Right (CDR) Consent Gateway"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","7056675e1aaa63a8f50d00f789783e123c2eb2cb","","[]"
