  }\n\n  const schema = EVENT_SCHEMA[eventType];\n  if (!schema) {\n    return { ok: false, errors: [{ path: \""eventType\"", reason: `eventType must be one of: ${Object.keys(EVENT_SCHEMA).join(\"", \"")}.` }] };\n  }\n\n  for (const key of Object.keys(raw)) {\n    if (!(key in schema.fields)) {\n      errors.push({ path: key, reason: `Field \""${key}\"" is not allowed for event type \""${eventType}\"".` });\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const fieldName of schema.required) {\n    if (raw[fieldName] === undefined) {\n      errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" is required.` });\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const [fieldName, value] of Object.entries(raw)) {\n    const spec = schema.fields[fieldName];\n    if (!spec) continue;\n    if (value === undefined) continue;\n    if (value === null) {\n      errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" cannot be null.` });\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    switch (spec.type) {\n      case \""string\"":\n        if (typeof value !== \""string\"") {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" must be a string.` });\n          continue;\n        }\n        if (spec.maxLength && value.length > spec.maxLength) {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" exceeds ${spec.maxLength} characters.` });\n        }\n        break;\n      case \""email\"":\n        if (typeof value !== \""string\"" || !EMAIL_REGEX.test(value.trim())) {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" must be a valid email address.` });\n          continue;\n        }\n        if (spec.maxLength && value.length > spec.maxLength) {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" exceeds ${spec.maxLength} characters.` });\n        }\n        break;\n      case \""phone\"":\n        if (typeof value !== \""string\"" || !AUSTRALIAN_PHONE_PATTERN.test(value.trim())) {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" must be a valid Australian phone number (e.g. 0412 345 678 or 02 9999 8888).` });\n          continue;\n        }\n        break;\n      case \""nationalId\"":\n        if (typeof value !== \""string\"" || !NATIONAL_ID_PATTERN.test(value.trim())) {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" must be a valid national identifier string.` });\n          continue;\n        }\n        break;\n      case \""enum\"":\n        if (typeof value !== \""string\"" || !spec.values.includes(value)) {\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field \""${fieldName}\"" must be one of: ${spec.values.join(\"", \"")}.` });\n        }\n        break;\n      default:\n        break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (errors.length > 0) {\n    return { ok: false, errors };\n  }\n\n  const sanitized = sanitizeEvent(raw);\n  return { ok: true, event: sanitized };\n}\n\nNote template literals with `${...}`. In JSON we must escape backtick? JSON doesn't need escape backtick. Double quotes inside template literals okay because JSON string uses double quotes but inner double quotes would terminate unless escaped. We are using double quotes inside template literal expressions like `.join(\"", \"")` with double quote characters. In JSON content, we need escape those double quotes or use single quotes. Better replace all internal double quotes in JS strings with single quotes to avoid escaping. For template literal expressions, we can use single quotes inside `${...}`. For `fieldName` reason strings, we use double quotes around fieldName? We can use single quotes: `Field '${fieldName}' is required.` etc. But in template literal, to include single quotes no issue. We'll use single quotes. For error object keys double quotes? Object keys can be unquoted? In object literal, keys can be identifiers unquoted. We'll use `path:` and `reason:`. Good. Avoid any double quotes in code entirely? We may still have JSON object strings from `JSON.stringify` in App. That's fine. For processEvent, no double quotes. We'll write all strings with single quotes in JS. For template literal backticks okay.\n\nNeed no double quotes in file contents? It's not required but helps JSON. We'll try to avoid double quotes entirely in JSX attributes and strings. Use single quotes for JSX attributes: `<section className='panel'>`. React accepts. For `style` maybe not. Good.\n\nBut sample event `SAMPLE_EVENT = JSON.stringify({...}, null, 2);` no double quote in source except JSON keys? We'll write object literal keys unquoted: `eventType: 'support_ticket'`, etc. good.\n\nIn App, we need `JSON.parse(input)` etc. no double quotes.\n\nIn textarea, no.\n\nCSS uses single quotes.\n\nNeed ensure no double quotes in regex string replacements? We use single quotes for constants. Good.\n\nFile 4: src/App.jsx\nimport { useState } from 'react';\nimport { processEvent } from './workflow/processEvent.js';\nimport { EVENT_SCHEMA } from './workflow/schema.js';\n\nconst SAMPLE_EVENT = JSON.stringify({\n  eventType: 'support_ticket',\n  eventId: 'evt_001',\n  customerEmail: 'jane.doe@example.com',\n  customerName: 'Jane Doe',\n  phone: '0412 345 678',\n  nationalId: '123 456 782',\n  description: 'Customer called from 02 9999 8888 and asked to update contact to jane.doe@example.com. TFN: 123 456 782.',\n  priority: 'high',\n}, null, 2);\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('');\n  const [errors, setErrors] = useState([]);\n  const [events, setEvents] = useState([]);\n  const [lastSanitized, setLastSanitized] = useState(null);\n\n  function handleProcess() {\n    setErrors([]);\n    setLastSanitized(null);\n\n    let parsed;\n    try {\n      parsed = JSON.parse(input);\n    } catch (err) {\n      setErrors([{ path: 'input', reason: `Invalid JSON: ${err.message}` }]);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const result = processEvent(parsed);\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      setErrors(result.errors);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const persisted = { ...result.event, persistedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\n    setEvents((prev) => [persisted, ...prev]);\n    setLastSanitized(result.event);\n    setInput('');\n  }\n\n  function loadSample() {\n    setInput(SAMPLE_EVENT);\n    setErrors([]);\n    setLastSanitized(null);\n  }\n\n  function clearAll() {\n    setInput('');\n    setErrors([]);\n    setLastSanitized(null);\n    setEvents([]);\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <main className='shell'>\n      <header className='hero'>\n        <p className='eyebrow'>Unknown · Australian Privacy Act 1988</p>\n        <h1>Workflow event sanitizer</h1>\n        <p className='lede'>\n          Validates workflow payloads against strict schemas and masks PII before anything is stored.\n          No raw phone numbers, national identifiers, or email addresses are persisted.\n        </p>\n      </header>\n\n      <div className='grid'>\n        <section className='panel'>\n          <h2>1. Submit workflow event</h2>\n          <textarea\n            className='editor'\n            rows={12}\n            value={input}\n            onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}\n            placeholder='Paste a JSON workflow event...'\n          />\n          <div className='actions'>\n            <button type='button' onClick={loadSample}>Load sample</button>\n            <button type='button' className='primary' onClick={handleProcess}>Process event</button>\n            <button type='button' className='secondary' onClick={clearAll}>Clear all</button>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section className='panel'>\n          <h2>2. Validation report</h2>\n          {errors.length > 0 ? (\n            <ul className='errors'>\n              {errors.map((err, index) => (\n                <li key={`${err.path}-${index}`}>\n                  <strong>{err.path}</strong> — {err.reason}\n                </li>\n              ))}\n            </ul>\n          ) : (\n            <p className='ok'>{lastSanitized ? 'Passed. PII was masked before persistence.' : 'No validation errors.'}</p>\n          )}\n          {lastSanitized && (\n            <pre className='preview'>{JSON.stringify(lastSanitized, null, 2)}</pre>\n          )}\n        </section>\n      </div>\n\n      <section className='panel'>\n        <h2>3. Persisted events ({events.length})</h2>\n        {events.length === 0 ? (\n          <p className='muted'>No events persisted yet. Process a valid event to see it here.</p>\n        ) : (\n          <ul className='event-list'>\n            {events.map((event) => (\n              <li key={event.eventId} className='event-card'>\n                <div className='event-meta'>\n                  <span className='badge'>{event.eventType}</span>\n                  <span>{event.persistedAt}</span>\n                </div>\n                <pre>{JSON.stringify(event, null, 2)}</pre>\n              </li>\n            ))}\n          </ul>\n        )}\n      </section>\n\n      <section className='panel'>\n        <h2>Strict schema boundaries</h2>\n        <div className='schema-grid'>\n          {Object.entries(EVENT_SCHEMA).map(([type, schema]) => (\n            <div className='schema-card' key={type}>\n              <h3>{type}</h3>\n              <p><strong>Required:</strong> {schema.required.join(', ')}</p>\n              <p><strong>Allowed:</strong> {Object.keys(schema.fields).join(', ')}</p>\n            </div>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\nNo double quotes in JSX strings? We have `<span className='badge'>` and contents. All single. In `key={`${err.path}-${index}`}` uses backtick with double quotes? It's template literal no double quotes. Good. `new Date().toISOString()` no. `placeholder='Paste a JSON workflow event...'` single. Good. No double quotes.\n\nFile 5: src/styles.css\n:root {\n  font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; /* single quotes */\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #f6f7f9;\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody { margin: 0; }\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 980px;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 40px 24px 64px;\n}\n\n.hero {\n  margin-bottom: 32px;\n}\n\n.eyebrow {\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #b45309;\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  font-size: 2rem;\n  margin: 0 0 12px;\n}\n\n.lede {\n  color: #4b5563;\n  max-width: 720px;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n.grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  gap: 20px;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n  .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n}\n\n.panel {\n  background: #ffffff;\n  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n  border-radius: 14px;\n  padding: 20px;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n\nh2 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 1.1rem; }\n\n.editor {\n  width: 100%;\n  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  resize: vertical;\n  background: #fafafa;\n}\n\n.actions { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n\nbutton {\n  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\n  background: #fff;\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n}\n\nbutton.primary { background: #0f172a; border-color: #0f172a; color: #fff; }\nbutton.secondary { background: #f3f4f6; }\n\n.errors {\n  list-style: none;\n  padding: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  border-left: 4px solid #dc2626;\n  background: #fef2f2;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n.errors li {\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #fee2e2;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n}\n\n.errors li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }\n\n.ok { background: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0; color: #166534; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 10px; }\n\n.preview {\n  background: #0f172a;\n  color: #e2e8f0;\n  padding: 14px;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  overflow: auto;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  max-height: 320px;\n  margin-top: 12px;\n}\n\n.event-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }\n\n.event-card { border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px; margin-bottom: 12px; background: #fff; }\n\n.event-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #6b7280; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n\n.badge {\n  background: #eef2ff;\n  color: #4338ca;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 2px 10px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\n}\n\n.event-card pre {\n  background: #f8fafc;\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  overflow: auto;\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  line-height: 1.45;\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.schema-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }\n\n.schema-card { background: #f9fafb; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; }\n\n.schema-card h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 0.95rem; }\n\n.schema-card p { margin: 4px 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #4b5563; }\n\n.muted { color: #6b7280; }\n\nNeed no double quotes in CSS. Font family single quotes. Good.\n\nNow ensure all file contents no double quotes. We can include in JSON without escaping double quotes? But JSON itself uses double quotes for keys and strings, but content strings can include single quotes only. Good. We still need escape backslashes in regex. Also maybe newline escapes `\\n`. We'll produce contents strings with `\\n` between lines. That's okay.\n\nNeed maybe for schema and sanitizer, there are regex literals with backslashes. We need double escape. Let's prepare each content with actual code and then JSON escape. I will manually write in final answer with `\\n` and `\\\\`.\n\nGiven space, we need be accurate.\n\nLet's write final message JSON.\n\nWe need \""message\"": plain brief: what did, assumed, check. Mention in-memory, no backend. \""Assumptions: interpreted unknown workflow event types, implemented mock event types; PII masking before in-memory persistence; strict schema rejects unknown fields; check sample and validation.\""\n\n\""files\"": array of five objects.\n\nNeed ensure all paths include leading? Use \""src/App.jsx\"", \""src/styles.css\"", \""src/workflow/schema.js\"", \""src/workflow/sanitizer.js\"", \""src/workflow/processEvent.js\"". Good.\n\nLet's craft JSON. Important: In JSON content, strings cannot contain unescaped newline. We'll use `\\n` for each line break. Indentation in code we can include as spaces. We can make each line separated by `\\n`. Need maintain code formatting.\n\nLet's generate each contents string. We'll write with newlines as `\\n` to be valid JSON. Since the final response is a JSON object, we can include actual newline between top-level fields, but inside string we must escape. I'll produce the JSON minified? It will be parsed by system; indentation optional. I can produce pretty JSON with actual newlines outside strings. That's fine. Within content strings, I'll use `\\n`. Let's do.\n\nNeed ensure no unescaped backslashes in JSON. In schema.js, regex:\n`/^[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}$/i`\ncontains `\\.` -> in JSON `\\\\.`? Actually regex literal in code has backslash dot. In JSON string, we need `\\\\`. So code content should show `\\\\.` in file? Wait code file should contain `\\.`? Let's clarify: If file content is `/\\.[A-Z]{2,}/` (one backslash in actual file), then in JSON string we need `\""/\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}/\""`. That means JSON text has two characters: backslash backslash then dot. The JSON parser interprets `\\\\` as single backslash, yielding actual `\\.` in file. So in final JSON representation, we write `\\\\`. Good.\n\nSimilarly `\\d` in regex => JSON `\\\\d`.\n\nIn string replacements? No regex literals in JS strings except constants. For sanitizer regex literals, we need backslashes doubled in JSON.\n\nLet's build content for schema.js with escaped:\n```\nexport const EVENT_TYPES = {\n  support_ticket: 'Support ticket',\n...\nexport const EMAIL_REGEX = /^[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}$/i;\nexport const AUSTRALIAN_PHONE_PATTERN = /^(?:(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)4\\\\d{2}[ -]?\\\\d{3}[ -]?\\\\d{3}|(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)[2378][ -]?\\\\d{4}[ -]?\\\\d{4})$/;\nexport const NATIONAL_ID_PATTERN = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\\\\s-]{5,19}$/;\n```\nNote in AUSTRALIAN_PHONE_PATTERN, second alternative had `(?:\\+?61[ -]?|0)` but inside first larger group; we write `(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)` and same. The `+` is literal, need `\\\\+`. Good.\n\nEVENT_SCHEMA object with nested fields; no backslashes.\n\nsanitizer.js:\n```\nexport const EMAIL_MASK = '***@***.***';\n...\nreturn input\n    .replace(/\\\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\\\b/gi, EMAIL_MASK)\n    .replace(/(?:(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)4\\\\d{2}[ -]?\\\\d{3}[ -]?\\\\d{3})|(?:(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)[2378][ -]?\\\\d{4}[ -]?\\\\d{4})\\\\b/g, PHONE_MASK)\n    .replace(/(?:\\\\bTFN\\\\b|\\\\btax file number\\\\b)[\\\\s:]*\\\\d{3}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{3}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{3}\\\\b/gi, NATIONAL_ID_MASK)\n    .replace(/(?:\\\\bmedicare\\\\b|\\\\bmedicare number\\\\b)[\\\\s:]*\\\\d{4}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{5}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{1}\\\\b/gi, NATIONAL_ID_MASK)\n    .replace(/(?:\\\\bdriver'?s? licence\\\\b|\\\\bdriver license\\\\b)[\\\\s:]*[a-z0-9]{6,12}\\\\b/gi, NATIONAL_ID_MASK);\n```\nNeed careful with `\\\\s` in JSON: `\\\\s` in JSON yields `\\s` in file. Good.\nIn `[\\\\s-]?` need JSON `[\\\\\\\\s-]?`? Let's think: actual file content should have `[\\s-]?`. That is backslash s then hyphen inside char class. In JSON string, backslash must be escaped as `\\\\`, so `[\\\\s-]?` becomes file `[\\s-]?`. Correct. In our JSON we write `[\\\\\\\\s-]?`? Wait `\\\\s` in JSON string is `\\s` in file. We need JSON string characters: `[`, `\\`, `\\`, `s`, `-`, `]`, `?`. In final output we type `[\\\\s-]?` (two backslashes). But in string representation, backslash is escaped, so to produce two backslashes, we write `\\\\\\\\`? Hmm.\n\nLet's reason: In the JSON text we are typing, every backslash in the actual file must be represented as `\\\\` in JSON. So if the file content string has chars: `[` `\\` `s` `-` `]`, then JSON text must have `[` `\\` `\\` `s` `-` `]`. So we type `[\\\\s-]`. That is two backslashes then s. But when I look at JSON, there are two characters: backslash backslash, which the JSON parser interprets as a single backslash. So correct. So we write `[\\\\s-]?` in the JSON string. There is no extra \""four backslashes\"". In the printed JSON, it will show as `[\\\\s-]?`. Good. No ambiguity.\n\nBut in our final answer, since it's plain text, we need physically have `\\\\s` (two backslash characters) in the contents string. The JSON parser will reduce to `\\s`. So each regex backslash becomes double. That means for each `\\` in code, JSON has `\\\\`. I'll write with `\\\\` in the contents. It may look like two characters. Good.\n\nIf code contains `\\b`, JSON `\\\\b`. `\\d` => `\\\\d`. `\\+` => `\\\\+`. `\\s` => `\\\\s`. `\\w` not used. `\\-` not used.\n\nNeed also ensure no unescaped double quote. We use single quotes, so okay.\n\nFor processEvent.js no regex, only template literals with `${}`. No backslashes. Good.\n\nFor App.jsx no backslashes. Good.\n\nFor CSS no backslashes. Good.\n\nNow produce JSON. Might be long but okay.\n\nLet's craft final answer now.""}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_object\""}"",""turnSeq"":""1"",""challengeTitle"":""Unknown — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","241476","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","140599a636cf63b237b309c9061d5be9d53ade3f","t-f114d33a-cce6-49d8-b076-67fbb1708af9","[]"
"t-f114d33a-cce6-49d8-b076-67fbb1708af9","f114d33a-cce6-49d8-b076-67fbb1708af9","ai_stage:assistant","SPAN","ai_stage:assistant","2026-09-29 15:33:53.391000","","","default","","u-jordan","zso59i0ef1elifo8altki4fd","DEFAULT","","","","","","","{}","{}","{}","0","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""Unknown — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for Unknown.\n\n# Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\n\n## Context & Objectives\nBuild a production-grade service module for **Unknown** that handles workflow events, enforces strict data scoping, and guarantees compliance with the Australian Privacy Act 1988.\n\n## Constraints\n1. **PII Masking**: Ensure phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses are masked prior to persistence.\n2. **Deterministic Validation**: Validate all inputs using strict schema boundaries.\n3. **Observable Verification**: Provide clear error reasons when input fails domain invariants.\n</challenge>\n\nCRITICAL: Respond ONLY with a valid JSON object strictly matching this schema:\n{\n  \""$schema\"": \""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\n  \""type\"": \""object\"",\n  \""properties\"": {\n    \""message\"": {\n      \""type\"": \""string\"",\n      \""description\"": \""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""\n    },\n    \""files\"": {\n      \""type\"": \""array\"",\n      \""items\"": {\n        \""type\"": \""object\"",\n        \""properties\"": {\n          \""path\"": {\n            \""type\"": \""string\""\n          },\n          \""contents\"": {\n            \""type\"": \""string\""\n          }\n        },\n        \""required\"": [\n          \""path\"",\n          \""contents\""\n        ],\n        \""additionalProperties\"": false\n      },\n      \""description\"": \""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""\n    },\n    \""reasoning\"": {\n      \""type\"": \""string\"",\n      \""description\"": \""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""\n    }\n  },\n  \""required\"": [\n    \""message\"",\n    \""files\"",\n    \""reasoning\""\n  ],\n  \""additionalProperties\"": false\n}""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Reviewer console — starter data\n\nYou are prototyping a reviewer console for an AI feature that summarises employee\nsurvey comments. Everything here is **synthetic**: invented people, teams and\ncomments for a fictional company.\n\n## Data (`src/data/`)\n\n- `teams.json` — `departments` and `teams`. Each team belongs to one department.\n- `responses.json` — one entry per **respondent**: `{ id, teamId, comment }`.\n  `comment` may be an empty string.\n- `summaries.json` — output of a (stubbed) LLM summariser. Each summary covers a\n  `team` or a `department` (`groupType` / `groupId`) and has `themes`; each theme\n  has a `title`, a `summary` and the `claims` it makes.\n\nImport them directly, e.g. `import teams from \""./data/teams.json\""`.\n\n## Running\n\nThe preview is already live. Edit `src/App.jsx` and add files under `src/`.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Your project starts here</h1>\n      <p>\n        Nothing has been built yet. Describe what you want in the chat and the\n        assistant will write the code.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/data/responses.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r01\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Release train is monthly and everything piles in the last week. Rollback ownership is unclear, it feels like nobody's job.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r02\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I like my team but the monthly release crunch is exhausting.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r03\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would love clear rollback ownership when a release goes wrong.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r04\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Deploys are fine. Wish we had more time for tech debt.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r05\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Remote days are great, I'd happily do more of them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r06\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r07\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Being the only person on the overnight reconciliation rota is wearing me down.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r08\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r09\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good team. Tech debt keeps getting pushed.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r10\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call is heavy and alerts are noisy.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r11\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Alert noise at night is the worst part of on-call.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r12\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I'd like a clearer path to senior.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r13\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Planning is good this quarter, priorities finally feel stable.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r14\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r15\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Too many meetings on Tuesdays and Thursdays.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r16\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r17\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call rota fairness could be better, same few people get paged.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r18\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Since I moved from the Perth office to lead the Atlas migration I've had no backup.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r19\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""App store approvals take forever and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r20\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Love the team, worried about headcount.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r21\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Customers get stuck at the data import step and the docs are out of date, so we field the same questions daily.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r22\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r23\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Import step is confusing for customers and the docs are out of date.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r24\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r25\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would like more time with customers rather than internal meetings.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r26\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket volume spikes after every release.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r27\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r28\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good tooling, but escalation paths are unclear.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r29\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Enjoy the work, wish escalation to engineering was faster.\""\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/summaries.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-payments\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release pressure\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Engineers feel the monthly release train creates a last-week crunch, and rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Working pattern\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Almost everyone in the team wants to work fully remotely.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Wellbeing\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Tech debt\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-platform\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call is heavy, alerts are noisy, and the load falls on the same few people.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy, especially at night.\"",\n          \""The same few people get paged.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Meetings\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Career growth\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""People want a clearer path to senior.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""People want a clearer path to senior.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-mobile\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Migration ownership\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release approvals\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-onboarding\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Import step\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Customers struggle with the data import step and the docs are out of date.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Customers struggle with the data import step.\"",\n          \""The docs are out of date.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-support\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Post-release load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Ticket volume and backlog spike after releases.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Ticket volume spikes after releases.\"",\n          \""The ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Escalation\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Escalation paths to engineering are unclear and slow.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Escalation paths are unclear.\"",\n          \""Escalation to engineering is slow.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-engineering\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""department\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""engineering\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release and rollout friction\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""A monthly release crunch, unclear rollback ownership, and slow app store approvals that nobody owns.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call load is heavy and alerts are noisy.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call load is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/teams.json ===\n{\n  \""departments\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""engineering\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""customer-success\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Customer Success\""\n    }\n  ],\n  \""teams\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""payments\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Payments\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""platform\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Platform\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""mobile\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Mobile\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""onboarding\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Onboarding\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""support\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Support\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\njust build it please, no mistake""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\n  \""message\"": \""I built an in-memory workflow event intake UI that validates payloads against strict event schemas, rejects unknown fields, and masks Australian phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses before the event is added to the persisted list. I assumed 'Unknown' is the fictional organisation and that the existing synthetic survey data was starter context, so the new feature is a standalone workflow-sanitization console. Check the preview by loading the sample event, processing it, then inspecting the sanitized preview and the persisted event list to confirm all raw PII is masked.\"",\n  \""files\"": [\n    {\n      \""path\"": \""src/App.jsx\"",\n      \""contents\"": \""import { useState } from 'react';\\nimport { processEvent } from './workflow/processEvent.js';\\nimport { EVENT_SCHEMA } from './workflow/schema.js';\\n\\nconst SAMPLE_EVENT = JSON.stringify({\\n  eventType: 'support_ticket',\\n  eventId: 'evt_001',\\n  customerEmail: 'jane.doe@example.com',\\n  customerName: 'Jane Doe',\\n  phone: '0412 345 678',\\n  nationalId: '123 456 782',\\n  description: 'Customer called from 02 9999 8888 and asked to update contact to jane.doe@example.com. TFN: 123 456 782.',\\n  priority: 'high',\\n}, null, 2);\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('');\\n  const [errors, setErrors] = useState([]);\\n  const [events, setEvents] = useState([]);\\n  const [lastSanitized, setLastSanitized] = useState(null);\\n\\n  function handleProcess() {\\n    setErrors([]);\\n    setLastSanitized(null);\\n\\n    let parsed;\\n    try {\\n      parsed = JSON.parse(input);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      setErrors([{ path: 'input', reason: `Invalid JSON: ${err.message}` }]);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const result = processEvent(parsed);\\n    if (!result.ok) {\\n      setErrors(result.errors);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const persisted = { ...result.event, persistedAt: new Date().toISOString() };\\n    setEvents((prev) => [persisted, ...prev]);\\n    setLastSanitized(result.event);\\n    setInput('');\\n  }\\n\\n  function loadSample() {\\n    setInput(SAMPLE_EVENT);\\n    setErrors([]);\\n    setLastSanitized(null);\\n  }\\n\\n  function clearAll() {\\n    setInput('');\\n    setErrors([]);\\n    setLastSanitized(null);\\n    setEvents([]);\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <main className='shell'>\\n      <header className='hero'>\\n        <p className='eyebrow'>Unknown · Australian Privacy Act 1988</p>\\n        <h1>Workflow event sanitizer</h1>\\n        <p className='lede'>\\n          Validates workflow payloads against strict schemas and masks PII before anything is stored.\\n          No raw phone numbers, national identifiers, or email addresses are persisted.\\n        </p>\\n      </header>\\n\\n      <div className='grid'>\\n        <section className='panel'>\\n          <h2>1. Submit workflow event</h2>\\n          <textarea\\n            className='editor'\\n            rows={12}\\n            value={input}\\n            onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}\\n            placeholder='Paste a JSON workflow event...'\\n          />\\n          <div className='actions'>\\n            <button type='button' onClick={loadSample}>Load sample</button>\\n            <button type='button' className='primary' onClick={handleProcess}>Process event</button>\\n            <button type='button' className='secondary' onClick={clearAll}>Clear all</button>\\n          </div>\\n        </section>\\n\\n        <section className='panel'>\\n          <h2>2. Validation report</h2>\\n          {errors.length > 0 ? (\\n            <ul className='errors'>\\n              {errors.map((err, index) => (\\n                <li key={`${err.path}-${index}`}>\\n                  <strong>{err.path}</strong> — {err.reason}\\n                </li>\\n              ))}\\n            </ul>\\n          ) : (\\n            <p className='ok'>{lastSanitized ? 'Passed. PII was masked before persistence.' : 'No validation errors.'}</p>\\n          )}\\n          {lastSanitized && (\\n            <pre className='preview'>{JSON.stringify(lastSanitized, null, 2)}</pre>\\n          )}\\n        </section>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      <section className='panel'>\\n        <h2>3. Persisted events ({events.length})</h2>\\n        {events.length === 0 ? (\\n          <p className='muted'>No events persisted yet. Process a valid event to see it here.</p>\\n        ) : (\\n          <ul className='event-list'>\\n            {events.map((event) => (\\n              <li key={event.eventId} className='event-card'>\\n                <div className='event-meta'>\\n                  <span className='badge'>{event.eventType}</span>\\n                  <span>{event.persistedAt}</span>\\n                </div>\\n                <pre>{JSON.stringify(event, null, 2)}</pre>\\n              </li>\\n            ))}\\n          </ul>\\n        )}\\n      </section>\\n\\n      <section className='panel'>\\n        <h2>Strict schema boundaries</h2>\\n        <div className='schema-grid'>\\n          {Object.entries(EVENT_SCHEMA).map(([type, schema]) => (\\n            <div className='schema-card' key={type}>\\n              <h3>{type}</h3>\\n              <p><strong>Required:</strong> {schema.required.join(', ')}</p>\\n              <p><strong>Allowed:</strong> {Object.keys(schema.fields).join(', ')}</p>\\n            </div>\\n          ))}\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n    </main>\\n  );\\n}\\n\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""path\"": \""src/styles.css\"",\n      \""contents\"": \"":root {\\n  font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;\\n  color: #1a1a1a;\\n  background: #f6f7f9;\\n}\\n\\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\\n\\nbody { margin: 0; }\\n\\n.shell {\\n  max-width: 980px;\\n  margin: 0 auto;\\n  padding: 40px 24px 64px;\\n}\\n\\n.hero {\\n  margin-bottom: 32px;\\n}\\n\\n.eyebrow {\\n  text-transform: uppercase;\\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\\n  font-weight: 700;\\n  color: #b45309;\\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\\n}\\n\\nh1 {\\n  font-size: 2rem;\\n  margin: 0 0 12px;\\n}\\n\\n.lede {\\n  color: #4b5563;\\n  max-width: 720px;\\n  line-height: 1.6;\\n}\\n\\n.grid {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\\n  gap: 20px;\\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\\n}\\n\\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\\n  .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\\n}\\n\\n.panel {\\n  background: #ffffff;\\n  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\\n  border-radius: 14px;\\n  padding: 20px;\\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\\n}\\n\\nh2 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 1.1rem; }\\n\\n.editor {\\n  width: 100%;\\n  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\\n  border-radius: 10px;\\n  padding: 12px;\\n  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace;\\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\\n  line-height: 1.5;\\n  resize: vertical;\\n  background: #fafafa;\\n}\\n\\n.actions { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\\n\\nbutton {\\n  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\\n  background: #fff;\\n  padding: 8px 14px;\\n  border-radius: 8px;\\n  cursor: pointer;\\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\\n}\\n\\nbutton.primary { background: #0f172a; border-color: #0f172a; color: #fff; }\\nbutton.secondary { background: #f3f4f6; }\\n\\n.errors {\\n  list-style: none;\\n  padding: 0;\\n  margin: 0;\\n  border-left: 4px solid #dc2626;\\n  background: #fef2f2;\\n  border-radius: 10px;\\n  overflow: hidden;\\n}\\n\\n.errors li {\\n  padding: 10px 14px;\\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #fee2e2;\\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\\n}\\n\\n.errors li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }\\n\\n.ok {\\n  background: #f0fdf4;\\n  border: 1px solid #bbf7d0;\\n  color: #166534;\\n  padding: 10px 14px;\\n  border-radius: 10px;\\n}\\n\\n.preview {\\n  background: #0f172a;\\n  color: #e2e8f0;\\n  padding: 14px;\\n  border-radius: 10px;\\n  overflow: auto;\\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\\n  line-height: 1.5;\\n  max-height: 320px;\\n  margin-top: 12px;\\n}\\n\\n.event-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }\\n\\n.event-card {\\n  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\\n  border-radius: 12px;\\n  padding: 14px;\\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\\n  background: #fff;\\n}\\n\\n.event-meta {\\n  display: flex;\\n  align-items: center;\\n  gap: 10px;\\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\\n  color: #6b7280;\\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\\n}\\n\\n.badge {\\n  background: #eef2ff;\\n  color: #4338ca;\\n  border-radius: 999px;\\n  padding: 2px 10px;\\n  font-weight: 600;\\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\\n}\\n\\n.event-card pre {\\n  background: #f8fafc;\\n  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;\\n  border-radius: 8px;\\n  padding: 12px;\\n  overflow: auto;\\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\\n  line-height: 1.45;\\n  margin: 0;\\n}\\n\\n.schema-grid {\\n  display: grid;\\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));\\n  gap: 14px;\\n}\\n\\n.schema-card {\\n  background: #f9fafb;\\n  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\\n  border-radius: 10px;\\n  padding: 14px;\\n}\\n\\n.schema-card h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 0.95rem; }\\n\\n.schema-card p { margin: 4px 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #4b5563; }\\n\\n.muted { color: #6b7280; }\\n\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""path\"": \""src/workflow/schema.js\"",\n      \""contents\"": \""export const EVENT_TYPES = {\\n  support_ticket: 'Support ticket',\\n  employee_update: 'Employee update',\\n  incident_report: 'Incident report',\\n};\\n\\nexport const PRIORITY_VALUES = ['low', 'medium', 'high', 'critical'];\\n\\nexport const EMAIL_REGEX = /^[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}$/i;\\nexport const AUSTRALIAN_PHONE_PATTERN = /^(?:(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)4\\\\d{2}[ -]?\\\\d{3}[ -]?\\\\d{3}|(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)[2378][ -]?\\\\d{4}[ -]?\\\\d{4})$/;\\nexport const NATIONAL_ID_PATTERN = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\\\\s-]{5,19}$/;\\n\\nexport const EVENT_SCHEMA = {\\n  support_ticket: {\\n    required: ['eventType', 'eventId', 'customerEmail', 'description'],\\n    fields: {\\n      eventType: { type: 'enum', values: ['support_ticket'] },\\n      eventId: { type: 'string', maxLength: 64 },\\n      customerEmail: { type: 'email', maxLength: 254 },\\n      customerName: { type: 'string', maxLength: 120 },\\n      phone: { type: 'phone' },\\n      nationalId: { type: 'nationalId' },\\n      description: { type: 'string', maxLength: 1000, scanPii: true },\\n      priority: { type: 'enum', values: PRIORITY_VALUES },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  employee_update: {\\n    required: ['eventType', 'eventId', 'employeeEmail', 'fullName'],\\n    fields: {\\n      eventType: { type: 'enum', values: ['employee_update'] },\\n      eventId: { type: 'string', maxLength: 64 },\\n      employeeEmail: { type: 'email', maxLength: 254 },\\n      fullName: { type: 'string', maxLength: 120 },\\n      phone: { type: 'phone' },\\n      nationalId: { type: 'nationalId' },\\n      note: { type: 'string', maxLength: 1000, scanPii: true },\\n      role: { type: 'string', maxLength: 80 },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  incident_report: {\\n    required: ['eventType', 'eventId', 'reporterEmail', 'summary'],\\n    fields: {\\n      eventType: { type: 'enum', values: ['incident_report'] },\\n      eventId: { type: 'string', maxLength: 64 },\\n      reporterEmail: { type: 'email', maxLength: 254 },\\n      reporterPhone: { type: 'phone' },\\n      reporterNationalId: { type: 'nationalId' },\\n      summary: { type: 'string', maxLength: 2000, scanPii: true },\\n      severity: { type: 'enum', values: ['minor', 'major', 'critical'] },\\n    },\\n  },\\n};\\n\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""path\"": \""src/workflow/sanitizer.js\"",\n      \""contents\"": \""import { EVENT_SCHEMA } from './schema.js';\\n\\nexport const EMAIL_MASK = '***@***.***';\\nexport const PHONE_MASK = '*** *** ***';\\nexport const NATIONAL_ID_MASK = '***-***-***';\\n\\nfunction scanAndMaskPii(input) {\\n  if (typeof input !== 'string') return input;\\n\\n  return input\\n    .replace(/\\\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\\\b/gi, EMAIL_MASK)\\n    .replace(/(?:(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)4\\\\d{2}[ -]?\\\\d{3}[ -]?\\\\d{3})|(?:(?:\\\\+?61[ -]?|0)[2378][ -]?\\\\d{4}[ -]?\\\\d{4})\\\\b/g, PHONE_MASK)\\n    .replace(/(?:\\\\bTFN\\\\b|\\\\btax file number\\\\b)[\\\\s:]*\\\\d{3}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{3}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{3}\\\\b/gi, NATIONAL_ID_MASK)\\n    .replace(/(?:\\\\bmedicare\\\\b|\\\\bmedicare number\\\\b)[\\\\s:]*\\\\d{4}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{5}[\\\\s-]?\\\\d{1}\\\\b/gi, NATIONAL_ID_MASK)\\n    .replace(/(?:\\\\bdriver'?s? licence\\\\b|\\\\bdriver license\\\\b)[\\\\s:]*[a-z0-9]{6,12}\\\\b/gi, NATIONAL_ID_MASK);\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskEmail() {\\n  return EMAIL_MASK;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskPhone() {\\n  return PHONE_MASK;\\n}\\n\\nexport function maskNationalId() {\\n  return NATIONAL_ID_MASK;\\n}\\n\\nexport function sanitizeEvent(event) {\\n  const schema = EVENT_SCHEMA[event.eventType];\\n  const sanitized = { ...event };\\n\\n  for (const [key, spec] of Object.entries(schema.fields)) {\\n    if (sanitized[key] === undefined) continue;\\n\\n    if (spec.type === 'email') {\\n      sanitized[key] = maskEmail();\\n    } else if (spec.type === 'phone') {\\n      sanitized[key] = maskPhone();\\n    } else if (spec.type === 'nationalId') {\\n      sanitized[key] = maskNationalId();\\n    } else if (spec.scanPii) {\\n      sanitized[key] = scanAndMaskPii(sanitized[key]);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return sanitized;\\n}\\n\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""path\"": \""src/workflow/processEvent.js\"",\n      \""contents\"": \""import { EVENT_SCHEMA, EMAIL_REGEX, AUSTRALIAN_PHONE_PATTERN, NATIONAL_ID_PATTERN } from './schema.js';\\nimport { sanitizeEvent } from './sanitizer.js';\\n\\nexport function processEvent(raw) {\\n  const errors = [];\\n\\n  if (!raw || typeof raw !== 'object' || Array.isArray(raw)) {\\n    return { ok: false, errors: [{ path: 'input', reason: 'Payload must be a JSON object.' }] };\\n  }\\n\\n  const eventType = raw.eventType;\\n  if (typeof eventType !== 'string') {\\n    return { ok: false, errors: [{ path: 'eventType', reason: 'eventType is required and must be a string.' }] };\\n  }\\n\\n  const schema = EVENT_SCHEMA[eventType];\\n  if (!schema) {\\n    return {\\n      ok: false,\\n      errors: [{ path: 'eventType', reason: `eventType must be one of: ${Object.keys(EVENT_SCHEMA).join(', ')}.` }],\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const key of Object.keys(raw)) {\\n    if (!(key in schema.fields)) {\\n      errors.push({ path: key, reason: `Field '${key}' is not allowed for event type '${eventType}'.` });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const fieldName of schema.required) {\\n    if (raw[fieldName] === undefined) {\\n      errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' is required.` });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const [fieldName, value] of Object.entries(raw)) {\\n    const spec = schema.fields[fieldName];\\n    if (!spec) continue;\\n    if (value === undefined) continue;\\n\\n    if (value === null) {\\n      errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' cannot be null.` });\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n\\n    switch (spec.type) {\\n      case 'string':\\n        if (typeof value !== 'string') {\\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' must be a string.` });\\n          continue;\\n        }\\n        if (spec.maxLength && value.length > spec.maxLength) {\\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' exceeds ${spec.maxLength} characters.` });\\n        }\\n        break;\\n      case 'email':\\n        if (typeof value !== 'string' || !EMAIL_REGEX.test(value.trim())) {\\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' must be a valid email address.` });\\n          continue;\\n        }\\n        if (spec.maxLength && value.length > spec.maxLength) {\\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' exceeds ${spec.maxLength} characters.` });\\n        }\\n        break;\\n      case 'phone':\\n        if (typeof value !== 'string' || !AUSTRALIAN_PHONE_PATTERN.test(value.trim())) {\\n          errors.push({\\n            path: fieldName,\\n            reason: `Field '${fieldName}' must be a valid Australian phone number (e.g. 0412 345 678 or 02 9999 8888).`,\\n          });\\n          continue;\\n        }\\n        break;\\n      case 'nationalId':\\n        if (typeof value !== 'string' || !NATIONAL_ID_PATTERN.test(value.trim())) {\\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' must be a valid national identifier string.` });\\n          continue;\\n        }\\n        break;\\n      case 'enum':\\n        if (typeof value !== 'string' || !spec.values.includes(value)) {\\n          errors.push({ path: fieldName, reason: `Field '${fieldName}' must be one of: ${spec.values.join(', ')}.` });\\n        }\\n        break;\\n      default:\\n        break;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  if (errors.length > 0) {\\n    return { ok: false, errors };\\n  }\\n\\n  const sanitized = sanitizeEvent(raw);\\n  return { ok: true, event: sanitized };\\n}\\n\""\n    }\n  ],\n  \""reasoning\"": \""I interpreted the brief as asking for a front-end implementation of the described service module, using in-memory state as the persistence layer because there is no backend. I created a strict schema per event type with unknown-field rejection, deterministic validation errors, and a sanitizer that masks entire PII fields plus free-text PII patterns before events are stored. The existing synthetic survey data was left unchanged since the new workflow console is self-contained.\""\n}"",""reasoning_content"":""We need answer JSON only. Need build project based on brief. Need infer what to build. We have starter reviewer console for AI summarization. Brief says \""Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\"" handling workflow events, strict data scoping, Australian Privacy Act PII masking phone numbers, national IDs, emails prior persistence, deterministic validation strict schema boundaries, observable verification clear error reasons. Also concept \""Unknown\"" maybe company. But starter data is reviewer console synthetic. Candidate says \""just build it please, no mistake\"" meaning implement the brief. Need decide build a component in React maybe a module/service that demonstrates sanitization and validation. Existing project imports JSON data. Need maybe create app with an \""Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\"". Since no backend, use local data/in-memory logic. Need produce files. We should read current files provided. Need implement production-grade service module for Unknown. Could be a UI with a workflow event ingestion form + list, masking PII, validation schemas, error reasons. Need satisfy constraints.\n\nWe need output complete new contents for files we create/change. Likely App.jsx, maybe add src/lib/sanitizer.js, src/lib/validator.js, maybe styles. Need keep under 300 lines.\n\nNeed think about exact requirements. \""handles workflow events, enforces strict data scoping\"" Data scoping maybe ensure only fields allowed per event type? We can design event types: incident, comment, support ticket? Need infer from existing data maybe survey comments. But brief says phone numbers, national IDs, email addresses. Could build \""Workflow Event Sanitizer Console\"" that validates an event payload against schema and masks PII before persisting to local list. That would be observable UI. Need include Australian Privacy Act compliance. Need deterministic validation. Strict schema boundaries. Clear error reasons.\n\nWe can create:\n- src/lib/piiMasking.js: maskPhone, maskEmail, maskNationalId (Australian TFN? Medicare? Driver's licence? We can mask generic national ID)\n- src/lib/workflowSchema.js: define event schema, event types (e.g., EMPLOYEE_SURVEY, SUPPORT_TICKET, INCIDENT_REPORT) with permitted fields, required fields, types, lengths, enums.\n- src/lib/workflowEvents.js: processWorkflowEvent(raw) returns { ok, value: sanitizedEvent, errors: [{ field, reason }] } or { ok:false, errors }. It validates then masks PII fields. Need \""prevent PII from persisting\"" — before adding to stored events, in-memory.\n\nUI:\n- Form to enter JSON event maybe textarea and submit, or individual fields. Better for observable verification: a textarea where candidate can paste JSON event, click Process & Queue. Shows validation errors or sanitized event and persisted list.\n- List queued persisted events with masked PII shown. Persistence in React state/localStorage? In-memory is okay but \""prior to persistence\"" can use in-memory store. Could use useState. To be production-like, maybe use a module store with events array, but React state fine.\n- Show sanitization explanation and examples.\n- Show data scoping: only fields defined in schema allowed; unknown fields rejected or stripped? Strict schema boundaries likely reject unknown fields. We can reject unknown fields with clear reasons. That ensures no extra data.\n- Provide sample event JSON with phone, email, nationalId.\n- Maybe built-in example buttons.\n\nNeed design JSON input to demonstrate. But UI could be complex. Need no mistake. We can implement a robust single-page app.\n\nLet's craft code. Need files:\n- src/App.jsx\n- src/styles.css (modify existing to style UI)\n- src/workflow/sanitize.js (or lib)\n- src/workflow/schema.js\n- src/workflow/processEvent.js\nPossibly src/workflow/sampleEvents.js.\n\nNeed ensure imports. Use ES modules. package JSON no additional deps. Vite can import JSON already. We might use JSON import for sample? Could just embed sample event in JS. Existing data not necessary to use but maybe candidate expects use provided data? The brief says \""Unknown\"" maybe should build on current project data. The starter data is about reviewer console employee survey summaries. The task is \""Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\"" for Unknown, maybe superimposed. We need use existing synthetic data? Could integrate by displaying summaries? But brief does not mention surveys. It says workflow events. Maybe we should keep existing data and augment App with new workflow sanitization. But \""just build it please\"" likely means implement brief with existing starter. We should not ignore afe. We can build workflow sanitizer and also maybe incorporate the existing data as context? The data includes comments that may contain PII? The comment in mobile mentions \""Perth office\"" but no phone/email/ID. We could demonstrate sanitization on survey comments? But PII includes phone numbers, national IDs, emails. Existing responses don't contain such. So build separate event ingestion. Could maybe create a data-sensitivity reviewer console that scans comments? But brief specific: workflow events, error reasons. So build a workflow event intake component.\n\nMaybe candidate simply wants the task done, no question. We can build.\n\nNeed be careful JSON output: message, files array with path/contents, reasoning. Files complete.\n\nLet's design schema.\n\nEvent types:\n- \""support_ticket\"": fields customerName?, customerEmail required, phone optional, nationalId optional, description required, priority enum\n- \""employee_update\"": fields employeeId required, email required, phone optional, nationalId optional, note optional\n- \""incident_report\"": fields reporterEmail required, phone optional, nationalId optional, summary required\nBut data scoping: different types permit different fields. Need not include actual collected PII in description? We can allow free text with PII? Need ensure phone/email/nationalId in free text? The brief says \""Ensure phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses are masked prior to persistence.\"" We should mask PII in any string field? Maybe define scanner that masks patterns inside any string, not just specific fields. Better: The sanitizer runs over all string values and masks email addresses, Australian phone numbers, and national ID patterns wherever they appear. That satisfies PII masking comprehensively. Specific phone/national/email fields also masked. Need production-grade: regex patterns.\n\nAustralian Privacy Act: mention in UI \""PII is masked before persistence, no raw PII stored\"".\n\nDeterministic validation:\n- schema object with type definitions.\n- Validation function:\n  - Check root is object.\n  - Check event type allowed.\n  - For each required field present and type correct.\n  - For optional fields, if present must be correct type.\n  - Unknown fields return errors? \""strict schema boundaries\"" yes reject unknown fields. But if logging raw payload? We can include unknown fields in errors. We can list unknown fields.\n  - String max length (maybe 500 for descriptions, 120 for names).\n  - Email format? We can validate format if field indicated as email or always when key contains email? Use regex.\n  - Phone maybe accept Australian formats.\n  - NationalId maybe generic pattern? Could be numeric/string length? We can validate if field marked nationalId and not empty; maybe accept string length 8-12 alphanumeric? Need not overdo.\n  - Enum for priority if present.\n- Error format: array of { path, reason, value? } but not raw value for PII? For observable verification, provide path + reason, not raw value to avoid leaking? Could include raw value? avoid for PII. We can not include value for PII fields. Fine.\n- If errors, return ok false, no persistence.\n\nProcess:\nfunction processEvent(raw) {\n  const validation = validateEvent(raw)\n  if (!validation.ok) return { ok:false, errors: validation.errors }\n  const sanitized = maskPiiDeep(validation.value)\n  // after masking, ensure no PII patterns? But if masked field contains \""***\"" no issue.\n  // We may re-run a check? Could verify no raw email/phone/national ID patterns. \n  return { ok:true, event: sanitized, changes: diff? }\n}\nNeed maybe persist: UI adds to store after process ok. We can also use sessionStorage for persistence. But in-memory state adequate. \""prior to persistence\"" not actual db. Use React useState. Could create store module with subscribe? Simpler: App state with processed events.\n\nNeed UI:\n- Header: \""Unknown — Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization\""\n- Information panel about compliance.\n- Left: Input JSON textarea.\n- Buttons: \""Load sample\"", \""Process event\"", \""Clear\"".\n- Error list: red card with reasons.\n- Sanitized preview: show sanitized JSON.\n- Persisted events: table/cards showing id, type, timestamp, sanitized payload.\n- Maybe show \""Data scoping\"" list allowed fields per selected type.\n\nNeed maybe no localStorage because synthetic, but in memory \""persisted\"" to state. Could localStorage be considered persistence and PII masked, okay. But initial empty. Use useState.\n\nNeed code compact.\n\nImplementation specifics:\n\nsanitizePiiDeep(value):\n- If string:\n  - Use regex to mask:\n    email regex: /\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\b/gi -> replace with \""[email masked]\""? Actually \""masked\"" maybe \""***@***.***\"" but preserving no info. Use \""[email masked]\"". But to be deterministic, can replace with \""***@***.***\""? Better for UI: \""***@***.***\"". But if we need \""no raw PII stored\"", any constant is fine. We can define \""email-masked\"" maybe.\n    phone regex for Australian numbers: need multiple formats:\n      - +61 4xx xxx xxx, +61 2 1234 5678\n      - 04xx xxx xxx, 02 1234 5678\n      - (02) 1234 5678\n      We can simpler:\n      /(?:\\+?61|0)[ ]?(?:4\\d{2}|[2378]\\d{1})[ ]?\\d{3}[ ]?\\d{3}\\b/g? But might mismatch. Better general phone: /(?:\\+?61|0)[\\s-]?(?:4\\d{2}|[2378]\\d{1})[\\s-]?\\d{3}[\\s-]?\\d{3}\\b/g. Also lo