or stored display, okay.\n\nNeed `maskEmail`:\nfunction maskEmail(email) { return \""***@***.***\""; }\nBut this is deterministic. Could preserve domain? Privacy could be more strict. \""no raw PII stored\"" okay constant. For UI maybe show exactly masked. But no way to distinguish. Fine.\nmaskPhone => \""(masked) *** *** ***\"" maybe.\nmaskNationalId => \""***-***-***\""\nscanAndMaskPii(value):\n- Apply email regex globally.\n- Apply phone regex globally.\n- Apply national id explicit patterns:\n   - /(?:\\bTFN\\b|\\btax file number\\b)\\s*:?\\s*\\d{3}[\\s-]?\\d{3}[\\s-]?\\d{3}\\b/ig -> \""[national id masked]\""\n   - /(?:\\bmedicare\\b|\\bmedicare number\\b)\\s*:?\\s*\\d{4}[\\s-]?\\d{5}[\\s-]?\\d{1}\\b/ig -> \""[national id masked]\""\n   - /(?:\\bdriver'?s? licence\\b|\\bdriver license\\b|\\bdriver's license\\b)\\s*:?\\s*[a-z0-9]{6,12}\\b/ig -> \""[national id masked]\""\nCould also generic 8-9 digit with TFN? Already covered.\nPhone regex must be robust, not mask random numeric in description. We'll use:\nconst phoneRegex = /(?:\\+?61[ -]?|0)(?:4\\d{2}|[2378]\\d{1})[ -]?\\d{3}[ -]?\\d{3}\\b/g\nThis matches:\n- +61 412 345 678: +61[ -]? => +61, then 4\\d{2} => 412, [ -]? space, \\d{3} => 345, [ -]? space, \\d{3} => 678. Yes.\n- 0412 345 678: 0 -> 0, 4\\d{2}=412, space, 345 space 678. good.\n- 02 9999 8888: 0 -> 0, [2378]\\d{1}=02? Actually [2378]\\d{1} = 02? It matches 0 then 2? Wait regex begins `(?:\\+?61[ -]?|0)` then group `(?:4\\d{2}|[2378]\\d{1})`. For \""02 9999 8888\"", begins with 0 (alternative), then [2378]\\d{1} needs 2 then digit, but \""02 \"" has 0 then 2 then space; [2378]\\d{1} tries '2' then space fails because \\d expected. So pattern fails. Need better local number pattern. Could use separate:\nconst australianPhoneRegex = /(?:(?:\\+?61[ -]?|0)(?:4\\d{2}|[2378]\\d{1})[ -]?\\d{3}[ -]?\\d{3})|(?:(?:\\+?61[ -]?|0)[2378][ -]?\\d{4}[ -]?\\d{4})\\b/g\nFor \""02 9999 8888\"": alternative 0, [2378] -> 2? Wait `[2378]` is one digit 2? But after 0 is 2