"ab26c0ef-dbf9-4567-a5ec-6402e29354a1","387570f2-c22b-43fc-9f67-53c99c5bef07","ai_stage:assistant","GENERATION","lV.chat","2026-09-28 04:37:00.949000","2026-09-28 04:37:52.963000","","default","","candidate-1","rsri7n9d9d4ij1ii7boywd8o","DEFAULT","","","","","0a8ec527-44e0-4ee3-8005-a1865d712ec6","gpt-5.5-2026-04-23","{""response_format"":null}","{""input"":""5497"",""output"":""7169"",""total"":""12666"",""input_cached_tokens"":""0"",""input_audio_tokens"":""0"",""output_reasoning_tokens"":""1536"",""output_audio_tokens"":""0"",""output_accepted_prediction_tokens"":""0"",""output_rejected_prediction_tokens"":""0""}","{""input"":0.027485,""output"":0.21507,""input_cached_tokens"":0,""output_reasoning_tokens"":0.04608,""total"":0.288635}","0.288635","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for BlueScope.\n\n# Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\n\n## Context & Objectives\nBuild a production-grade service module for **BlueScope** that handles workflow events, enforces strict data scoping, and guarantees compliance with the Australian Privacy Act 1988.\n\n## Constraints\n1. **PII Masking**: Ensure phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses are masked prior to persistence.\n2. **Deterministic Validation**: Validate all inputs using strict schema boundaries.\n3. **Observable Verification**: Provide clear error reasons when input fails domain invariants.\n</challenge>""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""can you help me explain the data given in the json?""},{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""The JSON data represents a synthetic employee survey review dataset. I haven’t changed any files.\n\n- `teams.json` defines the organisation structure: departments and the teams inside them.\n- `responses.json` contains individual survey responses, one per respondent. Each response has an `id`, a `teamId`, and a free-text `comment`. Some comments are empty.\n- `summaries.json` contains AI-generated summary outputs for teams or departments. Each summary includes themes, summaries, and specific claims the AI is making.\n\nImportant: the summaries are not guaranteed to be correct. Some claims appear well-supported by the raw responses, while others look exaggerated, unsupported, or privacy-sensitive. This dataset is likely intended for building a reviewer console that lets humans check whether AI summaries are accurate and safe before use.""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""give me a little stat about the data at least? is there any security concern?""},{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""Here are a few quick stats from the JSON, plus security/privacy observations. I didn’t change any files.\n\nStats:\n- 2 departments: Engineering and Customer Success.\n- 5 teams total.\n- 29 survey responses.\n- 23 responses contain comments; 6 are blank.\n- Team response counts:\n  - Payments: 9 responses, 7 with comments.\n  - Platform: 8 responses, 6 with comments.\n  - Mobile: 3 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Onboarding: 5 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Support: 4 responses, 4 with comments.\n- 6 AI summaries total: 5 team summaries and 1 Engineering department summary.\n- 12 summary themes total.\n\nPotential security/privacy concerns:\n- The dataset is synthetic, but it contains examples of potentially identifying details.\n- The Mobile comment and summary mention “Perth office”, “lead”, and “Atlas migration”. In a small team of only 3 responses, that could identify a specific person.\n- The Payments wellbeing summary says “One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.” That is sensitive wellbeing information and may identify someone if the rota is known.\n- Small groups are risky: Mobile has only 3 responses, and some claims are based on a single comment. Summaries for small teams should probably be suppressed, generalised, or flagged for reviewer approval.\n- Some summaries appear unsupported or exaggerated, e.g. Payments says “Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,” but only one comment says remote days are great.\n- There are no obvious phone numbers, emails, or national IDs in the current data, but a real system should still mask those before saving or displaying comments.\n\nIn short: the biggest concern is not classic credentials/security leakage, but privacy leakage through small-group comments, wellbeing details, location/project references, and unsupported AI claims.""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Reviewer console — starter data\n\nYou are prototyping a reviewer console for an AI feature that summarises employee\nsurvey comments. Everything here is **synthetic**: invented people, teams and\ncomments for a fictional company.\n\n## Data (`src/data/`)\n\n- `teams.json` — `departments` and `teams`. Each team belongs to one department.\n- `responses.json` — one entry per **respondent**: `{ id, teamId, comment }`.\n  `comment` may be an empty string.\n- `summaries.json` — output of a (stubbed) LLM summariser. Each summary covers a\n  `team` or a `department` (`groupType` / `groupId`) and has `themes`; each theme\n  has a `title`, a `summary` and the `claims` it makes.\n\nImport them directly, e.g. `import teams from \""./data/teams.json\""`.\n\n## Running\n\nThe preview is already live. Edit `src/App.jsx` and add files under `src/`.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Your project starts here</h1>\n      <p>\n        Nothing has been built yet. Describe what you want in the chat and the\n        assistant will write the code.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/data/responses.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r01\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Release train is monthly and everything piles in the last week. Rollback ownership is unclear, it feels like nobody's job.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r02\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I like my team but the monthly release crunch is exhausting.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r03\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would love clear rollback ownership when a release goes wrong.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r04\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Deploys are fine. Wish we had more time for tech debt.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r05\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Remote days are great, I'd happily do more of them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r06\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r07\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Being the only person on the overnight reconciliation rota is wearing me down.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r08\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r09\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good team. Tech debt keeps getting pushed.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r10\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call is heavy and alerts are noisy.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r11\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Alert noise at night is the worst part of on-call.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r12\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I'd like a clearer path to senior.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r13\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Planning is good this quarter, priorities finally feel stable.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r14\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r15\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Too many meetings on Tuesdays and Thursdays.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r16\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r17\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call rota fairness could be better, same few people get paged.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r18\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Since I moved from the Perth office to lead the Atlas migration I've had no backup.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r19\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""App store approvals take forever and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r20\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Love the team, worried about headcount.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r21\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Customers get stuck at the data import step and the docs are out of date, so we field the same questions daily.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r22\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r23\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Import step is confusing for customers and the docs are out of date.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r24\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r25\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would like more time with customers rather than internal meetings.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r26\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket volume spikes after every release.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r27\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r28\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good tooling, but escalation paths are unclear.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r29\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Enjoy the work, wish escalation to engineering was faster.\""\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/summaries.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-payments\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release pressure\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Engineers feel the monthly release train creates a last-week crunch, and rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Working pattern\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Almost everyone in the team wants to work fully remotely.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Wellbeing\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Tech debt\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-platform\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call is heavy, alerts are noisy, and the load falls on the same few people.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy, especially at night.\"",\n          \""The same few people get paged.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Meetings\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Career growth\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""People want a clearer path to senior.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""People want a clearer path to senior.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-mobile\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Migration ownership\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release approvals\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-onboarding\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Import step\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Customers struggle with the data import step and the docs are out of date.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Customers struggle with the data import step.\"",\n          \""The docs are out of date.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-support\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Post-release load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Ticket volume and backlog spike after releases.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Ticket volume spikes after releases.\"",\n          \""The ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Escalation\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Escalation paths to engineering are unclear and slow.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Escalation paths are unclear.\"",\n          \""Escalation to engineering is slow.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-engineering\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""department\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""engineering\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release and rollout friction\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""A monthly release crunch, unclear rollback ownership, and slow app store approvals that nobody owns.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call load is heavy and alerts are noisy.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call load is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/teams.json ===\n{\n  \""departments\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""engineering\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""customer-success\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Customer Success\""\n    }\n  ],\n  \""teams\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""payments\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Payments\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""platform\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Platform\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""mobile\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Mobile\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""onboarding\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Onboarding\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""support\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Support\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\nAct as a Principal AI Safety & Systems Architect specializing in enterprise privacy, human-in-the-loop (HITL) audit systems, and natural language verification.\n\n### System Overview & Context\nWe are engineering an automated review, verification, and sanitization engine for an enterprise employee survey platform. The system ingests raw survey data alongside AI-generated summaries and flags compliance violations, privacy risks, and hallucinations before any summary is published to leadership.\n\n### Input Data Topography\nThe system operates on three existing JSON datasets:\n1. `teams.json`: Org hierarchy defining departments (Engineering, Customer Success) and nested teams (Payments, Platform, Mobile, Onboarding, Support).\n2. `responses.json`: 29 raw survey records (`id`, `teamId`, free-text `comment`), including empty comments (6 records) and valid comments (23 records).\n3. `summaries.json`: 6 AI-generated summaries (5 team-level, 1 department-level) containing 12 themes, executive narratives, and discrete claims.\n\n### Identified Critical Vulnerabilities in Current Data\nOur system must catch and programmatically flag known anti-patterns present in this dataset:\n1. Re-identification via Small Cohorts & Quasi-Identifiers:\n   - The Mobile team has only 3 responses ($n=3$).\n   - Comments/summaries reference narrow quasi-identifiers (\""Perth office\"", \""lead\"", \""Atlas migration\""), creating extreme deanonymization risk.\n2. Sensitive Wellbeing & Attributable Disclosure:\n   - The Payments summary explicitly leaks: \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"" This attributes sensitive mental health/burnout state to a known, single-person operational role.\n3. Unsupported Claims & Frequency Hallucinations:\n   - The Payments summary claims \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,\"" despite only a single raw response mentioning remote work.\n4. Data Scoping & Rollup Boundary Breaches:\n   - Department summaries aggregating or leaking un-redacted team-specific identifiable claims.\n\n---\n\n### Core Objectives & Architecture Requirements\n\nYou will design and implement the backend verification & reviewer module adhering to strict Clean/Hexagonal Architecture:\n\n1. Deterministic Ingestion & Invariant Validation:\n   - Strongly typed data contracts (using strict schema validation with zero implicit coercion).\n   - Invariant checks: handle empty comments, missing teams, orphaned response IDs, and cross-department bleed.\n\n2. Privacy, k-Anonymity & Sanitization Engine:\n   - Cohort Suppression Policy: Enforce minimum response thresholds ($k \\ge 5$). Any team summary with $n < 5$ (e.g., Mobile) must be automatically marked `SUPPRESSED` or restricted from direct rollup.\n   - PII & Quasi-Identifier Detection: Mask direct PII (emails, phone numbers, employee IDs) and flag high-entropy quasi-identifiers (office locations + single-person roles).\n   - Sensitive Attribute Quarantine: Detect and redact individual health/burnout attributions tied to unique shifts/rotas.\n\n3. Claim Provenance & Faithfulness Verification:\n   - Claim Decomposition: Split AI summary text into atomic, testable claims.\n   - Grounding & Evidence Scoring: Map each claim against supporting raw responses.\n   - Hyperbole/Frequency Mismatch Detection: Flag quantifier mismatches (e.g., summary claims \""almost everyone\"", \""consistently\"", \""unanimously\"" when support count is $< 50\\%$ or $n = 1$).\n\n4. Observable Reviewer Console Contracts:\n   - Produce a structured audit verdict for every summary:\n     `{ summaryId, status: \""APPROVED\"" | \""FLAGGED\"" | \""BLOCKED\"", riskScore, findings: [ { ruleId, severity, message, evidencePaths, remediationSuggestion } ] }`.\n   - Never leak raw unmasked comments in telemetry, error payloads, or public API responses.\n\n---\n\n### Phased Implementation Plan\n\nWork step-by-step. Do not rush to output all code at once:\n\n- Step 1: Data Contracts & Invariant Rules. Define the schema interfaces, error taxonomy, and threshold configs ($k$-anonymity limits, sensitive lexicons, quantifier rules).\n- Step 2: Verification Core (Pure Logic). Implement the evaluation pipeline as pure functions with zero I/O side effects:\n  - `CohortSizeGuard`\n  - `QuasiIdentifierSanitizer`\n  - `ClaimGroundingEvaluator`\n- Step 3: End-to-End Orchestrator. Wire the pipeline against the actual test scenarios (`Mobile` re-identification, `Payments` burnout disclosure, and `Payments` remote-work exaggeration).\n- Step 4: Verification Test Suite. Write automated assertions verifying that all 3 known security/hallucination traps are correctly intercepted with clear, machine-readable finding codes.\n\nBegin by delivering Step 1: Formalize the TypeScript / Python data models and the Invariant Rule definitions.""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\""message\"":\""Implemented Step 1 as a pure domain layer: strict runtime data contracts, audit/error taxonomy, threshold/privacy configs, and invariant rule definitions. Assumption: because this project is currently JS-only and dependencies are constrained, I used JavaScript modules with JSDoc-style contracts and deterministic runtime validation rather than adding TypeScript tooling. Nothing visible changes in the preview yet; these files are ready for Step 2 verification logic.\"",\""files\"":[{\""path\"":\""src/domain/policyConfig.js\"",\""contents\"":\""export const SEVERITY = Object.freeze({\\n  INFO: \\\""INFO\\\"",\\n  LOW: \\\""LOW\\\"",\\n  MEDIUM: \\\""MEDIUM\\\"",\\n  HIGH: \\\""HIGH\\\"",\\n  CRITICAL: \\\""CRITICAL\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const AUDIT_STATUS = Object.freeze({\\n  APPROVED: \\\""APPROVED\\\"",\\n  FLAGGED: \\\""FLAGGED\\\"",\\n  BLOCKED: \\\""BLOCKED\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const FINDING_CATEGORY = Object.freeze({\\n  SCHEMA: \\\""SCHEMA\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT: \\\""INVARIANT\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY: \\\""PRIVACY\\\"",\\n  CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS: \\\""CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS\\\"",\\n  DATA_SCOPE: \\\""DATA_SCOPE\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const RULE_IDS = Object.freeze({\\n  SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS: \\\""SCHEMA.EXACT_KEYS\\\"",\\n  SCHEMA_TYPE: \\\""SCHEMA.TYPE\\\"",\\n  SCHEMA_ENUM: \\\""SCHEMA.ENUM\\\"",\\n  SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING: \\\""SCHEMA.NON_EMPTY_STRING\\\"",\\n\\n  INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID: \\\""INVARIANT.DUPLICATE_ID\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT: \\\""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM: \\\""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_TEAM\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT: \\\""INVARIANT.EMPTY_COMMENT\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP: \\\""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE: \\\""INVARIANT.EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE\\\"",\\n\\n  SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED: \\\""SCOPE.CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED\\\"",\\n\\n  PRIVACY_COHORT_TOO_SMALL: \\\""PRIVACY.COHORT_TOO_SMALL\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY_DIRECT_PII: \\\""PRIVACY.DIRECT_PII\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY_QUASI_IDENTIFIER: \\\""PRIVACY.QUASI_IDENTIFIER\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY_SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION: \\\""PRIVACY.SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION\\\"",\\n\\n  CLAIM_UNSUPPORTED: \\\""CLAIM.UNSUPPORTED\\\"",\\n  CLAIM_FREQUENCY_MISMATCH: \\\""CLAIM.FREQUENCY_MISMATCH\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const POLICY_CONFIG = Object.freeze({\\n  anonymity: Object.freeze({\\n    minCohortResponses: 5,\\n    minSupportingResponsesForAttributableClaim: 2,\\n  }),\\n\\n  pii: Object.freeze({\\n    email: /\\\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\\\b/gi,\\n    australianPhone: /(?:\\\\+?61|0)\\\\s?(?:2|3|4|7|8)\\\\s?(?:\\\\d\\\\s?){8}\\\\b/g,\\n    employeeId: /\\\\b(?:employee|emp|staff|worker)[-\\\\s_]*id[:#]?\\\\s*[A-Z0-9-]{4,}\\\\b/gi,\\n    taxFileNumberLike: /\\\\b\\\\d{3}\\\\s?\\\\d{3}\\\\s?\\\\d{3}\\\\b/g,\\n  }),\\n\\n  quasiIdentifiers: Object.freeze({\\n    locationTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""perth\\\"",\\n      \\\""sydney\\\"",\\n      \\\""melbourne\\\"",\\n      \\\""brisbane\\\"",\\n      \\\""adelaide\\\"",\\n      \\\""office\\\"",\\n      \\\""site\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n    singlePersonRoleTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""lead\\\"",\\n      \\\""owner\\\"",\\n      \\\""only person\\\"",\\n      \\\""sole\\\"",\\n      \\\""alone\\\"",\\n      \\\""single person\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n    narrowWorkTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""atlas migration\\\"",\\n      \\\""overnight reconciliation\\\"",\\n      \\\""rota\\\"",\\n      \\\""on-call\\\"",\\n      \\\""migration\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n  }),\\n\\n  sensitiveAttributes: Object.freeze({\\n    wellbeingTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""burning out\\\"",\\n      \\\""burnout\\\"",\\n      \\\""wearing me down\\\"",\\n      \\\""exhausting\\\"",\\n      \\\""stressful\\\"",\\n      \\\""mental health\\\"",\\n      \\\""health\\\"",\\n      \\\""wellbeing\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n    attributionTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""one engineer\\\"",\\n      \\\""only person\\\"",\\n      \\\""alone\\\"",\\n      \\\""sole\\\"",\\n      \\\""single person\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n  }),\\n\\n  quantifiers: Object.freeze([\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""almost everyone\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.8, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""everyone\\\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""unanimously\\\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""most\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.6, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""consistently\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""many\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\\n  ]),\\n});\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/domain/contracts.js\"",\""contents\"":\""import { FINDING_CATEGORY, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \\\""./policyConfig.js\\\"";\\n\\nconst GROUP_TYPES = Object.freeze([\\\""team\\\"", \\\""department\\\""]);\\n\\nexport function makeValidationIssue({\\n  ruleId,\\n  severity = SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n  category = FINDING_CATEGORY.SCHEMA,\\n  message,\\n  path,\\n  expected,\\n  actual,\\n}) {\\n  return {\\n    ruleId,\\n    severity,\\n    category,\\n    message,\\n    path,\\n    expected,\\n    actual,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction isPlainObject(value) {\\n  return Object.prototype.toString.call(value) === \\\""[object Object]\\\"";\\n}\\n\\nfunction describeType(value) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return \\\""array\\\"";\\n  if (value === null) return \\\""null\\\"";\\n  return typeof value;\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateExactKeys(value, expectedKeys, path, issues) {\\n  if (!isPlainObject(value)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path} must be an object with an exact schema.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""plain object\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  const actualKeys = Object.keys(value).sort();\\n  const sortedExpected = [...expectedKeys].sort();\\n  const missing = sortedExpected.filter((key) => !actualKeys.includes(key));\\n  const unexpected = actualKeys.filter((key) => !sortedExpected.includes(key));\\n\\n  if (missing.length > 0 || unexpected.length > 0) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS,\\n        message: `${path} has schema key mismatch.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: sortedExpected,\\n        actual: actualKeys,\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return missing.length === 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateString(value, path, issues, { allowEmpty = false } = {}) {\\n  if (typeof value !== \\\""string\\\"") {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path} must be a string.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""string\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!allowEmpty && value.trim().length === 0) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING,\\n        message: `${path} must be a non-empty string.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""non-empty string\\\"",\\n        actual: value,\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateStringArray(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path} must be an array of strings.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  value.forEach((item, index) => {\\n    validateString(item, `${path}[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateDepartment(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""name\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateTeam(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""name\\\"", \\\""departmentId\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.departmentId, `${path}.departmentId`, issues);\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateResponse(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""teamId\\\"", \\\""comment\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.teamId, `${path}.teamId`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.comment, `${path}.comment`, issues, { allowEmpty: true });\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateTheme(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""title\\\"", \\\""summary\\\"", \\\""claims\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.title, `${path}.title`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.summary, `${path}.summary`, issues);\\n  validateStringArray(value.claims, `${path}.claims`, issues);\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateSummary(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""groupType\\\"", \\\""groupId\\\"", \\\""themes\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.groupType, `${path}.groupType`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.groupId, `${path}.groupId`, issues);\\n\\n  if (typeof value.groupType === \\\""string\\\"" && !GROUP_TYPES.includes(value.groupType)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_ENUM,\\n        message: `${path}.groupType must be one of the supported summary scopes.`,\\n        path: `${path}.groupType`,\\n        expected: GROUP_TYPES,\\n        actual: value.groupType,\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(value.themes)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path}.themes must be an array.`,\\n        path: `${path}.themes`,\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value.themes),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  value.themes.forEach((theme, index) => {\\n    validateTheme(theme, `${path}.themes[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateOrgContract(org) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(org, [\\\""departments\\\"", \\\""teams\\\""], \\\""teams\\\"", issues)) {\\n    return { valid: false, issues };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.departments)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""teams.departments must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""teams.departments\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(org.departments),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  } else {\\n    org.departments.forEach((department, index) => {\\n      validateDepartment(department, `teams.departments[${index}]`, issues);\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.teams)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""teams.teams must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""teams.teams\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(org.teams),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  } else {\\n    org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\\n      validateTeam(team, `teams.teams[${index}]`, issues);\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateResponsesContract(responses) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(responses)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""responses must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""responses\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(responses),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return { valid: false, issues };\\n  }\\n\\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\\n    validateResponse(response, `responses[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateSummariesContract(summaries) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(summaries)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""summaries must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""summaries\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(summaries),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return { valid: false, issues };\\n  }\\n\\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\\n    validateSummary(summary, `summaries[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries }) {\\n  const results = [\\n    validateOrgContract(org),\\n    validateResponsesContract(responses),\\n    validateSummariesContract(summaries),\\n  ];\\n\\n  const issues = results.flatMap((result) => result.issues);\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/domain/invariants.js\"",\""contents\"":\""import { makeValidationIssue, validateDataContracts } from \\\""./contracts.js\\\"";\\nimport { FINDING_CATEGORY, POLICY_CONFIG, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \\\""./policyConfig.js\\\"";\\n\\nfunction buildDuplicateIdIssues(records, path, entityName) {\\n  const seen = new Map();\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  records.forEach((record, index) => {\\n    if (typeof record?.id !== \\\""string\\\"") return;\\n\\n    if (seen.has(record.id)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Duplicate ${entityName} id '${record.id}' detected.`,\\n          path: `${path}[${index}].id`,\\n          expected: \\\""globally unique id within collection\\\"",\\n          actual: record.id,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    seen.set(record.id, index);\\n  });\\n\\n  return issues;\\n}\\n\\nexport function getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org) {\\n  if (summary.groupType === \\\""team\\\"") {\\n    const team = org.teams.find((candidate) => candidate.id === summary.groupId);\\n    return team ? [team.id] : [];\\n  }\\n\\n  if (summary.groupType === \\\""department\\\"") {\\n    return org.teams\\n      .filter((team) => team.departmentId === summary.groupId)\\n      .map((team) => team.id);\\n  }\\n\\n  return [];\\n}\\n\\nexport function getDepartmentIdForTeam(teamId, org) {\\n  return org.teams.find((team) => team.id === teamId)?.departmentId ?? null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateEvidenceWithinSummaryScope({ summary, evidenceTeamIds, org, path }) {\\n  const allowedTeamIds = new Set(getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org));\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  evidenceTeamIds.forEach((teamId, index) => {\\n    if (!allowedTeamIds.has(teamId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.CRITICAL,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.DATA_SCOPE,\\n          message: `Evidence team '${teamId}' is outside summary '${summary.id}' scope.`,\\n          path: `${path}.evidenceTeamIds[${index}]`,\\n          expected: [...allowedTeamIds],\\n          actual: teamId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  return issues;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries }) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n  const departmentIds = new Set(org.departments.map((department) => department.id));\\n  const teamIds = new Set(org.teams.map((team) => team.id));\\n\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.departments, \\\""teams.departments\\\"", \\\""department\\\""));\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.teams, \\\""teams.teams\\\"", \\\""team\\\""));\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(responses, \\\""responses\\\"", \\\""response\\\""));\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(summaries, \\\""summaries\\\"", \\\""summary\\\""));\\n\\n  org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\\n    if (!departmentIds.has(team.departmentId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Team '${team.id}' references unknown department '${team.departmentId}'.`,\\n          path: `teams.teams[${index}].departmentId`,\\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\\n          actual: team.departmentId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\\n    if (!teamIds.has(response.teamId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' references unknown team '${response.teamId}'.`,\\n          path: `responses[${index}].teamId`,\\n          expected: [...teamIds],\\n          actual: response.teamId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    if (typeof response.comment === \\\""string\\\"" && response.comment.trim().length === 0) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.INFO,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' has an empty comment and must not be used as text evidence.`,\\n          path: `responses[${index}].comment`,\\n          expected: \\\""non-empty comment for claim evidence\\\"",\\n          actual: \\\""\\\"",\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\\n    const path = `summaries[${index}]`;\\n\\n    if (summary.groupType === \\\""team\\\"" && !teamIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown team '${summary.groupId}'.`,\\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\\n          expected: [...teamIds],\\n          actual: summary.groupId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    if (summary.groupType === \\\""department\\\"" && !departmentIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown department '${summary.groupId}'.`,\\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\\n          actual: summary.groupId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    const scopedTeamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\\n    if ((summary.groupType === \\\""team\\\"" || summary.groupType === \\\""department\\\"") && scopedTeamIds.length === 0) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' has no valid response scope.`,\\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\\n          expected: \\\""at least one team in summary scope\\\"",\\n          actual: summary.groupId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.every((issue) => issue.severity === SEVERITY.INFO), issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function getResponseCountsByTeam(responses) {\\n  return responses.reduce((counts, response) => {\\n    counts[response.teamId] ??= { total: 0, nonEmpty: 0 };\\n    counts[response.teamId].total += 1;\\n\\n    if (typeof response.comment === \\\""string\\\"" && response.comment.trim().length > 0) {\\n      counts[response.teamId].nonEmpty += 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    return counts;\\n  }, {});\\n}\\n\\nexport function getCohortPolicyForSummary(summary, org, responses, config = POLICY_CONFIG) {\\n  const teamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\\n  const responseCounts = getResponseCountsByTeam(responses);\\n  const totalResponses = teamIds.reduce((total, teamId) => {\\n    return total + (responseCounts[teamId]?.total ?? 0);\\n  }, 0);\\n\\n  return {\\n    summaryId: summary.id,\\n    scopedTeamIds: teamIds,\\n    responseCount: totalResponses,\\n    minRequiredResponses: config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\\n    publishable: totalResponses >= config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateDatasetReadiness({ org, responses, summaries }) {\\n  const contractResult = validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries });\\n\\n  if (!contractResult.valid) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      issues: contractResult.issues,\\n      stage: \\\""contract\\\"",\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const invariantResult = validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries });\\n  return {\\n    valid: invariantResult.valid,\\n    issues: invariantResult.issues,\\n    stage: \\\""invariant\\\"",\\n  };\\n}\\n\""}],\""reasoning\"":\""The user asked to begin Step 1 only, so I avoided building the verification pipeline/UI/tests. I created strict runtime schemas, enumerated rule IDs and severities, privacy threshold config, and invariant helpers including summary scoping and cohort policy primitives for Step 2. I used JS modules rather than adding TypeScript because the current workspace has no TS setup and dependency additions are constrained.\""}"",""refusal"":null,""annotations"":[],""parsed"":{""message"":""Implemented Step 1 as a pure domain layer: strict runtime data contracts, audit/error taxonomy, threshold/privacy configs, and invariant rule definitions. Assumption: because this project is currently JS-only and dependencies are constrained, I used JavaScript modules with JSDoc-style contracts and deterministic runtime validation rather than adding TypeScript tooling. Nothing visible changes in the preview yet; these files are ready for Step 2 verification logic."",""files"":[{""path"":""src/domain/policyConfig.js"",""contents"":""export const SEVERITY = Object.freeze({\n  INFO: \""INFO\"",\n  LOW: \""LOW\"",\n  MEDIUM: \""MEDIUM\"",\n  HIGH: \""HIGH\"",\n  CRITICAL: \""CRITICAL\"",\n});\n\nexport const AUDIT_STATUS = Object.freeze({\n  APPROVED: \""APPROVED\"",\n  FLAGGED: \""FLAGGED\"",\n  BLOCKED: \""BLOCKED\"",\n});\n\nexport const FINDING_CATEGORY = Object.freeze({\n  SCHEMA: \""SCHEMA\"",\n  INVARIANT: \""INVARIANT\"",\n  PRIVACY: \""PRIVACY\"",\n  CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS: \""CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS\"",\n  DATA_SCOPE: \""DATA_SCOPE\"",\n});\n\nexport const RULE_IDS = Object.freeze({\n  SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS: \""SCHEMA.EXACT_KEYS\"",\n  SCHEMA_TYPE: \""SCHEMA.TYPE\"",\n  SCHEMA_ENUM: \""SCHEMA.ENUM\"",\n  SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING: \""SCHEMA.NON_EMPTY_STRING\"",\n\n  INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID: \""INVARIANT.DUPLICATE_ID\"",\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT: \""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT\"",\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM: \""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_TEAM\"",\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT: \""INVARIANT.EMPTY_COMMENT\"",\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP: \""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP\"",\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE: \""INVARIANT.EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE\"",\n\n  SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED: \""SCOPE.CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED\"",\n\n  PRIVACY_COHORT_TOO_SMALL: \""PRIVACY.COHORT_TOO_SMALL\"",\n  PRIVACY_DIRECT_PII: \""PRIVACY.DIRECT_PII\"",\n  PRIVACY_QUASI_IDENTIFIER: \""PRIVACY.QUASI_IDENTIFIER\"",\n  PRIVACY_SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION: \""PRIVACY.SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION\"",\n\n  CLAIM_UNSUPPORTED: \""CLAIM.UNSUPPORTED\"",\n  CLAIM_FREQUENCY_MISMATCH: \""CLAIM.FREQUENCY_MISMATCH\"",\n});\n\nexport const POLICY_CONFIG = Object.freeze({\n  anonymity: Object.freeze({\n    minCohortResponses: 5,\n    minSupportingResponsesForAttributableClaim: 2,\n  }),\n\n  pii: Object.freeze({\n    email: /\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\b/gi,\n    australianPhone: /(?:\\+?61|0)\\s?(?:2|3|4|7|8)\\s?(?:\\d\\s?){8}\\b/g,\n    employeeId: /\\b(?:employee|emp|staff|worker)[-\\s_]*id[:#]?\\s*[A-Z0-9-]{4,}\\b/gi,\n    taxFileNumberLike: /\\b\\d{3}\\s?\\d{3}\\s?\\d{3}\\b/g,\n  }),\n\n  quasiIdentifiers: Object.freeze({\n    locationTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""perth\"",\n      \""sydney\"",\n      \""melbourne\"",\n      \""brisbane\"",\n      \""adelaide\"",\n      \""office\"",\n      \""site\"",\n    ]),\n    singlePersonRoleTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""lead\"",\n      \""owner\"",\n      \""only person\"",\n      \""sole\"",\n      \""alone\"",\n      \""single person\"",\n    ]),\n    narrowWorkTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""atlas migration\"",\n      \""overnight reconciliation\"",\n      \""rota\"",\n      \""on-call\"",\n      \""migration\"",\n    ]),\n  }),\n\n  sensitiveAttributes: Object.freeze({\n    wellbeingTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""burning out\"",\n      \""burnout\"",\n      \""wearing me down\"",\n      \""exhausting\"",\n      \""stressful\"",\n      \""mental health\"",\n      \""health\"",\n      \""wellbeing\"",\n    ]),\n    attributionTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""one engineer\"",\n      \""only person\"",\n      \""alone\"",\n      \""sole\"",\n      \""single person\"",\n    ]),\n  }),\n\n  quantifiers: Object.freeze([\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""almost everyone\"", minSupportRatio: 0.8, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""everyone\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""unanimously\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""most\"", minSupportRatio: 0.6, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""consistently\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""many\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\n  ]),\n});\n""},{""path"":""src/domain/contracts.js"",""contents"":""import { FINDING_CATEGORY, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \""./policyConfig.js\"";\n\nconst GROUP_TYPES = Object.freeze([\""team\"", \""department\""]);\n\nexport function makeValidationIssue({\n  ruleId,\n  severity = SEVERITY.HIGH,\n  category = FINDING_CATEGORY.SCHEMA,\n  message,\n  path,\n  expected,\n  actual,\n}) {\n  return {\n    ruleId,\n    severity,\n    category,\n    message,\n    path,\n    expected,\n    actual,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction isPlainObject(value) {\n  return Object.prototype.toString.call(value) === \""[object Object]\"";\n}\n\nfunction describeType(value) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return \""array\"";\n  if (value === null) return \""null\"";\n  return typeof value;\n}\n\nfunction validateExactKeys(value, expectedKeys, path, issues) {\n  if (!isPlainObject(value)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path} must be an object with an exact schema.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""plain object\"",\n        actual: describeType(value),\n      }),\n    );\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const actualKeys = Object.keys(value).sort();\n  const sortedExpected = [...expectedKeys].sort();\n  const missing = sortedExpected.filter((key) => !actualKeys.includes(key));\n  const unexpected = actualKeys.filter((key) => !sortedExpected.includes(key));\n\n  if (missing.length > 0 || unexpected.length > 0) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS,\n        message: `${path} has schema key mismatch.`,\n        path,\n        expected: sortedExpected,\n        actual: actualKeys,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  return missing.length === 0;\n}\n\nfunction validateString(value, path, issues, { allowEmpty = false } = {}) {\n  if (typeof value !== \""string\"") {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path} must be a string.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""string\"",\n        actual: describeType(value),\n      }),\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!allowEmpty && value.trim().length === 0) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING,\n        message: `${path} must be a non-empty string.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""non-empty string\"",\n        actual: value,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateStringArray(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path} must be an array of strings.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(value),\n      }),\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n\n  value.forEach((item, index) => {\n    validateString(item, `${path}[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction validateDepartment(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""name\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\n}\n\nfunction validateTeam(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""name\"", \""departmentId\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\n  validateString(value.departmentId, `${path}.departmentId`, issues);\n}\n\nfunction validateResponse(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""teamId\"", \""comment\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.teamId, `${path}.teamId`, issues);\n  validateString(value.comment, `${path}.comment`, issues, { allowEmpty: true });\n}\n\nfunction validateTheme(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""title\"", \""summary\"", \""claims\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.title, `${path}.title`, issues);\n  validateString(value.summary, `${path}.summary`, issues);\n  validateStringArray(value.claims, `${path}.claims`, issues);\n}\n\nfunction validateSummary(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""groupType\"", \""groupId\"", \""themes\""], path, issues)) return;\n\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.groupType, `${path}.groupType`, issues);\n  validateString(value.groupId, `${path}.groupId`, issues);\n\n  if (typeof value.groupType === \""string\"" && !GROUP_TYPES.includes(value.groupType)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_ENUM,\n        message: `${path}.groupType must be one of the supported summary scopes.`,\n        path: `${path}.groupType`,\n        expected: GROUP_TYPES,\n        actual: value.groupType,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(value.themes)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path}.themes must be an array.`,\n        path: `${path}.themes`,\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(value.themes),\n      }),\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n\n  value.themes.forEach((theme, index) => {\n    validateTheme(theme, `${path}.themes[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n}\n\nexport function validateOrgContract(org) {\n  const issues = [];\n\n  if (!validateExactKeys(org, [\""departments\"", \""teams\""], \""teams\"", issues)) {\n    return { valid: false, issues };\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.departments)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""teams.departments must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""teams.departments\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(org.departments),\n      }),\n    );\n  } else {\n    org.departments.forEach((department, index) => {\n      validateDepartment(department, `teams.departments[${index}]`, issues);\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.teams)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""teams.teams must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""teams.teams\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(org.teams),\n      }),\n    );\n  } else {\n    org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\n      validateTeam(team, `teams.teams[${index}]`, issues);\n    });\n  }\n\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n\nexport function validateResponsesContract(responses) {\n  const issues = [];\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(responses)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""responses must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""responses\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(responses),\n      }),\n    );\n    return { valid: false, issues };\n  }\n\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\n    validateResponse(response, `responses[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n\nexport function validateSummariesContract(summaries) {\n  const issues = [];\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(summaries)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""summaries must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""summaries\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(summaries),\n      }),\n    );\n    return { valid: false, issues };\n  }\n\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\n    validateSummary(summary, `summaries[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n\nexport function validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries }) {\n  const results = [\n    validateOrgContract(org),\n    validateResponsesContract(responses),\n    validateSummariesContract(summaries),\n  ];\n\n  const issues = results.flatMap((result) => result.issues);\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n""},{""path"":""src/domain/invariants.js"",""contents"":""import { makeValidationIssue, validateDataContracts } from \""./contracts.js\"";\nimport { FINDING_CATEGORY, POLICY_CONFIG, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \""./policyConfig.js\"";\n\nfunction buildDuplicateIdIssues(records, path, entityName) {\n  const seen = new Map();\n  const issues = [];\n\n  records.forEach((record, index) => {\n    if (typeof record?.id !== \""string\"") return;\n\n    if (seen.has(record.id)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Duplicate ${entityName} id '${record.id}' detected.`,\n          path: `${path}[${index}].id`,\n          expected: \""globally unique id within collection\"",\n          actual: record.id,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    seen.set(record.id, index);\n  });\n\n  return issues;\n}\n\nexport function getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org) {\n  if (summary.groupType === \""team\"") {\n    const team = org.teams.find((candidate) => candidate.id === summary.groupId);\n    return team ? [team.id] : [];\n  }\n\n  if (summary.groupType === \""department\"") {\n    return org.teams\n      .filter((team) => team.departmentId === summary.groupId)\n      .map((team) => team.id);\n  }\n\n  return [];\n}\n\nexport function getDepartmentIdForTeam(teamId, org) {\n  return org.teams.find((team) => team.id === teamId)?.departmentId ?? null;\n}\n\nexport function validateEvidenceWithinSummaryScope({ summary, evidenceTeamIds, org, path }) {\n  const allowedTeamIds = new Set(getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org));\n  const issues = [];\n\n  evidenceTeamIds.forEach((teamId, index) => {\n    if (!allowedTeamIds.has(teamId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED,\n          severity: SEVERITY.CRITICAL,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.DATA_SCOPE,\n          message: `Evidence team '${teamId}' is outside summary '${summary.id}' scope.`,\n          path: `${path}.evidenceTeamIds[${index}]`,\n          expected: [...allowedTeamIds],\n          actual: teamId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  return issues;\n}\n\nexport function validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries }) {\n  const issues = [];\n  const departmentIds = new Set(org.departments.map((department) => department.id));\n  const teamIds = new Set(org.teams.map((team) => team.id));\n\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.departments, \""teams.departments\"", \""department\""));\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.teams, \""teams.teams\"", \""team\""));\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(responses, \""responses\"", \""response\""));\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(summaries, \""summaries\"", \""summary\""));\n\n  org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\n    if (!departmentIds.has(team.departmentId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Team '${team.id}' references unknown department '${team.departmentId}'.`,\n          path: `teams.teams[${index}].departmentId`,\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\n          actual: team.departmentId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\n    if (!teamIds.has(response.teamId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' references unknown team '${response.teamId}'.`,\n          path: `responses[${index}].teamId`,\n          expected: [...teamIds],\n          actual: response.teamId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    if (typeof response.comment === \""string\"" && response.comment.trim().length === 0) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT,\n          severity: SEVERITY.INFO,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' has an empty comment and must not be used as text evidence.`,\n          path: `responses[${index}].comment`,\n          expected: \""non-empty comment for claim evidence\"",\n          actual: \""\"",\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\n    const path = `summaries[${index}]`;\n\n    if (summary.groupType === \""team\"" && !teamIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown team '${summary.groupId}'.`,\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\n          expected: [...teamIds],\n          actual: summary.groupId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    if (summary.groupType === \""department\"" && !departmentIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown department '${summary.groupId}'.`,\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\n          actual: summary.groupId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    const scopedTeamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\n    if ((summary.groupType === \""team\"" || summary.groupType === \""department\"") && scopedTeamIds.length === 0) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' has no valid response scope.`,\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\n          expected: \""at least one team in summary scope\"",\n          actual: summary.groupId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  return { valid: issues.every((issue) => issue.severity === SEVERITY.INFO), issues };\n}\n\nexport function getResponseCountsByTeam(responses) {\n  return responses.reduce((counts, response) => {\n    counts[response.teamId] ??= { total: 0, nonEmpty: 0 };\n    counts[response.teamId].total += 1;\n\n    if (typeof response.comment === \""string\"" && response.comment.trim().length > 0) {\n      counts[response.teamId].nonEmpty += 1;\n    }\n\n    return counts;\n  }, {});\n}\n\nexport function getCohortPolicyForSummary(summary, org, responses, config = POLICY_CONFIG) {\n  const teamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\n  const responseCounts = getResponseCountsByTeam(responses);\n  const totalResponses = teamIds.reduce((total, teamId) => {\n    return total + (responseCounts[teamId]?.total ?? 0);\n  }, 0);\n\n  return {\n    summaryId: summary.id,\n    scopedTeamIds: teamIds,\n    responseCount: totalResponses,\n    minRequiredResponses: config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\n    publishable: totalResponses >= config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function validateDatasetReadiness({ org, responses, summaries }) {\n  const contractResult = validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries });\n\n  if (!contractResult.valid) {\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      issues: contractResult.issues,\n      stage: \""contract\"",\n    };\n  }\n\n  const invariantResult = validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries });\n  return {\n    valid: invariantResult.valid,\n    issues: invariantResult.issues,\n    stage: \""invariant\"",\n  };\n}\n""}],""reasoning"":""The user asked to begin Step 1 only, so I avoided building the verification pipeline/UI/tests. I created strict runtime schemas, enumerated rule IDs and severities, privacy threshold config, and invariant helpers including summary scoping and cohort policy primitives for Step 2. I used JS modules rather than adding TypeScript because the current workspace has no TS setup and dependency additions are constrained.""}}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_schema\"",\""json_schema\"":{\""name\"":\""assistant_output\"",\""strict\"":true,\""schema\"":{\""$schema\"":\""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""message\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""},\""files\"":{\""type\"":\""array\"",\""items\"":{\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""path\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""},\""contents\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""}},\""required\"":[\""path\"",\""contents\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false},\""description\"":\""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""},\""reasoning\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""}},\""required\"":[\""message\"",\""files\"",\""reasoning\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false}}}"",""turnSeq"":""5"",""challengeTitle"":""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","52014","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","c91ed571cd62c2e3b899615cfde5183f81e7f4ba","t-387570f2-c22b-43fc-9f67-53c99c5bef07","[]"
"t-387570f2-c22b-43fc-9f67-53c99c5bef07","387570f2-c22b-43fc-9f67-53c99c5bef07","ai_stage:assistant","SPAN","ai_stage:assistant","2026-09-28 04:37:00.949000","","","default","","candidate-1","rsri7n9d9d4ij1ii7boywd8o","DEFAULT","","","","","","","{}","{}","{}","0","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for BlueScope.\n\n# Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\n\n## Context & Objectives\nBuild a production-grade service module for **BlueScope** that handles workflow events, enforces strict data scoping, and guarantees compliance with the Australian Privacy Act 1988.\n\n## Constraints\n1. **PII Masking**: Ensure phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses are masked prior to persistence.\n2. **Deterministic Validation**: Validate all inputs using strict schema boundaries.\n3. **Observable Verification**: Provide clear error reasons when input fails domain invariants.\n</challenge>""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""can you help me explain the data given in the json?""},{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""The JSON data represents a synthetic employee survey review dataset. I haven’t changed any files.\n\n- `teams.json` defines the organisation structure: departments and the teams inside them.\n- `responses.json` contains individual survey responses, one per respondent. Each response has an `id`, a `teamId`, and a free-text `comment`. Some comments are empty.\n- `summaries.json` contains AI-generated summary outputs for teams or departments. Each summary includes themes, summaries, and specific claims the AI is making.\n\nImportant: the summaries are not guaranteed to be correct. Some claims appear well-supported by the raw responses, while others look exaggerated, unsupported, or privacy-sensitive. This dataset is likely intended for building a reviewer console that lets humans check whether AI summaries are accurate and safe before use.""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""give me a little stat about the data at least? is there any security concern?""},{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""Here are a few quick stats from the JSON, plus security/privacy observations. I didn’t change any files.\n\nStats:\n- 2 departments: Engineering and Customer Success.\n- 5 teams total.\n- 29 survey responses.\n- 23 responses contain comments; 6 are blank.\n- Team response counts:\n  - Payments: 9 responses, 7 with comments.\n  - Platform: 8 responses, 6 with comments.\n  - Mobile: 3 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Onboarding: 5 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Support: 4 responses, 4 with comments.\n- 6 AI summaries total: 5 team summaries and 1 Engineering department summary.\n- 12 summary themes total.\n\nPotential security/privacy concerns:\n- The dataset is synthetic, but it contains examples of potentially identifying details.\n- The Mobile comment and summary mention “Perth office”, “lead”, and “Atlas migration”. In a small team of only 3 responses, that could identify a specific person.\n- The Payments wellbeing summary says “One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.” That is sensitive wellbeing information and may identify someone if the rota is known.\n- Small groups are risky: Mobile has only 3 responses, and some claims are based on a single comment. Summaries for small teams should probably be suppressed, generalised, or flagged for reviewer approval.\n- Some summaries appear unsupported or exaggerated, e.g. Payments says “Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,” but only one comment says remote days are great.\n- There are no obvious phone numbers, emails, or national IDs in the current data, but a real system should still mask those before saving or displaying comments.\n\nIn short: the biggest concern is not classic credentials/security leakage, but privacy leakage through small-group comments, wellbeing details, location/project references, and unsupported AI claims.""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Reviewer console — starter data\n\nYou are prototyping a reviewer console for an AI feature that summarises employee\nsurvey comments. Everything here is **synthetic**: invented people, teams and\ncomments for a fictional company.\n\n## Data (`src/data/`)\n\n- `teams.json` — `departments` and `teams`. Each team belongs to one department.\n- `responses.json` — one entry per **respondent**: `{ id, teamId, comment }`.\n  `comment` may be an empty string.\n- `summaries.json` — output of a (stubbed) LLM summariser. Each summary covers a\n  `team` or a `department` (`groupType` / `groupId`) and has `themes`; each theme\n  has a `title`, a `summary` and the `claims` it makes.\n\nImport them directly, e.g. `import teams from \""./data/teams.json\""`.\n\n## Running\n\nThe preview is already live. Edit `src/App.jsx` and add files under `src/`.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Your project starts here</h1>\n      <p>\n        Nothing has been built yet. Describe what you want in the chat and the\n        assistant will write the code.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/data/responses.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r01\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Release train is monthly and everything piles in the last week. Rollback ownership is unclear, it feels like nobody's job.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r02\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I like my team but the monthly release crunch is exhausting.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r03\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would love clear rollback ownership when a release goes wrong.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r04\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Deploys are fine. Wish we had more time for tech debt.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r05\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Remote days are great, I'd happily do more of them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r06\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r07\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Being the only person on the overnight reconciliation rota is wearing me down.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r08\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r09\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good team. Tech debt keeps getting pushed.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r10\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call is heavy and alerts are noisy.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r11\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Alert noise at night is the worst part of on-call.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r12\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I'd like a clearer path to senior.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r13\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Planning is good this quarter, priorities finally feel stable.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r14\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r15\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Too many meetings on Tuesdays and Thursdays.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r16\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r17\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call rota fairness could be better, same few people get paged.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r18\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Since I moved from the Perth office to lead the Atlas migration I've had no backup.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r19\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""App store approvals take forever and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r20\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Love the team, worried about headcount.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r21\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Customers get stuck at the data import step and the docs are out of date, so we field the same questions daily.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r22\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r23\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Import step is confusing for customers and the docs are out of date.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r24\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r25\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would like more time with customers rather than internal meetings.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r26\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket volume spikes after every release.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r27\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r28\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good tooling, but escalation paths are unclear.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r29\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Enjoy the work, wish escalation to engineering was faster.\""\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/summaries.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-payments\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release pressure\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Engineers feel the monthly release train creates a last-week crunch, and rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Working pattern\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Almost everyone in the team wants to work fully remotely.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Wellbeing\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Tech debt\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-platform\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call is heavy, alerts are noisy, and the load falls on the same few people.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy, especially at night.\"",\n          \""The same few people get paged.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Meetings\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Career growth\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""People want a clearer path to senior.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""People want a clearer path to senior.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-mobile\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Migration ownership\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release approvals\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-onboarding\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Import step\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Customers struggle with the data import step and the docs are out of date.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Customers struggle with the data import step.\"",\n          \""The docs are out of date.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-support\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Post-release load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Ticket volume and backlog spike after releases.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Ticket volume spikes after releases.\"",\n          \""The ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Escalation\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Escalation paths to engineering are unclear and slow.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Escalation paths are unclear.\"",\n          \""Escalation to engineering is slow.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-engineering\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""department\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""engineering\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release and rollout friction\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""A monthly release crunch, unclear rollback ownership, and slow app store approvals that nobody owns.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call load is heavy and alerts are noisy.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call load is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/teams.json ===\n{\n  \""departments\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""engineering\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""customer-success\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Customer Success\""\n    }\n  ],\n  \""teams\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""payments\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Payments\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""platform\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Platform\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""mobile\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Mobile\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""onboarding\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Onboarding\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""support\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Support\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\nAct as a Principal AI Safety & Systems Architect specializing in enterprise privacy, human-in-the-loop (HITL) audit systems, and natural language verification.\n\n### System Overview & Context\nWe are engineering an automated review, verification, and sanitization engine for an enterprise employee survey platform. The system ingests raw survey data alongside AI-generated summaries and flags compliance violations, privacy risks, and hallucinations before any summary is published to leadership.\n\n### Input Data Topography\nThe system operates on three existing JSON datasets:\n1. `teams.json`: Org hierarchy defining departments (Engineering, Customer Success) and nested teams (Payments, Platform, Mobile, Onboarding, Support).\n2. `responses.json`: 29 raw survey records (`id`, `teamId`, free-text `comment`), including empty comments (6 records) and valid comments (23 records).\n3. `summaries.json`: 6 AI-generated summaries (5 team-level, 1 department-level) containing 12 themes, executive narratives, and discrete claims.\n\n### Identified Critical Vulnerabilities in Current Data\nOur system must catch and programmatically flag known anti-patterns present in this dataset:\n1. Re-identification via Small Cohorts & Quasi-Identifiers:\n   - The Mobile team has only 3 responses ($n=3$).\n   - Comments/summaries reference narrow quasi-identifiers (\""Perth office\"", \""lead\"", \""Atlas migration\""), creating extreme deanonymization risk.\n2. Sensitive Wellbeing & Attributable Disclosure:\n   - The Payments summary explicitly leaks: \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"" This attributes sensitive mental health/burnout state to a known, single-person operational role.\n3. Unsupported Claims & Frequency Hallucinations:\n   - The Payments summary claims \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,\"" despite only a single raw response mentioning remote work.\n4. Data Scoping & Rollup Boundary Breaches:\n   - Department summaries aggregating or leaking un-redacted team-specific identifiable claims.\n\n---\n\n### Core Objectives & Architecture Requirements\n\nYou will design and implement the backend verification & reviewer module adhering to strict Clean/Hexagonal Architecture:\n\n1. Deterministic Ingestion & Invariant Validation:\n   - Strongly typed data contracts (using strict schema validation with zero implicit coercion).\n   - Invariant checks: handle empty comments, missing teams, orphaned response IDs, and cross-department bleed.\n\n2. Privacy, k-Anonymity & Sanitization Engine:\n   - Cohort Suppression Policy: Enforce minimum response thresholds ($k \\ge 5$). Any team summary with $n < 5$ (e.g., Mobile) must be automatically marked `SUPPRESSED` or restricted from direct rollup.\n   - PII & Quasi-Identifier Detection: Mask direct PII (emails, phone numbers, employee IDs) and flag high-entropy quasi-identifiers (office locations + single-person roles).\n   - Sensitive Attribute Quarantine: Detect and redact individual health/burnout attributions tied to unique shifts/rotas.\n\n3. Claim Provenance & Faithfulness Verification:\n   - Claim Decomposition: Split AI summary text into atomic, testable claims.\n   - Grounding & Evidence Scoring: Map each claim against supporting raw responses.\n   - Hyperbole/Frequency Mismatch Detection: Flag quantifier mismatches (e.g., summary claims \""almost everyone\"", \""consistently\"", \""unanimously\"" when support count is $< 50\\%$ or $n = 1$).\n\n4. Observable Reviewer Console Contracts:\n   - Produce a structured audit verdict for every summary:\n     `{ summaryId, status: \""APPROVED\"" | \""FLAGGED\"" | \""BLOCKED\"", riskScore, findings: [ { ruleId, severity, message, evidencePaths, remediationSuggestion } ] }`.\n   - Never leak raw unmasked comments in telemetry, error payloads, or public API responses.\n\n---\n\n### Phased Implementation Plan\n\nWork step-by-step. Do not rush to output all code at once:\n\n- Step 1: Data Contracts & Invariant Rules. Define the schema interfaces, error taxonomy, and threshold configs ($k$-anonymity limits, sensitive lexicons, quantifier rules).\n- Step 2: Verification Core (Pure Logic). Implement the evaluation pipeline as pure functions with zero I/O side effects:\n  - `CohortSizeGuard`\n  - `QuasiIdentifierSanitizer`\n  - `ClaimGroundingEvaluator`\n- Step 3: End-to-End Orchestrator. Wire the pipeline against the actual test scenarios (`Mobile` re-identification, `Payments` burnout disclosure, and `Payments` remote-work exaggeration).\n- Step 4: Verification Test Suite. Write automated assertions verifying that all 3 known security/hallucination traps are correctly intercepted with clear, machine-readable finding codes.\n\nBegin by delivering Step 1: Formalize the TypeScript / Python data models and the Invariant Rule definitions.""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\""message\"":\""Implemented Step 1 as a pure domain layer: strict runtime data contracts, audit/error taxonomy, threshold/privacy configs, and invariant rule definitions. Assumption: because this project is currently JS-only and dependencies are constrained, I used JavaScript modules with JSDoc-style contracts and deterministic runtime validation rather than adding TypeScript tooling. Nothing visible changes in the preview yet; these files are ready for Step 2 verification logic.\"",\""files\"":[{\""path\"":\""src/domain/policyConfig.js\"",\""contents\"":\""export const SEVERITY = Object.freeze({\\n  INFO: \\\""INFO\\\"",\\n  LOW: \\\""LOW\\\"",\\n  MEDIUM: \\\""MEDIUM\\\"",\\n  HIGH: \\\""HIGH\\\"",\\n  CRITICAL: \\\""CRITICAL\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const AUDIT_STATUS = Object.freeze({\\n  APPROVED: \\\""APPROVED\\\"",\\n  FLAGGED: \\\""FLAGGED\\\"",\\n  BLOCKED: \\\""BLOCKED\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const FINDING_CATEGORY = Object.freeze({\\n  SCHEMA: \\\""SCHEMA\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT: \\\""INVARIANT\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY: \\\""PRIVACY\\\"",\\n  CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS: \\\""CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS\\\"",\\n  DATA_SCOPE: \\\""DATA_SCOPE\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const RULE_IDS = Object.freeze({\\n  SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS: \\\""SCHEMA.EXACT_KEYS\\\"",\\n  SCHEMA_TYPE: \\\""SCHEMA.TYPE\\\"",\\n  SCHEMA_ENUM: \\\""SCHEMA.ENUM\\\"",\\n  SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING: \\\""SCHEMA.NON_EMPTY_STRING\\\"",\\n\\n  INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID: \\\""INVARIANT.DUPLICATE_ID\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT: \\\""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM: \\\""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_TEAM\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT: \\\""INVARIANT.EMPTY_COMMENT\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP: \\\""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP\\\"",\\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE: \\\""INVARIANT.EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE\\\"",\\n\\n  SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED: \\\""SCOPE.CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED\\\"",\\n\\n  PRIVACY_COHORT_TOO_SMALL: \\\""PRIVACY.COHORT_TOO_SMALL\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY_DIRECT_PII: \\\""PRIVACY.DIRECT_PII\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY_QUASI_IDENTIFIER: \\\""PRIVACY.QUASI_IDENTIFIER\\\"",\\n  PRIVACY_SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION: \\\""PRIVACY.SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION\\\"",\\n\\n  CLAIM_UNSUPPORTED: \\\""CLAIM.UNSUPPORTED\\\"",\\n  CLAIM_FREQUENCY_MISMATCH: \\\""CLAIM.FREQUENCY_MISMATCH\\\"",\\n});\\n\\nexport const POLICY_CONFIG = Object.freeze({\\n  anonymity: Object.freeze({\\n    minCohortResponses: 5,\\n    minSupportingResponsesForAttributableClaim: 2,\\n  }),\\n\\n  pii: Object.freeze({\\n    email: /\\\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\\\b/gi,\\n    australianPhone: /(?:\\\\+?61|0)\\\\s?(?:2|3|4|7|8)\\\\s?(?:\\\\d\\\\s?){8}\\\\b/g,\\n    employeeId: /\\\\b(?:employee|emp|staff|worker)[-\\\\s_]*id[:#]?\\\\s*[A-Z0-9-]{4,}\\\\b/gi,\\n    taxFileNumberLike: /\\\\b\\\\d{3}\\\\s?\\\\d{3}\\\\s?\\\\d{3}\\\\b/g,\\n  }),\\n\\n  quasiIdentifiers: Object.freeze({\\n    locationTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""perth\\\"",\\n      \\\""sydney\\\"",\\n      \\\""melbourne\\\"",\\n      \\\""brisbane\\\"",\\n      \\\""adelaide\\\"",\\n      \\\""office\\\"",\\n      \\\""site\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n    singlePersonRoleTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""lead\\\"",\\n      \\\""owner\\\"",\\n      \\\""only person\\\"",\\n      \\\""sole\\\"",\\n      \\\""alone\\\"",\\n      \\\""single person\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n    narrowWorkTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""atlas migration\\\"",\\n      \\\""overnight reconciliation\\\"",\\n      \\\""rota\\\"",\\n      \\\""on-call\\\"",\\n      \\\""migration\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n  }),\\n\\n  sensitiveAttributes: Object.freeze({\\n    wellbeingTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""burning out\\\"",\\n      \\\""burnout\\\"",\\n      \\\""wearing me down\\\"",\\n      \\\""exhausting\\\"",\\n      \\\""stressful\\\"",\\n      \\\""mental health\\\"",\\n      \\\""health\\\"",\\n      \\\""wellbeing\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n    attributionTerms: Object.freeze([\\n      \\\""one engineer\\\"",\\n      \\\""only person\\\"",\\n      \\\""alone\\\"",\\n      \\\""sole\\\"",\\n      \\\""single person\\\"",\\n    ]),\\n  }),\\n\\n  quantifiers: Object.freeze([\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""almost everyone\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.8, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""everyone\\\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""unanimously\\\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""most\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.6, minSupportCount: 3 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""consistently\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \\\""many\\\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\\n  ]),\\n});\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/domain/contracts.js\"",\""contents\"":\""import { FINDING_CATEGORY, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \\\""./policyConfig.js\\\"";\\n\\nconst GROUP_TYPES = Object.freeze([\\\""team\\\"", \\\""department\\\""]);\\n\\nexport function makeValidationIssue({\\n  ruleId,\\n  severity = SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n  category = FINDING_CATEGORY.SCHEMA,\\n  message,\\n  path,\\n  expected,\\n  actual,\\n}) {\\n  return {\\n    ruleId,\\n    severity,\\n    category,\\n    message,\\n    path,\\n    expected,\\n    actual,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction isPlainObject(value) {\\n  return Object.prototype.toString.call(value) === \\\""[object Object]\\\"";\\n}\\n\\nfunction describeType(value) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return \\\""array\\\"";\\n  if (value === null) return \\\""null\\\"";\\n  return typeof value;\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateExactKeys(value, expectedKeys, path, issues) {\\n  if (!isPlainObject(value)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path} must be an object with an exact schema.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""plain object\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  const actualKeys = Object.keys(value).sort();\\n  const sortedExpected = [...expectedKeys].sort();\\n  const missing = sortedExpected.filter((key) => !actualKeys.includes(key));\\n  const unexpected = actualKeys.filter((key) => !sortedExpected.includes(key));\\n\\n  if (missing.length > 0 || unexpected.length > 0) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS,\\n        message: `${path} has schema key mismatch.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: sortedExpected,\\n        actual: actualKeys,\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return missing.length === 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateString(value, path, issues, { allowEmpty = false } = {}) {\\n  if (typeof value !== \\\""string\\\"") {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path} must be a string.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""string\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!allowEmpty && value.trim().length === 0) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING,\\n        message: `${path} must be a non-empty string.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""non-empty string\\\"",\\n        actual: value,\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateStringArray(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path} must be an array of strings.`,\\n        path,\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  value.forEach((item, index) => {\\n    validateString(item, `${path}[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateDepartment(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""name\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateTeam(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""name\\\"", \\\""departmentId\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.departmentId, `${path}.departmentId`, issues);\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateResponse(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""teamId\\\"", \\\""comment\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.teamId, `${path}.teamId`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.comment, `${path}.comment`, issues, { allowEmpty: true });\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateTheme(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""title\\\"", \\\""summary\\\"", \\\""claims\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n  validateString(value.title, `${path}.title`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.summary, `${path}.summary`, issues);\\n  validateStringArray(value.claims, `${path}.claims`, issues);\\n}\\n\\nfunction validateSummary(value, path, issues) {\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\\\""id\\\"", \\\""groupType\\\"", \\\""groupId\\\"", \\\""themes\\\""], path, issues)) return;\\n\\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.groupType, `${path}.groupType`, issues);\\n  validateString(value.groupId, `${path}.groupId`, issues);\\n\\n  if (typeof value.groupType === \\\""string\\\"" && !GROUP_TYPES.includes(value.groupType)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_ENUM,\\n        message: `${path}.groupType must be one of the supported summary scopes.`,\\n        path: `${path}.groupType`,\\n        expected: GROUP_TYPES,\\n        actual: value.groupType,\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(value.themes)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: `${path}.themes must be an array.`,\\n        path: `${path}.themes`,\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(value.themes),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  value.themes.forEach((theme, index) => {\\n    validateTheme(theme, `${path}.themes[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateOrgContract(org) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  if (!validateExactKeys(org, [\\\""departments\\\"", \\\""teams\\\""], \\\""teams\\\"", issues)) {\\n    return { valid: false, issues };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.departments)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""teams.departments must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""teams.departments\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(org.departments),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  } else {\\n    org.departments.forEach((department, index) => {\\n      validateDepartment(department, `teams.departments[${index}]`, issues);\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.teams)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""teams.teams must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""teams.teams\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(org.teams),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  } else {\\n    org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\\n      validateTeam(team, `teams.teams[${index}]`, issues);\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateResponsesContract(responses) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(responses)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""responses must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""responses\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(responses),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return { valid: false, issues };\\n  }\\n\\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\\n    validateResponse(response, `responses[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateSummariesContract(summaries) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  if (!Array.isArray(summaries)) {\\n    issues.push(\\n      makeValidationIssue({\\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\\n        message: \\\""summaries must be an array.\\\"",\\n        path: \\\""summaries\\\"",\\n        expected: \\\""array\\\"",\\n        actual: describeType(summaries),\\n      }),\\n    );\\n    return { valid: false, issues };\\n  }\\n\\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\\n    validateSummary(summary, `summaries[${index}]`, issues);\\n  });\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries }) {\\n  const results = [\\n    validateOrgContract(org),\\n    validateResponsesContract(responses),\\n    validateSummariesContract(summaries),\\n  ];\\n\\n  const issues = results.flatMap((result) => result.issues);\\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\\n}\\n\""},{\""path\"":\""src/domain/invariants.js\"",\""contents\"":\""import { makeValidationIssue, validateDataContracts } from \\\""./contracts.js\\\"";\\nimport { FINDING_CATEGORY, POLICY_CONFIG, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \\\""./policyConfig.js\\\"";\\n\\nfunction buildDuplicateIdIssues(records, path, entityName) {\\n  const seen = new Map();\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  records.forEach((record, index) => {\\n    if (typeof record?.id !== \\\""string\\\"") return;\\n\\n    if (seen.has(record.id)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Duplicate ${entityName} id '${record.id}' detected.`,\\n          path: `${path}[${index}].id`,\\n          expected: \\\""globally unique id within collection\\\"",\\n          actual: record.id,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    seen.set(record.id, index);\\n  });\\n\\n  return issues;\\n}\\n\\nexport function getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org) {\\n  if (summary.groupType === \\\""team\\\"") {\\n    const team = org.teams.find((candidate) => candidate.id === summary.groupId);\\n    return team ? [team.id] : [];\\n  }\\n\\n  if (summary.groupType === \\\""department\\\"") {\\n    return org.teams\\n      .filter((team) => team.departmentId === summary.groupId)\\n      .map((team) => team.id);\\n  }\\n\\n  return [];\\n}\\n\\nexport function getDepartmentIdForTeam(teamId, org) {\\n  return org.teams.find((team) => team.id === teamId)?.departmentId ?? null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateEvidenceWithinSummaryScope({ summary, evidenceTeamIds, org, path }) {\\n  const allowedTeamIds = new Set(getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org));\\n  const issues = [];\\n\\n  evidenceTeamIds.forEach((teamId, index) => {\\n    if (!allowedTeamIds.has(teamId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.CRITICAL,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.DATA_SCOPE,\\n          message: `Evidence team '${teamId}' is outside summary '${summary.id}' scope.`,\\n          path: `${path}.evidenceTeamIds[${index}]`,\\n          expected: [...allowedTeamIds],\\n          actual: teamId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  return issues;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries }) {\\n  const issues = [];\\n  const departmentIds = new Set(org.departments.map((department) => department.id));\\n  const teamIds = new Set(org.teams.map((team) => team.id));\\n\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.departments, \\\""teams.departments\\\"", \\\""department\\\""));\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.teams, \\\""teams.teams\\\"", \\\""team\\\""));\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(responses, \\\""responses\\\"", \\\""response\\\""));\\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(summaries, \\\""summaries\\\"", \\\""summary\\\""));\\n\\n  org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\\n    if (!departmentIds.has(team.departmentId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Team '${team.id}' references unknown department '${team.departmentId}'.`,\\n          path: `teams.teams[${index}].departmentId`,\\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\\n          actual: team.departmentId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\\n    if (!teamIds.has(response.teamId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' references unknown team '${response.teamId}'.`,\\n          path: `responses[${index}].teamId`,\\n          expected: [...teamIds],\\n          actual: response.teamId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    if (typeof response.comment === \\\""string\\\"" && response.comment.trim().length === 0) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.INFO,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' has an empty comment and must not be used as text evidence.`,\\n          path: `responses[${index}].comment`,\\n          expected: \\\""non-empty comment for claim evidence\\\"",\\n          actual: \\\""\\\"",\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\\n    const path = `summaries[${index}]`;\\n\\n    if (summary.groupType === \\\""team\\\"" && !teamIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown team '${summary.groupId}'.`,\\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\\n          expected: [...teamIds],\\n          actual: summary.groupId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    if (summary.groupType === \\\""department\\\"" && !departmentIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown department '${summary.groupId}'.`,\\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\\n          actual: summary.groupId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n\\n    const scopedTeamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\\n    if ((summary.groupType === \\\""team\\\"" || summary.groupType === \\\""department\\\"") && scopedTeamIds.length === 0) {\\n      issues.push(\\n        makeValidationIssue({\\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE,\\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' has no valid response scope.`,\\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\\n          expected: \\\""at least one team in summary scope\\\"",\\n          actual: summary.groupId,\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  return { valid: issues.every((issue) => issue.severity === SEVERITY.INFO), issues };\\n}\\n\\nexport function getResponseCountsByTeam(responses) {\\n  return responses.reduce((counts, response) => {\\n    counts[response.teamId] ??= { total: 0, nonEmpty: 0 };\\n    counts[response.teamId].total += 1;\\n\\n    if (typeof response.comment === \\\""string\\\"" && response.comment.trim().length > 0) {\\n      counts[response.teamId].nonEmpty += 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    return counts;\\n  }, {});\\n}\\n\\nexport function getCohortPolicyForSummary(summary, org, responses, config = POLICY_CONFIG) {\\n  const teamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\\n  const responseCounts = getResponseCountsByTeam(responses);\\n  const totalResponses = teamIds.reduce((total, teamId) => {\\n    return total + (responseCounts[teamId]?.total ?? 0);\\n  }, 0);\\n\\n  return {\\n    summaryId: summary.id,\\n    scopedTeamIds: teamIds,\\n    responseCount: totalResponses,\\n    minRequiredResponses: config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\\n    publishable: totalResponses >= config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateDatasetReadiness({ org, responses, summaries }) {\\n  const contractResult = validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries });\\n\\n  if (!contractResult.valid) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      issues: contractResult.issues,\\n      stage: \\\""contract\\\"",\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const invariantResult = validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries });\\n  return {\\n    valid: invariantResult.valid,\\n    issues: invariantResult.issues,\\n    stage: \\\""invariant\\\"",\\n  };\\n}\\n\""}],\""reasoning\"":\""The user asked to begin Step 1 only, so I avoided building the verification pipeline/UI/tests. I created strict runtime schemas, enumerated rule IDs and severities, privacy threshold config, and invariant helpers including summary scoping and cohort policy primitives for Step 2. I used JS modules rather than adding TypeScript because the current workspace has no TS setup and dependency additions are constrained.\""}"",""refusal"":null,""annotations"":[],""parsed"":{""message"":""Implemented Step 1 as a pure domain layer: strict runtime data contracts, audit/error taxonomy, threshold/privacy configs, and invariant rule definitions. Assumption: because this project is currently JS-only and dependencies are constrained, I used JavaScript modules with JSDoc-style contracts and deterministic runtime validation rather than adding TypeScript tooling. Nothing visible changes in the preview yet; these files are ready for Step 2 verification logic."",""files"":[{""path"":""src/domain/policyConfig.js"",""contents"":""export const SEVERITY = Object.freeze({\n  INFO: \""INFO\"",\n  LOW: \""LOW\"",\n  MEDIUM: \""MEDIUM\"",\n  HIGH: \""HIGH\"",\n  CRITICAL: \""CRITICAL\"",\n});\n\nexport const AUDIT_STATUS = Object.freeze({\n  APPROVED: \""APPROVED\"",\n  FLAGGED: \""FLAGGED\"",\n  BLOCKED: \""BLOCKED\"",\n});\n\nexport const FINDING_CATEGORY = Object.freeze({\n  SCHEMA: \""SCHEMA\"",\n  INVARIANT: \""INVARIANT\"",\n  PRIVACY: \""PRIVACY\"",\n  CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS: \""CLAIM_FAITHFULNESS\"",\n  DATA_SCOPE: \""DATA_SCOPE\"",\n});\n\nexport const RULE_IDS = Object.freeze({\n  SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS: \""SCHEMA.EXACT_KEYS\"",\n  SCHEMA_TYPE: \""SCHEMA.TYPE\"",\n  SCHEMA_ENUM: \""SCHEMA.ENUM\"",\n  SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING: \""SCHEMA.NON_EMPTY_STRING\"",\n\n  INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID: \""INVARIANT.DUPLICATE_ID\"",\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT: \""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT\"",\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM: \""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_TEAM\"",\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT: \""INVARIANT.EMPTY_COMMENT\"",\n  INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP: \""INVARIANT.UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP\"",\n  INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE: \""INVARIANT.EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE\"",\n\n  SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED: \""SCOPE.CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED\"",\n\n  PRIVACY_COHORT_TOO_SMALL: \""PRIVACY.COHORT_TOO_SMALL\"",\n  PRIVACY_DIRECT_PII: \""PRIVACY.DIRECT_PII\"",\n  PRIVACY_QUASI_IDENTIFIER: \""PRIVACY.QUASI_IDENTIFIER\"",\n  PRIVACY_SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION: \""PRIVACY.SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTION\"",\n\n  CLAIM_UNSUPPORTED: \""CLAIM.UNSUPPORTED\"",\n  CLAIM_FREQUENCY_MISMATCH: \""CLAIM.FREQUENCY_MISMATCH\"",\n});\n\nexport const POLICY_CONFIG = Object.freeze({\n  anonymity: Object.freeze({\n    minCohortResponses: 5,\n    minSupportingResponsesForAttributableClaim: 2,\n  }),\n\n  pii: Object.freeze({\n    email: /\\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}\\b/gi,\n    australianPhone: /(?:\\+?61|0)\\s?(?:2|3|4|7|8)\\s?(?:\\d\\s?){8}\\b/g,\n    employeeId: /\\b(?:employee|emp|staff|worker)[-\\s_]*id[:#]?\\s*[A-Z0-9-]{4,}\\b/gi,\n    taxFileNumberLike: /\\b\\d{3}\\s?\\d{3}\\s?\\d{3}\\b/g,\n  }),\n\n  quasiIdentifiers: Object.freeze({\n    locationTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""perth\"",\n      \""sydney\"",\n      \""melbourne\"",\n      \""brisbane\"",\n      \""adelaide\"",\n      \""office\"",\n      \""site\"",\n    ]),\n    singlePersonRoleTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""lead\"",\n      \""owner\"",\n      \""only person\"",\n      \""sole\"",\n      \""alone\"",\n      \""single person\"",\n    ]),\n    narrowWorkTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""atlas migration\"",\n      \""overnight reconciliation\"",\n      \""rota\"",\n      \""on-call\"",\n      \""migration\"",\n    ]),\n  }),\n\n  sensitiveAttributes: Object.freeze({\n    wellbeingTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""burning out\"",\n      \""burnout\"",\n      \""wearing me down\"",\n      \""exhausting\"",\n      \""stressful\"",\n      \""mental health\"",\n      \""health\"",\n      \""wellbeing\"",\n    ]),\n    attributionTerms: Object.freeze([\n      \""one engineer\"",\n      \""only person\"",\n      \""alone\"",\n      \""sole\"",\n      \""single person\"",\n    ]),\n  }),\n\n  quantifiers: Object.freeze([\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""almost everyone\"", minSupportRatio: 0.8, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""everyone\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""unanimously\"", minSupportRatio: 1, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""most\"", minSupportRatio: 0.6, minSupportCount: 3 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""consistently\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\n    Object.freeze({ phrase: \""many\"", minSupportRatio: 0.5, minSupportCount: 2 }),\n  ]),\n});\n""},{""path"":""src/domain/contracts.js"",""contents"":""import { FINDING_CATEGORY, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \""./policyConfig.js\"";\n\nconst GROUP_TYPES = Object.freeze([\""team\"", \""department\""]);\n\nexport function makeValidationIssue({\n  ruleId,\n  severity = SEVERITY.HIGH,\n  category = FINDING_CATEGORY.SCHEMA,\n  message,\n  path,\n  expected,\n  actual,\n}) {\n  return {\n    ruleId,\n    severity,\n    category,\n    message,\n    path,\n    expected,\n    actual,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction isPlainObject(value) {\n  return Object.prototype.toString.call(value) === \""[object Object]\"";\n}\n\nfunction describeType(value) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return \""array\"";\n  if (value === null) return \""null\"";\n  return typeof value;\n}\n\nfunction validateExactKeys(value, expectedKeys, path, issues) {\n  if (!isPlainObject(value)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path} must be an object with an exact schema.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""plain object\"",\n        actual: describeType(value),\n      }),\n    );\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const actualKeys = Object.keys(value).sort();\n  const sortedExpected = [...expectedKeys].sort();\n  const missing = sortedExpected.filter((key) => !actualKeys.includes(key));\n  const unexpected = actualKeys.filter((key) => !sortedExpected.includes(key));\n\n  if (missing.length > 0 || unexpected.length > 0) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_EXACT_KEYS,\n        message: `${path} has schema key mismatch.`,\n        path,\n        expected: sortedExpected,\n        actual: actualKeys,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  return missing.length === 0;\n}\n\nfunction validateString(value, path, issues, { allowEmpty = false } = {}) {\n  if (typeof value !== \""string\"") {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path} must be a string.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""string\"",\n        actual: describeType(value),\n      }),\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!allowEmpty && value.trim().length === 0) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_NON_EMPTY_STRING,\n        message: `${path} must be a non-empty string.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""non-empty string\"",\n        actual: value,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateStringArray(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path} must be an array of strings.`,\n        path,\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(value),\n      }),\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n\n  value.forEach((item, index) => {\n    validateString(item, `${path}[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction validateDepartment(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""name\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\n}\n\nfunction validateTeam(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""name\"", \""departmentId\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.name, `${path}.name`, issues);\n  validateString(value.departmentId, `${path}.departmentId`, issues);\n}\n\nfunction validateResponse(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""teamId\"", \""comment\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.teamId, `${path}.teamId`, issues);\n  validateString(value.comment, `${path}.comment`, issues, { allowEmpty: true });\n}\n\nfunction validateTheme(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""title\"", \""summary\"", \""claims\""], path, issues)) return;\n  validateString(value.title, `${path}.title`, issues);\n  validateString(value.summary, `${path}.summary`, issues);\n  validateStringArray(value.claims, `${path}.claims`, issues);\n}\n\nfunction validateSummary(value, path, issues) {\n  if (!validateExactKeys(value, [\""id\"", \""groupType\"", \""groupId\"", \""themes\""], path, issues)) return;\n\n  validateString(value.id, `${path}.id`, issues);\n  validateString(value.groupType, `${path}.groupType`, issues);\n  validateString(value.groupId, `${path}.groupId`, issues);\n\n  if (typeof value.groupType === \""string\"" && !GROUP_TYPES.includes(value.groupType)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_ENUM,\n        message: `${path}.groupType must be one of the supported summary scopes.`,\n        path: `${path}.groupType`,\n        expected: GROUP_TYPES,\n        actual: value.groupType,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(value.themes)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: `${path}.themes must be an array.`,\n        path: `${path}.themes`,\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(value.themes),\n      }),\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n\n  value.themes.forEach((theme, index) => {\n    validateTheme(theme, `${path}.themes[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n}\n\nexport function validateOrgContract(org) {\n  const issues = [];\n\n  if (!validateExactKeys(org, [\""departments\"", \""teams\""], \""teams\"", issues)) {\n    return { valid: false, issues };\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.departments)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""teams.departments must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""teams.departments\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(org.departments),\n      }),\n    );\n  } else {\n    org.departments.forEach((department, index) => {\n      validateDepartment(department, `teams.departments[${index}]`, issues);\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(org.teams)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""teams.teams must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""teams.teams\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(org.teams),\n      }),\n    );\n  } else {\n    org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\n      validateTeam(team, `teams.teams[${index}]`, issues);\n    });\n  }\n\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n\nexport function validateResponsesContract(responses) {\n  const issues = [];\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(responses)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""responses must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""responses\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(responses),\n      }),\n    );\n    return { valid: false, issues };\n  }\n\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\n    validateResponse(response, `responses[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n\nexport function validateSummariesContract(summaries) {\n  const issues = [];\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(summaries)) {\n    issues.push(\n      makeValidationIssue({\n        ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCHEMA_TYPE,\n        message: \""summaries must be an array.\"",\n        path: \""summaries\"",\n        expected: \""array\"",\n        actual: describeType(summaries),\n      }),\n    );\n    return { valid: false, issues };\n  }\n\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\n    validateSummary(summary, `summaries[${index}]`, issues);\n  });\n\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n\nexport function validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries }) {\n  const results = [\n    validateOrgContract(org),\n    validateResponsesContract(responses),\n    validateSummariesContract(summaries),\n  ];\n\n  const issues = results.flatMap((result) => result.issues);\n  return { valid: issues.length === 0, issues };\n}\n""},{""path"":""src/domain/invariants.js"",""contents"":""import { makeValidationIssue, validateDataContracts } from \""./contracts.js\"";\nimport { FINDING_CATEGORY, POLICY_CONFIG, RULE_IDS, SEVERITY } from \""./policyConfig.js\"";\n\nfunction buildDuplicateIdIssues(records, path, entityName) {\n  const seen = new Map();\n  const issues = [];\n\n  records.forEach((record, index) => {\n    if (typeof record?.id !== \""string\"") return;\n\n    if (seen.has(record.id)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_DUPLICATE_ID,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Duplicate ${entityName} id '${record.id}' detected.`,\n          path: `${path}[${index}].id`,\n          expected: \""globally unique id within collection\"",\n          actual: record.id,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    seen.set(record.id, index);\n  });\n\n  return issues;\n}\n\nexport function getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org) {\n  if (summary.groupType === \""team\"") {\n    const team = org.teams.find((candidate) => candidate.id === summary.groupId);\n    return team ? [team.id] : [];\n  }\n\n  if (summary.groupType === \""department\"") {\n    return org.teams\n      .filter((team) => team.departmentId === summary.groupId)\n      .map((team) => team.id);\n  }\n\n  return [];\n}\n\nexport function getDepartmentIdForTeam(teamId, org) {\n  return org.teams.find((team) => team.id === teamId)?.departmentId ?? null;\n}\n\nexport function validateEvidenceWithinSummaryScope({ summary, evidenceTeamIds, org, path }) {\n  const allowedTeamIds = new Set(getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org));\n  const issues = [];\n\n  evidenceTeamIds.forEach((teamId, index) => {\n    if (!allowedTeamIds.has(teamId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.SCOPE_CROSS_DEPARTMENT_BLEED,\n          severity: SEVERITY.CRITICAL,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.DATA_SCOPE,\n          message: `Evidence team '${teamId}' is outside summary '${summary.id}' scope.`,\n          path: `${path}.evidenceTeamIds[${index}]`,\n          expected: [...allowedTeamIds],\n          actual: teamId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  return issues;\n}\n\nexport function validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries }) {\n  const issues = [];\n  const departmentIds = new Set(org.departments.map((department) => department.id));\n  const teamIds = new Set(org.teams.map((team) => team.id));\n\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.departments, \""teams.departments\"", \""department\""));\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(org.teams, \""teams.teams\"", \""team\""));\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(responses, \""responses\"", \""response\""));\n  issues.push(...buildDuplicateIdIssues(summaries, \""summaries\"", \""summary\""));\n\n  org.teams.forEach((team, index) => {\n    if (!departmentIds.has(team.departmentId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_DEPARTMENT,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Team '${team.id}' references unknown department '${team.departmentId}'.`,\n          path: `teams.teams[${index}].departmentId`,\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\n          actual: team.departmentId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  responses.forEach((response, index) => {\n    if (!teamIds.has(response.teamId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_TEAM,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' references unknown team '${response.teamId}'.`,\n          path: `responses[${index}].teamId`,\n          expected: [...teamIds],\n          actual: response.teamId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    if (typeof response.comment === \""string\"" && response.comment.trim().length === 0) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_COMMENT,\n          severity: SEVERITY.INFO,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Response '${response.id}' has an empty comment and must not be used as text evidence.`,\n          path: `responses[${index}].comment`,\n          expected: \""non-empty comment for claim evidence\"",\n          actual: \""\"",\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  summaries.forEach((summary, index) => {\n    const path = `summaries[${index}]`;\n\n    if (summary.groupType === \""team\"" && !teamIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown team '${summary.groupId}'.`,\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\n          expected: [...teamIds],\n          actual: summary.groupId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    if (summary.groupType === \""department\"" && !departmentIds.has(summary.groupId)) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_UNKNOWN_SUMMARY_GROUP,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' references unknown department '${summary.groupId}'.`,\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\n          expected: [...departmentIds],\n          actual: summary.groupId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n\n    const scopedTeamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\n    if ((summary.groupType === \""team\"" || summary.groupType === \""department\"") && scopedTeamIds.length === 0) {\n      issues.push(\n        makeValidationIssue({\n          ruleId: RULE_IDS.INVARIANT_EMPTY_SUMMARY_SCOPE,\n          severity: SEVERITY.HIGH,\n          category: FINDING_CATEGORY.INVARIANT,\n          message: `Summary '${summary.id}' has no valid response scope.`,\n          path: `${path}.groupId`,\n          expected: \""at least one team in summary scope\"",\n          actual: summary.groupId,\n        }),\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  return { valid: issues.every((issue) => issue.severity === SEVERITY.INFO), issues };\n}\n\nexport function getResponseCountsByTeam(responses) {\n  return responses.reduce((counts, response) => {\n    counts[response.teamId] ??= { total: 0, nonEmpty: 0 };\n    counts[response.teamId].total += 1;\n\n    if (typeof response.comment === \""string\"" && response.comment.trim().length > 0) {\n      counts[response.teamId].nonEmpty += 1;\n    }\n\n    return counts;\n  }, {});\n}\n\nexport function getCohortPolicyForSummary(summary, org, responses, config = POLICY_CONFIG) {\n  const teamIds = getTeamIdsForSummaryScope(summary, org);\n  const responseCounts = getResponseCountsByTeam(responses);\n  const totalResponses = teamIds.reduce((total, teamId) => {\n    return total + (responseCounts[teamId]?.total ?? 0);\n  }, 0);\n\n  return {\n    summaryId: summary.id,\n    scopedTeamIds: teamIds,\n    responseCount: totalResponses,\n    minRequiredResponses: config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\n    publishable: totalResponses >= config.anonymity.minCohortResponses,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function validateDatasetReadiness({ org, responses, summaries }) {\n  const contractResult = validateDataContracts({ org, responses, summaries });\n\n  if (!contractResult.valid) {\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      issues: contractResult.issues,\n      stage: \""contract\"",\n    };\n  }\n\n  const invariantResult = validateInvariants({ org, responses, summaries });\n  return {\n    valid: invariantResult.valid,\n    issues: invariantResult.issues,\n    stage: \""invariant\"",\n  };\n}\n""}],""reasoning"":""The user asked to begin Step 1 only, so I avoided building the verification pipeline/UI/tests. I created strict runtime schemas, enumerated rule IDs and severities, privacy threshold config, and invariant helpers including summary scoping and cohort policy primitives for Step 2. I used JS modules rather than adding TypeScript because the current workspace has no TS setup and dependency additions are constrained.""}}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_schema\"",\""json_schema\"":{\""name\"":\""assistant_output\"",\""strict\"":true,\""schema\"":{\""$schema\"":\""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""message\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""},\""files\"":{\""type\"":\""array\"",\""items\"":{\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""path\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""},\""contents\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""}},\""required\"":[\""path\"",\""contents\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false},\""description\"":\""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""},\""reasoning\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""}},\""required\"":[\""message\"",\""files\"",\""reasoning\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false}}}"",""turnSeq"":""5"",""challengeTitle"":""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","c91ed571cd62c2e3b899615cfde5183f81e7f4ba","","[]"
"t-39e5635f-9e37-4d85-8fb1-0cf421c1511e","39e5635f-9e37-4d85-8fb1-0cf421c1511e","candidate_turn","SPAN","candidate_turn","2026-09-28 04:37:00.948000","","","default","","candidate-1","rsri7n9d9d4ij1ii7boywd8o","DEFAULT","","","","","","","{}","{}","{}","0","{""message"":""Act as a Principal AI Safety & Systems Architect specializing in enterprise privacy, human-in-the-loop (HITL) audit systems, and natural language verification.\n\n### System Overview & Context\nWe are engineering an automated review, verification, and sanitization engine for an enterprise employee survey platform. The system ingests raw survey data alongside AI-generated summaries and flags compliance violations, privacy risks, and hallucinations before any summary is published to leadership.\n\n### Input Data Topography\nThe system operates on three existing JSON datasets:\n1. `teams.json`: Org hierarchy defining departments (Engineering, Customer Success) and nested teams (Payments, Platform, Mobile, Onboarding, Support).\n2. `responses.json`: 29 raw survey records (`id`, `teamId`, free-text `comment`), including empty comments (6 records) and valid comments (23 records).\n3. `summaries.json`: 6 AI-generated summaries (5 team-level, 1 department-level) containing 12 themes, executive narratives, and discrete claims.\n\n### Identified Critical Vulnerabilities in Current Data\nOur system must catch and programmatically flag known anti-patterns present in this dataset:\n1. Re-identification via Small Cohorts & Quasi-Identifiers:\n   - The Mobile team has only 3 responses ($n=3$).\n   - Comments/summaries reference narrow quasi-identifiers (\""Perth office\"", \""lead\"", \""Atlas migration\""), creating extreme deanonymization risk.\n2. Sensitive Wellbeing & Attributable Disclosure:\n   - The Payments summary explicitly leaks: \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"" This attributes sensitive mental health/burnout state to a known, single-person operational role.\n3. Unsupported Claims & Frequency Hallucinations:\n   - The Payments summary claims \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,\"" despite only a single raw response mentioning remote work.\n4. Data Scoping & Rollup Boundary Breaches:\n   - Department summaries aggregating or leaking un-redacted team-specific identifiable claims.\n\n---\n\n### Core Objectives & Architecture Requirements\n\nYou will design and implement the backend verification & reviewer module adhering to strict Clean/Hexagonal Architecture:\n\n1. Deterministic Ingestion & Invariant Validation:\n   - Strongly typed data contracts (using strict schema validation with zero implicit coercion).\n   - Invariant checks: handle empty comments, missing teams, orphaned response IDs, and cross-department bleed.\n\n2. Privacy, k-Anonymity & Sanitization Engine:\n   - Cohort Suppression Policy: Enforce minimum response thresholds ($k \\ge 5$). Any team summary with $n < 5$ (e.g., Mobile) must be automatically marked `SUPPRESSED` or restricted from direct rollup.\n   - PII & Quasi-Identifier Detection: Mask direct PII (emails, phone numbers, employee IDs) and flag high-entropy quasi-identifiers (office locations + single-person roles).\n   - Sensitive Attribute Quarantine: Detect and redact individual health/burnout attributions tied to unique shifts/rotas.\n\n3. Claim Provenance & Faithfulness Verification:\n   - Claim Decomposition: Split AI summary text into atomic, testable claims.\n   - Grounding & Evidence Scoring: Map each claim against supporting raw responses.\n   - Hyperbole/Frequency Mismatch Detection: Flag quantifier mismatches (e.g., summary claims \""almost everyone\"", \""consistently\"", \""unanimously\"" when support count is $< 50\\%$ or $n = 1$).\n\n4. Observable Reviewer Console Contracts:\n   - Produce a structured audit verdict for every summary:\n     `{ summaryId, status: \""APPROVED\"" | \""FLAGGED\"" | \""BLOCKED\"", riskScore, findings: [ { ruleId, severity, message, evidencePaths, remediationSuggestion } ] }`.\n   - Never leak raw unmasked comments in telemetry, error payloads, or public API responses.\n\n---\n\n### Phased Implementation Plan\n\nWork step-by-step. Do not rush to output all code at once:\n\n- Step 1: Data Contracts & Invariant Rules. Define the schema interfaces, error taxonomy, and threshold configs ($k$-anonymity limits, sensitive lexicons, quantifier rules).\n- Step 2: Verification Core (Pure Logic). Implement the evaluation pipeline as pure functions with zero I/O side effects:\n  - `CohortSizeGuard`\n  - `QuasiIdentifierSanitizer`\n  - `ClaimGroundingEvaluator`\n- Step 3: End-to-End Orchestrator. Wire the pipeline against the actual test scenarios (`Mobile` re-identification, `Payments` burnout disclosure, and `Payments` remote-work exaggeration).\n- Step 4: Verification Test Suite. Write automated assertions verifying that all 3 known security/hallucination traps are correctly intercepted with clear, machine-readable finding codes.\n\nBegin by delivering Step 1: Formalize the TypeScript / Python data models and the Invariant Rule definitions.""}","","{""charCount"":""4744"",""challengeTitle"":""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking""}","","","[""candidate_prompt"",""workspace_chat""]","c91ed571cd62c2e3b899615cfde5183f81e7f4ba","","[]"
"2b85cb32-fd18-43e7-bee2-640077ab2a8e","39e5635f-9e37-4d85-8fb1-0cf421c1511e","candidate_turn","EVENT","user_message_received","2026-09-28 04:37:00.948000","","","default","","candidate-1","rsri7n9d9d4ij1ii7boywd8o","DEFAULT","","","","","","","{}","{}","{}","0","{""message"":""Act as a Principal AI Safety & Systems Architect specializing in enterprise privacy, human-in-the-loop (HITL) audit systems, and natural language verification.\n\n### System Overview & Context\nWe are engineering an automated review, verification, and sanitization engine for an enterprise employee survey platform. The system ingests raw survey data alongside AI-generated summaries and flags compliance violations, privacy risks, and hallucinations before any summary is published to leadership.\n\n### Input Data Topography\nThe system operates on three existing JSON datasets:\n1. `teams.json`: Org hierarchy defining departments (Engineering, Customer Success) and nested teams (Payments, Platform, Mobile, Onboarding, Support).\n2. `responses.json`: 29 raw survey records (`id`, `teamId`, free-text `comment`), including empty comments (6 records) and valid comments (23 records).\n3. `summaries.json`: 6 AI-generated summaries (5 team-level, 1 department-level) containing 12 themes, executive narratives, and discrete claims.\n\n### Identified Critical Vulnerabilities in Current Data\nOur system must catch and programmatically flag known anti-patterns present in this dataset:\n1. Re-identification via Small Cohorts & Quasi-Identifiers:\n   - The Mobile team has only 3 responses ($n=3$).\n   - Comments/summaries reference narrow quasi-identifiers (\""Perth office\"", \""lead\"", \""Atlas migration\""), creating extreme deanonymization risk.\n2. Sensitive Wellbeing & Attributable Disclosure:\n   - The Payments summary explicitly leaks: \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"" This attributes sensitive mental health/burnout state to a known, single-person operational role.\n3. Unsupported Claims & Frequency Hallucinations:\n   - The Payments summary claims \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,\"" despite only a single raw response mentioning remote work.\n4. Data Scoping & Rollup Boundary Breaches:\n   - Department summaries aggregating or leaking un-redacted team-specific identifiable claims.\n\n---\n\n### Core Objectives & Architecture Requirements\n\nYou will design and implement the backend verification & reviewer module adhering to strict Clean/Hexagonal Architecture:\n\n1. Deterministic Ingestion & Invariant Validation:\n   - Strongly typed data contracts (using strict schema validation with zero implicit coercion).\n   - Invariant checks: handle empty comments, missing teams, orphaned response IDs, and cross-department bleed.\n\n2. Privacy, k-Anonymity & Sanitization Engine:\n   - Cohort Suppression Policy: Enforce minimum response thresholds ($k \\ge 5$). Any team summary with $n < 5$ (e.g., Mobile) must be automatically marked `SUPPRESSED` or restricted from direct rollup.\n   - PII & Quasi-Identifier Detection: Mask direct PII (emails, phone numbers, employee IDs) and flag high-entropy quasi-identifiers (office locations + single-person roles).\n   - Sensitive Attribute Quarantine: Detect and redact individual health/burnout attributions tied to unique shifts/rotas.\n\n3. Claim Provenance & Faithfulness Verification:\n   - Claim Decomposition: Split AI summary text into atomic, testable claims.\n   - Grounding & Evidence Scoring: Map each claim against supporting raw responses.\n   - Hyperbole/Frequency Mismatch Detection: Flag quantifier mismatches (e.g., summary claims \""almost everyone\"", \""consistently\"", \""unanimously\"" when support count is $< 50\\%$ or $n = 1$).\n\n4. Observable Reviewer Console Contracts:\n   - Produce a structured audit verdict for every summary:\n     `{ summaryId, status: \""APPROVED\"" | \""FLAGGED\"" | \""BLOCKED\"", riskScore, findings: [ { ruleId, severity, message, evidencePaths, remediationSuggestion } ] }`.\n   - Never leak raw unmasked comments in telemetry, error payloads, or public API responses.\n\n---\n\n### Phased Implementation Plan\n\nWork step-by-step. Do not rush to output all code at once:\n\n- Step 1: Data Contracts & Invariant Rules. Define the schema interfaces, error taxonomy, and threshold configs ($k$-anonymity limits, sensitive lexicons, quantifier rules).\n- Step 2: Verification Core (Pure Logic). Implement the evaluation pipeline as pure functions with zero I/O side effects:\n  - `CohortSizeGuard`\n  - `QuasiIdentifierSanitizer`\n  - `ClaimGroundingEvaluator`\n- Step 3: End-to-End Orchestrator. Wire the pipeline against the actual test scenarios (`Mobile` re-identification, `Payments` burnout disclosure, and `Payments` remote-work exaggeration).\n- Step 4: Verification Test Suite. Write automated assertions verifying that all 3 known security/hallucination traps are correctly intercepted with clear, machine-readable finding codes.\n\nBegin by delivering Step 1: Formalize the TypeScript / Python data models and the Invariant Rule definitions.""}","","{""charCount"":""4744"",""challengeTitle"":""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking""}","","","[""candidate_prompt"",""workspace_chat""]","c91ed571cd62c2e3b899615cfde5183f81e7f4ba","t-39e5635f-9e37-4d85-8fb1-0cf421c1511e","[]"
"t-1472ec4c-8063-4677-b1f2-a7d0799cbccb","1472ec4c-8063-4677-b1f2-a7d0799cbccb","ai_stage:assistant","SPAN","ai_stage:assistant","2026-09-28 04:35:33.355000","","","default","","candidate-1","rsri7n9d9d4ij1ii7boywd8o","DEFAULT","","","","","","","{}","{}","{}","0","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for BlueScope.\n\n# Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\n\n## Context & Objectives\nBuild a production-grade service module for **BlueScope** that handles workflow events, enforces strict data scoping, and guarantees compliance with the Australian Privacy Act 1988.\n\n## Constraints\n1. **PII Masking**: Ensure phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses are masked prior to persistence.\n2. **Deterministic Validation**: Validate all inputs using strict schema boundaries.\n3. **Observable Verification**: Provide clear error reasons when input fails domain invariants.\n</challenge>""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""can you help me explain the data given in the json?""},{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""The JSON data represents a synthetic employee survey review dataset. I haven’t changed any files.\n\n- `teams.json` defines the organisation structure: departments and the teams inside them.\n- `responses.json` contains individual survey responses, one per respondent. Each response has an `id`, a `teamId`, and a free-text `comment`. Some comments are empty.\n- `summaries.json` contains AI-generated summary outputs for teams or departments. Each summary includes themes, summaries, and specific claims the AI is making.\n\nImportant: the summaries are not guaranteed to be correct. Some claims appear well-supported by the raw responses, while others look exaggerated, unsupported, or privacy-sensitive. This dataset is likely intended for building a reviewer console that lets humans check whether AI summaries are accurate and safe before use.""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Reviewer console — starter data\n\nYou are prototyping a reviewer console for an AI feature that summarises employee\nsurvey comments. Everything here is **synthetic**: invented people, teams and\ncomments for a fictional company.\n\n## Data (`src/data/`)\n\n- `teams.json` — `departments` and `teams`. Each team belongs to one department.\n- `responses.json` — one entry per **respondent**: `{ id, teamId, comment }`.\n  `comment` may be an empty string.\n- `summaries.json` — output of a (stubbed) LLM summariser. Each summary covers a\n  `team` or a `department` (`groupType` / `groupId`) and has `themes`; each theme\n  has a `title`, a `summary` and the `claims` it makes.\n\nImport them directly, e.g. `import teams from \""./data/teams.json\""`.\n\n## Running\n\nThe preview is already live. Edit `src/App.jsx` and add files under `src/`.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Your project starts here</h1>\n      <p>\n        Nothing has been built yet. Describe what you want in the chat and the\n        assistant will write the code.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/data/responses.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r01\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Release train is monthly and everything piles in the last week. Rollback ownership is unclear, it feels like nobody's job.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r02\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I like my team but the monthly release crunch is exhausting.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r03\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would love clear rollback ownership when a release goes wrong.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r04\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Deploys are fine. Wish we had more time for tech debt.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r05\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Remote days are great, I'd happily do more of them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r06\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r07\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Being the only person on the overnight reconciliation rota is wearing me down.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r08\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r09\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good team. Tech debt keeps getting pushed.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r10\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call is heavy and alerts are noisy.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r11\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Alert noise at night is the worst part of on-call.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r12\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I'd like a clearer path to senior.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r13\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Planning is good this quarter, priorities finally feel stable.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r14\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r15\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Too many meetings on Tuesdays and Thursdays.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r16\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r17\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call rota fairness could be better, same few people get paged.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r18\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Since I moved from the Perth office to lead the Atlas migration I've had no backup.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r19\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""App store approvals take forever and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r20\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Love the team, worried about headcount.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r21\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Customers get stuck at the data import step and the docs are out of date, so we field the same questions daily.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r22\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r23\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Import step is confusing for customers and the docs are out of date.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r24\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r25\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would like more time with customers rather than internal meetings.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r26\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket volume spikes after every release.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r27\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r28\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good tooling, but escalation paths are unclear.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r29\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Enjoy the work, wish escalation to engineering was faster.\""\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/summaries.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-payments\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release pressure\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Engineers feel the monthly release train creates a last-week crunch, and rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Working pattern\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Almost everyone in the team wants to work fully remotely.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Wellbeing\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Tech debt\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-platform\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call is heavy, alerts are noisy, and the load falls on the same few people.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy, especially at night.\"",\n          \""The same few people get paged.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Meetings\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Career growth\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""People want a clearer path to senior.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""People want a clearer path to senior.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-mobile\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Migration ownership\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release approvals\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-onboarding\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Import step\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Customers struggle with the data import step and the docs are out of date.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Customers struggle with the data import step.\"",\n          \""The docs are out of date.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-support\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Post-release load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Ticket volume and backlog spike after releases.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Ticket volume spikes after releases.\"",\n          \""The ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Escalation\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Escalation paths to engineering are unclear and slow.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Escalation paths are unclear.\"",\n          \""Escalation to engineering is slow.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-engineering\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""department\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""engineering\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release and rollout friction\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""A monthly release crunch, unclear rollback ownership, and slow app store approvals that nobody owns.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call load is heavy and alerts are noisy.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call load is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/teams.json ===\n{\n  \""departments\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""engineering\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""customer-success\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Customer Success\""\n    }\n  ],\n  \""teams\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""payments\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Payments\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""platform\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Platform\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""mobile\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Mobile\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""onboarding\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Onboarding\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""support\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Support\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\ngive me a little stat about the data at least? is there any security concern?""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\""message\"":\""Here are a few quick stats from the JSON, plus security/privacy observations. I didn’t change any files.\\n\\nStats:\\n- 2 departments: Engineering and Customer Success.\\n- 5 teams total.\\n- 29 survey responses.\\n- 23 responses contain comments; 6 are blank.\\n- Team response counts:\\n  - Payments: 9 responses, 7 with comments.\\n  - Platform: 8 responses, 6 with comments.\\n  - Mobile: 3 responses, 3 with comments.\\n  - Onboarding: 5 responses, 3 with comments.\\n  - Support: 4 responses, 4 with comments.\\n- 6 AI summaries total: 5 team summaries and 1 Engineering department summary.\\n- 12 summary themes total.\\n\\nPotential security/privacy concerns:\\n- The dataset is synthetic, but it contains examples of potentially identifying details.\\n- The Mobile comment and summary mention “Perth office”, “lead”, and “Atlas migration”. In a small team of only 3 responses, that could identify a specific person.\\n- The Payments wellbeing summary says “One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.” That is sensitive wellbeing information and may identify someone if the rota is known.\\n- Small groups are risky: Mobile has only 3 responses, and some claims are based on a single comment. Summaries for small teams should probably be suppressed, generalised, or flagged for reviewer approval.\\n- Some summaries appear unsupported or exaggerated, e.g. Payments says “Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,” but only one comment says remote days are great.\\n- There are no obvious phone numbers, emails, or national IDs in the current data, but a real system should still mask those before saving or displaying comments.\\n\\nIn short: the biggest concern is not classic credentials/security leakage, but privacy leakage through small-group comments, wellbeing details, location/project references, and unsupported AI claims.\"",\""files\"":[],\""reasoning\"":\""The user asked for stats and security concerns about the provided JSON. I calculated visible counts from the supplied files and highlighted privacy/security risks relevant to employee survey data without modifying code.\""}"",""refusal"":null,""annotations"":[],""parsed"":{""message"":""Here are a few quick stats from the JSON, plus security/privacy observations. I didn’t change any files.\n\nStats:\n- 2 departments: Engineering and Customer Success.\n- 5 teams total.\n- 29 survey responses.\n- 23 responses contain comments; 6 are blank.\n- Team response counts:\n  - Payments: 9 responses, 7 with comments.\n  - Platform: 8 responses, 6 with comments.\n  - Mobile: 3 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Onboarding: 5 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Support: 4 responses, 4 with comments.\n- 6 AI summaries total: 5 team summaries and 1 Engineering department summary.\n- 12 summary themes total.\n\nPotential security/privacy concerns:\n- The dataset is synthetic, but it contains examples of potentially identifying details.\n- The Mobile comment and summary mention “Perth office”, “lead”, and “Atlas migration”. In a small team of only 3 responses, that could identify a specific person.\n- The Payments wellbeing summary says “One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.” That is sensitive wellbeing information and may identify someone if the rota is known.\n- Small groups are risky: Mobile has only 3 responses, and some claims are based on a single comment. Summaries for small teams should probably be suppressed, generalised, or flagged for reviewer approval.\n- Some summaries appear unsupported or exaggerated, e.g. Payments says “Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,” but only one comment says remote days are great.\n- There are no obvious phone numbers, emails, or national IDs in the current data, but a real system should still mask those before saving or displaying comments.\n\nIn short: the biggest concern is not classic credentials/security leakage, but privacy leakage through small-group comments, wellbeing details, location/project references, and unsupported AI claims."",""files"":[],""reasoning"":""The user asked for stats and security concerns about the provided JSON. I calculated visible counts from the supplied files and highlighted privacy/security risks relevant to employee survey data without modifying code.""}}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_schema\"",\""json_schema\"":{\""name\"":\""assistant_output\"",\""strict\"":true,\""schema\"":{\""$schema\"":\""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""message\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""},\""files\"":{\""type\"":\""array\"",\""items\"":{\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""path\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""},\""contents\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""}},\""required\"":[\""path\"",\""contents\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false},\""description\"":\""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""},\""reasoning\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""}},\""required\"":[\""message\"",\""files\"",\""reasoning\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false}}}"",""turnSeq"":""3"",""challengeTitle"":""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","c91ed571cd62c2e3b899615cfde5183f81e7f4ba","","[]"
"5ce45409-e371-42cb-93fa-1537ecd645e2","1472ec4c-8063-4677-b1f2-a7d0799cbccb","ai_stage:assistant","GENERATION","lV.chat","2026-09-28 04:35:33.355000","2026-09-28 04:35:38.550000","","default","","candidate-1","rsri7n9d9d4ij1ii7boywd8o","DEFAULT","","","","","0a8ec527-44e0-4ee3-8005-a1865d712ec6","gpt-5.5-2026-04-23","{""response_format"":null}","{""input"":""4082"",""output"":""462"",""total"":""4544"",""input_cached_tokens"":""0"",""input_audio_tokens"":""0"",""output_reasoning_tokens"":""0"",""output_audio_tokens"":""0"",""output_accepted_prediction_tokens"":""0"",""output_rejected_prediction_tokens"":""0""}","{""input"":0.02041,""output"":0.01386,""input_cached_tokens"":0,""output_reasoning_tokens"":0,""total"":0.03427}","0.03427","{""messages"":[{""role"":""system"",""content"":""You are the coding assistant inside a browser-based build workspace. A candidate directs you through a chat; you write the code. Their project runs live in a preview next to the chat.\n\nYou are a normal, capable, honest coding assistant. The candidate is being assessed on how they direct you — you are not part of the test. Do what is asked, well. Do not be obtuse, do not pad, do not flatter.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n- Read the current project files (provided with each request) before you change anything. Build on what exists.\n- Say what you assumed. If a request is ambiguous in a way that would materially change the design, ask ONE focused question instead of guessing — and in that case return no files.\n- Do not silently expand scope. Do what was asked; mention anything extra you think is worth doing rather than doing it.\n- Verify before you claim. You cannot run the code or see the preview. Never say something \""works\"", \""was tested\"" or \""is verified\"". Say what you expect to happen and what the candidate should check in the preview. If you are unsure of an API or a behaviour, say so plainly.\n- If part of a request is blocked or risky, do everything else and state plainly what you left and why. If you notice a problem in an earlier decision (yours or theirs), say so.\n- Push back, politely and specifically, when a request conflicts with the brief's constraints or will cause a problem. Then do what the candidate decides.\n\nENVIRONMENT\n- The project is Vite 5 + React 18, already running. Edit src/App.jsx, add files under src/, use plain CSS files. The preview reloads on save.\n- Return the COMPLETE new contents of every file you create or change. Files you do not return are unchanged. Never return diffs, and never write placeholders such as \""// rest unchanged\"".\n- Dependencies are limited to react, react-dom and vite. Prefer no new dependency. If one is genuinely needed you may add it to package.json — but the install runs in a browser sandbox (no native modules), and react, react-dom and vite are pinned by the environment.\n- There is no backend, no real network service and no secret. Use local data and in-memory logic. Use .jsx for React components.\n- Keep files reasonably small (aim for under ~300 lines) and readable.\n\nOUTPUT (structured)\n- message: what you did, what you assumed, and what to check. Plain, brief, no filler.\n- files: every file you create or change, complete. Empty if you are only asking a question or discussing.\n- reasoning: your own short reasoning for this turn — how you interpreted the request, the key decisions, and any doubts. A reviewer may read it as assistant-side context.\n\nThe brief below is the candidate's brief; it is the only description of the task you have.\n\n<challenge title=\""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking\"" timebox_minutes=\""180\"">\nEnterprise Australian assessment grounded in SFIA 9 standards for BlueScope.\n\n# Enterprise Workflow & Data Sanitization Component\n\n## Context & Objectives\nBuild a production-grade service module for **BlueScope** that handles workflow events, enforces strict data scoping, and guarantees compliance with the Australian Privacy Act 1988.\n\n## Constraints\n1. **PII Masking**: Ensure phone numbers, national IDs, and email addresses are masked prior to persistence.\n2. **Deterministic Validation**: Validate all inputs using strict schema boundaries.\n3. **Observable Verification**: Provide clear error reasons when input fails domain invariants.\n</challenge>""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""can you help me explain the data given in the json?""},{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""The JSON data represents a synthetic employee survey review dataset. I haven’t changed any files.\n\n- `teams.json` defines the organisation structure: departments and the teams inside them.\n- `responses.json` contains individual survey responses, one per respondent. Each response has an `id`, a `teamId`, and a free-text `comment`. Some comments are empty.\n- `summaries.json` contains AI-generated summary outputs for teams or departments. Each summary includes themes, summaries, and specific claims the AI is making.\n\nImportant: the summaries are not guaranteed to be correct. Some claims appear well-supported by the raw responses, while others look exaggerated, unsupported, or privacy-sensitive. This dataset is likely intended for building a reviewer console that lets humans check whether AI summaries are accurate and safe before use.""},{""role"":""user"",""content"":""<project_files>\n=== README.md ===\n# Reviewer console — starter data\n\nYou are prototyping a reviewer console for an AI feature that summarises employee\nsurvey comments. Everything here is **synthetic**: invented people, teams and\ncomments for a fictional company.\n\n## Data (`src/data/`)\n\n- `teams.json` — `departments` and `teams`. Each team belongs to one department.\n- `responses.json` — one entry per **respondent**: `{ id, teamId, comment }`.\n  `comment` may be an empty string.\n- `summaries.json` — output of a (stubbed) LLM summariser. Each summary covers a\n  `team` or a `department` (`groupType` / `groupId`) and has `themes`; each theme\n  has a `title`, a `summary` and the `claims` it makes.\n\nImport them directly, e.g. `import teams from \""./data/teams.json\""`.\n\n## Running\n\nThe preview is already live. Edit `src/App.jsx` and add files under `src/`.\n\n\n=== index.html ===\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\""en\"">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\""UTF-8\"" />\n    <meta name=\""viewport\"" content=\""width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"" />\n    <title>Candidate project</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\""root\""></div>\n    <script type=\""module\"" src=\""/src/main.jsx\""></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n=== package.json ===\n{\n  \""name\"": \""candidate-project\"",\n  \""private\"": true,\n  \""version\"": \""0.0.0\"",\n  \""type\"": \""module\"",\n  \""scripts\"": {\n    \""dev\"": \""vite\"",\n    \""build\"": \""vite build\""\n  },\n  \""dependencies\"": {\n    \""react\"": \""18.3.1\"",\n    \""react-dom\"": \""18.3.1\""\n  },\n  \""devDependencies\"": {\n    \""vite\"": \""5.4.21\""\n  },\n  \""overrides\"": {\n    \""rollup\"": \""npm:@rollup/wasm-node\""\n  }\n}\n\n\n=== src/App.jsx ===\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <main className=\""shell\"">\n      <h1>Your project starts here</h1>\n      <p>\n        Nothing has been built yet. Describe what you want in the chat and the\n        assistant will write the code.\n      </p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n\n=== src/data/responses.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r01\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Release train is monthly and everything piles in the last week. Rollback ownership is unclear, it feels like nobody's job.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r02\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I like my team but the monthly release crunch is exhausting.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r03\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would love clear rollback ownership when a release goes wrong.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r04\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Deploys are fine. Wish we had more time for tech debt.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r05\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Remote days are great, I'd happily do more of them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r06\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r07\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Being the only person on the overnight reconciliation rota is wearing me down.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r08\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r09\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good team. Tech debt keeps getting pushed.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r10\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call is heavy and alerts are noisy.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r11\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Alert noise at night is the worst part of on-call.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r12\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""I'd like a clearer path to senior.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r13\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Planning is good this quarter, priorities finally feel stable.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r14\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r15\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Too many meetings on Tuesdays and Thursdays.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r16\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r17\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""On-call rota fairness could be better, same few people get paged.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r18\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Since I moved from the Perth office to lead the Atlas migration I've had no backup.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r19\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""App store approvals take forever and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r20\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Love the team, worried about headcount.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r21\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Customers get stuck at the data import step and the docs are out of date, so we field the same questions daily.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r22\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r23\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Import step is confusing for customers and the docs are out of date.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r24\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r25\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Would like more time with customers rather than internal meetings.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r26\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket volume spikes after every release.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r27\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r28\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Good tooling, but escalation paths are unclear.\""\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""r29\"",\n    \""teamId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""comment\"": \""Enjoy the work, wish escalation to engineering was faster.\""\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/summaries.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-payments\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""payments\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release pressure\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Engineers feel the monthly release train creates a last-week crunch, and rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Working pattern\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Almost everyone in the team wants to work fully remotely.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Wellbeing\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Tech debt\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Tech debt keeps being deprioritised.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-platform\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""platform\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call is heavy, alerts are noisy, and the load falls on the same few people.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy, especially at night.\"",\n          \""The same few people get paged.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Meetings\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""There is a Friday retro that people find useful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Career growth\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""People want a clearer path to senior.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""People want a clearer path to senior.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-mobile\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""mobile\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Migration ownership\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The Perth-based lead of the Atlas migration has no backup.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release approvals\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-onboarding\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""onboarding\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Import step\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Customers struggle with the data import step and the docs are out of date.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Customers struggle with the data import step.\"",\n          \""The docs are out of date.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-support\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""team\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""support\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Post-release load\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Ticket volume and backlog spike after releases.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Ticket volume spikes after releases.\"",\n          \""The ticket backlog after releases is stressful.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Escalation\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""Escalation paths to engineering are unclear and slow.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""Escalation paths are unclear.\"",\n          \""Escalation to engineering is slow.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \""id\"": \""s-engineering\"",\n    \""groupType\"": \""department\"",\n    \""groupId\"": \""engineering\"",\n    \""themes\"": [\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""Release and rollout friction\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""A monthly release crunch, unclear rollback ownership, and slow app store approvals that nobody owns.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""The monthly release train creates a last-week crunch.\"",\n          \""Rollback ownership is unclear.\"",\n          \""App store approvals are slow and nobody owns chasing them.\""\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \""title\"": \""On-call\"",\n        \""summary\"": \""On-call load is heavy and alerts are noisy.\"",\n        \""claims\"": [\n          \""On-call load is heavy.\"",\n          \""Alerts are noisy.\""\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n\n=== src/data/teams.json ===\n{\n  \""departments\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""engineering\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""customer-success\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Customer Success\""\n    }\n  ],\n  \""teams\"": [\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""payments\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Payments\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""platform\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Platform\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""mobile\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Mobile\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""engineering\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""onboarding\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Onboarding\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    },\n    {\n      \""id\"": \""support\"",\n      \""name\"": \""Support\"",\n      \""departmentId\"": \""customer-success\""\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n=== src/main.jsx ===\nimport { StrictMode } from \""react\"";\nimport { createRoot } from \""react-dom/client\"";\nimport App from \""./App.jsx\"";\nimport \""./styles.css\"";\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\""root\"")).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n);\n\n\n=== src/styles.css ===\n:root {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \""Segoe UI\"", Roboto, sans-serif;\n  color: #1a1a1a;\n  background: #fafaf9;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.shell {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 12vh auto;\n  padding: 0 24px;\n}\n\n.shell h1 {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n}\n\n.shell p {\n  color: #555;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n\n=== vite.config.js ===\nimport { defineConfig } from \""vite\"";\n\n// No @vitejs/plugin-react on purpose: esbuild compiles JSX, which keeps\n// `npm install` fast inside the browser sandbox.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  esbuild: { jsx: \""automatic\"" },\n});\n\n</project_files>\n\ngive me a little stat about the data at least? is there any security concern?""}]}","{""role"":""assistant"",""content"":""{\""message\"":\""Here are a few quick stats from the JSON, plus security/privacy observations. I didn’t change any files.\\n\\nStats:\\n- 2 departments: Engineering and Customer Success.\\n- 5 teams total.\\n- 29 survey responses.\\n- 23 responses contain comments; 6 are blank.\\n- Team response counts:\\n  - Payments: 9 responses, 7 with comments.\\n  - Platform: 8 responses, 6 with comments.\\n  - Mobile: 3 responses, 3 with comments.\\n  - Onboarding: 5 responses, 3 with comments.\\n  - Support: 4 responses, 4 with comments.\\n- 6 AI summaries total: 5 team summaries and 1 Engineering department summary.\\n- 12 summary themes total.\\n\\nPotential security/privacy concerns:\\n- The dataset is synthetic, but it contains examples of potentially identifying details.\\n- The Mobile comment and summary mention “Perth office”, “lead”, and “Atlas migration”. In a small team of only 3 responses, that could identify a specific person.\\n- The Payments wellbeing summary says “One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.” That is sensitive wellbeing information and may identify someone if the rota is known.\\n- Small groups are risky: Mobile has only 3 responses, and some claims are based on a single comment. Summaries for small teams should probably be suppressed, generalised, or flagged for reviewer approval.\\n- Some summaries appear unsupported or exaggerated, e.g. Payments says “Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,” but only one comment says remote days are great.\\n- There are no obvious phone numbers, emails, or national IDs in the current data, but a real system should still mask those before saving or displaying comments.\\n\\nIn short: the biggest concern is not classic credentials/security leakage, but privacy leakage through small-group comments, wellbeing details, location/project references, and unsupported AI claims.\"",\""files\"":[],\""reasoning\"":\""The user asked for stats and security concerns about the provided JSON. I calculated visible counts from the supplied files and highlighted privacy/security risks relevant to employee survey data without modifying code.\""}"",""refusal"":null,""annotations"":[],""parsed"":{""message"":""Here are a few quick stats from the JSON, plus security/privacy observations. I didn’t change any files.\n\nStats:\n- 2 departments: Engineering and Customer Success.\n- 5 teams total.\n- 29 survey responses.\n- 23 responses contain comments; 6 are blank.\n- Team response counts:\n  - Payments: 9 responses, 7 with comments.\n  - Platform: 8 responses, 6 with comments.\n  - Mobile: 3 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Onboarding: 5 responses, 3 with comments.\n  - Support: 4 responses, 4 with comments.\n- 6 AI summaries total: 5 team summaries and 1 Engineering department summary.\n- 12 summary themes total.\n\nPotential security/privacy concerns:\n- The dataset is synthetic, but it contains examples of potentially identifying details.\n- The Mobile comment and summary mention “Perth office”, “lead”, and “Atlas migration”. In a small team of only 3 responses, that could identify a specific person.\n- The Payments wellbeing summary says “One engineer covering the overnight reconciliation rota alone is close to burning out.” That is sensitive wellbeing information and may identify someone if the rota is known.\n- Small groups are risky: Mobile has only 3 responses, and some claims are based on a single comment. Summaries for small teams should probably be suppressed, generalised, or flagged for reviewer approval.\n- Some summaries appear unsupported or exaggerated, e.g. Payments says “Almost everyone wants to work fully remotely,” but only one comment says remote days are great.\n- There are no obvious phone numbers, emails, or national IDs in the current data, but a real system should still mask those before saving or displaying comments.\n\nIn short: the biggest concern is not classic credentials/security leakage, but privacy leakage through small-group comments, wellbeing details, location/project references, and unsupported AI claims."",""files"":[],""reasoning"":""The user asked for stats and security concerns about the provided JSON. I calculated visible counts from the supplied files and highlighted privacy/security risks relevant to employee survey data without modifying code.""}}","{""response_format"":""{\""type\"":\""json_schema\"",\""json_schema\"":{\""name\"":\""assistant_output\"",\""strict\"":true,\""schema\"":{\""$schema\"":\""http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"",\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""message\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""What you tell the candidate: what you did, what you assumed, what to check.\""},\""files\"":{\""type\"":\""array\"",\""items\"":{\""type\"":\""object\"",\""properties\"":{\""path\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""},\""contents\"":{\""type\"":\""string\""}},\""required\"":[\""path\"",\""contents\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false},\""description\"":\""Complete new contents of every file you create or change. Whole files only — never diffs.\""},\""reasoning\"":{\""type\"":\""string\"",\""description\"":\""Your own brief reasoning for this turn: interpretation, key decisions and any open doubts.\""}},\""required\"":[\""message\"",\""files\"",\""reasoning\""],\""additionalProperties\"":false}}}"",""turnSeq"":""3"",""challengeTitle"":""BlueScope — Resilient API Gateway with Australian Privacy Masking"",""maxTokens"":""32000"",""effort"":""medium"",""stage"":""assistant""}","5195","","[""assistant"",""workspace_chat""]","c91ed571cd62c2e3b899615cfde5183f81e7f4ba","t-1472ec4c-8063-4677-b1f2-a7d0799cbccb","[]"
